window.GLP_JAPJI_LESSONS = {"project":"GLP-001","release":"0.8-japji-v1","reviewStatus":"draft","lessons":{"mool":{"id":"mool","meaningEn":"One all-pervading Reality: true, creative, without fear or enmity, beyond time and birth, self-existent; known through the Guru’s grace.","meaningPa":"ਇੱਕੋ ਸਰਬ-ਵਿਆਪਕ ਹਸਤੀ ਹੈ—ਸਦਾ ਸੱਚੀ, ਰਚਨਹਾਰ, ਨਿਰਭਉ, ਨਿਰਵੈਰ, ਕਾਲ ਤੇ ਜਨਮ ਤੋਂ ਪਰੇ ਅਤੇ ਆਪਣੇ ਆਪ ਤੋਂ ਪ੍ਰਕਾਸ਼ਮਾਨ; ਉਸ ਦੀ ਪਛਾਣ ਗੁਰੂ ਦੀ ਕਿਰਪਾ ਨਾਲ ਹੁੰਦੀ ਹੈ।","directSense":"The opening gives a connected description of the One. Truth is joined to creation, freedom from fear and enmity, and an existence not dependent on birth or time. Its ending, gur prasad, places the approach to this Reality in the Guru’s grace. Do not reduce the passage to a list of slogans about human self-improvement: it first describes the Divine. The ethical implications for our own conduct belong to a further interpretive step.","directSensePa":"ਇਹ ਆਰੰਭ ਇੱਕ ਹਸਤੀ ਦੇ ਗੁਣਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਇਕੱਠੇ ਰੱਖਦਾ ਹੈ। ਸੱਚ, ਰਚਨਾ, ਨਿਰਭਉਤਾ ਅਤੇ ਨਿਰਵੈਰਤਾ ਵੱਖ-ਵੱਖ ਦੇਵਤਿਆਂ ਦੀ ਗੱਲ ਨਹੀਂ। ਅਕਾਲ ਅਤੇ ਅਜੂਨੀ ਉਸ ਹਸਤੀ ਨੂੰ ਸਮੇਂ ਤੇ ਜਨਮ ਦੀਆਂ ਹੱਦਾਂ ਤੋਂ ਪਰੇ ਦਰਸਾਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ। ਅਖ਼ੀਰ ਦੇ ‘ਗੁਰ ਪ੍ਰਸਾਦਿ’ ਨਾਲ ਪਛਾਣ ਦਾ ਸੰਬੰਧ ਗੁਰੂ ਦੀ ਕਿਰਪਾ ਨਾਲ ਬਣਦਾ ਹੈ। ਪਹਿਲਾਂ ਇਹ ਪ੍ਰਭੂ ਦੇ ਸਰੂਪ ਦਾ ਵਰਣਨ ਹੈ; ਇਸ ਤੋਂ ਆਪਣੇ ਵਰਤਾਓ ਲਈ ਸੇਧ ਲੈਣਾ ਅਗਲਾ ਵਿਚਾਰ ਹੈ।","context":"Read this before the opening affirmation of Truth and the first Pauri’s question about becoming truthful. The movement is from the One to the life of the learner. The app keeps Mool Mantar, Jap heading and opening Salok as separate display units without claiming that this interface settles every tradition’s use of the term Mool Mantar.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ੴ","note":"The opening symbol is read as Ik Oankar. The numeral and written form belong to the scripture; the interface never replaces them with an English label."},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਿਰਭਉ · ਨਿਰਵੈਰੁ","note":"Without fear; without enmity. The paired descriptions keep power from being confused with hostility."},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਕਾਲ ਮੂਰਤਿ","note":"Timeless being/form. Sahib Singh’s grammatical note treats akal with murat; the phrase should not be split casually."},{"gurmukhi":"ਗੁਰ ਪ੍ਰਸਾਦਿ","note":"Through the Guru’s grace. Retaining the phrase avoids making the encounter simply an achievement of intellect."}],"pronunciation":"Keep the original vowel signs visible, especially in ਮੂਰਤਿ and ਪ੍ਰਸਾਦਿ. Ik Oankar is a rough verbal label for ੴ, not a complete pronunciation guide. Ask a qualified teacher about articulation and pauses rather than treating the app’s visual token divisions as a recitation prescription.","interpretations":"English words such as Reality, Being, Creator and God carry different associations; none alone replaces ੴ. ‘Form’ in ਅਕਾਲ ਮੂਰਤਿ does not authorize an inference that the text prescribes an idol. The scope of Mool Mantar and customary recital groupings should be attributed to a named tradition before this app teaches them as settled. The concise sense here ends at ਗੁਰ ਪ੍ਰਸਾਦਿ, following the frozen display unit.","reflection":"When fear or resentment shapes a decision, pause to notice it. Consider what a truthful action without hostility might look like. This is an application prompted by the passage, not a claim that a person becomes the Divine by following a checklist.","reflectionPa":"ਜਦੋਂ ਡਰ ਜਾਂ ਵੈਰ ਕਿਸੇ ਫ਼ੈਸਲੇ ਨੂੰ ਚਲਾ ਰਿਹਾ ਹੋਵੇ, ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਪਛਾਣੀਏ। ਸੱਚਾ ਅਤੇ ਵੈਰ-ਰਹਿਤ ਕਦਮ ਕੀ ਹੋ ਸਕਦਾ ਹੈ? ਇਹ ਅਮਲੀ ਮਨਨ ਹੈ, ਮੂਲ ਪਾਠ ਦਾ ਬਦਲ ਨਹੀਂ।","teachBack":"Which descriptions concern the Divine directly, and which ethical implications are you drawing for your own life? Explain the difference.","teachBackPa":"ਇੱਥੇ ਕਿਹੜੇ ਗੁਣ ਸਿੱਧੇ ਪ੍ਰਭੂ ਦਾ ਵਰਣਨ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ ਅਤੇ ਆਪਣੇ ਜੀਵਨ ਲਈ ਕਿਹੜੀ ਸੇਧ ਤੁਸੀਂ ਕੱਢ ਰਹੇ ਹੋ? ਦੋਹਾਂ ਦਾ ਫ਼ਰਕ ਦੱਸੋ।","sources":[{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0001.html","label":"Darpan · Ang 1 · Mool Mantar and grammatical notes"},{"url":"https://www.srigranth.org/servlet/gurbani.gurbani?Action=Page&Param=1","label":"SriGranth · Ang 1 · original passage and comparison"}],"status":"draft","unitId":"mool","passageIds":["mool.line01"],"sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"mool.line01","ang":1,"sourceLine":1,"sha256":"9c83d0b7995531208b087fc82e87ac477f04ca2119b77365dbcf58190998b9d4"}],"humanReviewed":false,"researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete"},"title":{"id":"title","meaningEn":"Jap is the heading of the composition. It introduces attentive remembrance and meditation; it is not the name of a raag.","meaningPa":"‘ਜਪੁ’ ਇਸ ਬਾਣੀ ਦਾ ਸਿਰਲੇਖ ਹੈ। ਇਹ ਯਾਦ ਅਤੇ ਧਿਆਨ ਵੱਲ ਸੇਧ ਕਰਦਾ ਹੈ; ਇਹ ਕਿਸੇ ਰਾਗ ਦਾ ਨਾਮ ਨਹੀਂ।","directSense":"This is a heading, not an additional Pauri. The surrounding marks and the final written vowel remain part of the original line. A heading gives orientation; it does not contain the whole teaching that follows. Read the opening Salok next, then the numbered Pauris.","directSensePa":"ਇਹ ਸਿਰਲੇਖ ਹੈ, ਵੱਖਰੀ ਪਉੜੀ ਨਹੀਂ। ਇਸ ਲਫ਼ਜ਼ ਦੀ ਲਿਖਤ ਅਤੇ ਆਲੇ-ਦੁਆਲੇ ਦੇ ਚਿੰਨ੍ਹ ਜਿਵੇਂ ਸਰੋਤ ਵਿਚ ਹਨ, ਤਿਵੇਂ ਰੱਖੇ ਗਏ ਹਨ। ਸਿਰਲੇਖ ਬਾਣੀ ਵੱਲ ਲੈ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹੈ; ਪੂਰੀ ਸਿੱਖਿਆ ਅਗਲੇ ਸਲੋਕ ਅਤੇ ਪਉੜੀਆਂ ਵਿਚ ਖੁੱਲ੍ਹਦੀ ਹੈ।","context":"The reader’s 42 display units count this heading separately for source integrity. That interface count must not be confused with 42 Pauris: there are 38 numbered Pauris.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਪੁ","note":"Composition heading; related to remembrance or meditative utterance. A short English gloss cannot establish a particular ritual method."}],"pronunciation":"The written final aunkar is preserved. A transliteration such as Jap or Japu is a reading convention and should not be used to alter the original spelling.","interpretations":"Do not infer a prescribed melody from this heading. A person may sing or recite Japji in different ways, but performance practice and scriptural raag assignment are separate matters.","reflection":"Before beginning, take a moment to arrive with attention. This optional pause is a reading practice, not an added scriptural instruction.","reflectionPa":"ਪੜ੍ਹਨਾ ਸ਼ੁਰੂ ਕਰਨ ਤੋਂ ਪਹਿਲਾਂ ਧਿਆਨ ਇਕੱਠਾ ਕਰਨ ਲਈ ਥੋੜ੍ਹਾ ਰੁਕ ਸਕਦੇ ਹੋ। ਇਹ ਪੜ੍ਹਨ ਦੀ ਚੋਣ ਹੈ, ਪਾਠ ਵਿਚ ਜੋੜੀ ਗਈ ਹਦਾਇਤ ਨਹੀਂ।","teachBack":"Why does the app count 42 display units while saying that Japji has 38 Pauris?","teachBackPa":"ਐਪ ਵਿਚ 42 ਇਕਾਈਆਂ ਹੋਣ ਦੇ ਬਾਵਜੂਦ ਜਪੁਜੀ ਦੀਆਂ ਪਉੜੀਆਂ 38 ਕਿਉਂ ਕਹੀਆਂ ਜਾਂਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ?","sources":[{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0001.html","label":"Darpan · Ang 1 · Jap heading"},{"url":"https://www.thesikhencyclopedia.com/japu/","label":"The Sikh Encyclopedia · Japu · retained reference"}],"status":"draft","unitId":"title","passageIds":["title.line01"],"sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"title.line01","ang":1,"sourceLine":3,"sha256":"b340c7a88f181b1e67ed41306c725165340385b639c36ade51f58eec17145172"}],"humanReviewed":false,"researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete"},"opening":{"id":"opening","meaningEn":"The True One is before the ages, through the ages, here now, and will remain. The passage sets passing human life beside enduring Reality.","meaningPa":"ਸੱਚੀ ਹਸਤੀ ਮੁੱਢ ਤੋਂ, ਜੁਗਾਂ ਦੇ ਮੁੱਢ ਤੋਂ, ਹੁਣ ਵੀ ਹੈ ਅਤੇ ਅੱਗੇ ਵੀ ਰਹੇਗੀ। ਬਦਲਦੇ ਜੀਵਨ ਦੇ ਸਾਹਮਣੇ ਇਹ ਅਟੱਲ ਸੱਚ ਨੂੰ ਰੱਖਦਾ ਹੈ।","directSense":"The two lines move through beginnings, ages, the present and what is to come. Repeated sach holds these temporal expressions together. The emphasis is not simply that an honest statement stays correct: the affirmation concerns the enduring True One. Nanak appears within this affirmation, not as an invitation to add a personal name while reciting.","directSensePa":"ਦੋ ਤੁਕਾਂ ਵਿਚ ਮੁੱਢ, ਜੁਗ, ਵਰਤਮਾਨ ਅਤੇ ਅੱਗੇ ਦੇ ਸਮੇਂ ਦਾ ਜ਼ਿਕਰ ਹੈ। ‘ਸਚੁ’ ਦੀ ਦੁਹਰਾਈ ਇਨ੍ਹਾਂ ਸਭ ਨੂੰ ਜੋੜਦੀ ਹੈ। ਗੱਲ ਕੇਵਲ ਕਿਸੇ ਵਾਕ ਦੇ ਸਹੀ ਹੋਣ ਦੀ ਨਹੀਂ, ਸਦਾ ਕਾਇਮ ਸੱਚੀ ਹਸਤੀ ਦੀ ਹੈ। ਪਾਠ ਵਿਚ ‘ਨਾਨਕ’ ਜਿਵੇਂ ਲਿਖਿਆ ਹੈ ਤਿਵੇਂ ਹੀ ਪੜ੍ਹਨਾ ਹੈ।","context":"The Salok follows the heading and precedes Pauri 1’s question: how can one become truthful? The shared language of truth invites a connection while leaving the Divine description and human ethical question distinct.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਆਦਿ · ਜੁਗਾਦਿ","note":"Beginning; the beginning of ages. Notice how the opening expands the time frame."},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੈ ਭੀ · ਹੋਸੀ ਭੀ","note":"Is also now; will also be. The repeated ਭੀ links present and future."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਚੁ","note":"Truth/lasting Reality in this setting; context determines more than a one-word dictionary gloss."}],"pronunciation":"Keep the paired phrases audible when learning with a teacher: ਆਦਿ ਸਚੁ / ਜੁਗਾਦਿ ਸਚੁ and ਹੈ ਭੀ / ਹੋਸੀ ਭੀ. These are study groupings, not a checked recording-specific pause map.","interpretations":"The language can orient reflection on the Divine’s permanence, but it supplies no physical date for the universe’s beginning. Turning it into a scientific chronology would add a claim the passage does not give.","reflection":"Name something in your day that changes quickly. Then consider what it means to orient conduct toward truth when circumstances change. This exercise is personal application.","reflectionPa":"ਦਿਨ ਦੀ ਕੋਈ ਜਲਦੀ ਬਦਲਣ ਵਾਲੀ ਗੱਲ ਯਾਦ ਕਰੋ। ਹਾਲਾਤ ਬਦਲਣ ਵੇਲੇ ਵੀ ਸੱਚ ਵੱਲ ਟਿਕੇ ਰਹਿਣ ਦਾ ਕੀ ਭਾਵ ਹੋ ਸਕਦਾ ਹੈ? ਇਹ ਨਿੱਜੀ ਅਭਿਆਸ ਹੈ।","teachBack":"How does the repeated ਸਚੁ connect the four time expressions without making this a scientific timeline?","teachBackPa":"‘ਸਚੁ’ ਦੀ ਦੁਹਰਾਈ ਸਮੇਂ ਦੇ ਵੱਖਰੇ ਜ਼ਿਕਰਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਕਿਵੇਂ ਜੋੜਦੀ ਹੈ? ਇਸ ਨੂੰ ਵਿਗਿਆਨਕ ਸਮਾਂ-ਰੇਖਾ ਕਿਉਂ ਨਹੀਂ ਮੰਨਣਾ ਚਾਹੀਦਾ?","sources":[{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0001.html","label":"Darpan · Ang 1 · opening Salok"},{"url":"https://srec.gurmat.info/articles/sri-guru-granth-sahib/japji-sahib/","label":"SREC · Japji · opening Salok comparison"}],"status":"draft","unitId":"opening","passageIds":["opening.line01","opening.line02"],"sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"opening.line01","ang":1,"sourceLine":4,"sha256":"5fa82252d22db0550c6688cd528788a6ab6f6bec06803ccd9e68106d1fe6af2f"},{"passageId":"opening.line02","ang":1,"sourceLine":4,"sha256":"4850e11c9083aea58a1874c3607c4d56dc86529d411aac59b05ccdb3dcaa0c6a"}],"humanReviewed":false,"researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete"},"pauri01":{"id":"pauri01","pauri":1,"meaningEn":"Outward purity, silence, possessions and cleverness cannot by themselves make us truthful. The answer is to live in accord with Hukam, the Divine order and will.","meaningPa":"ਬਾਹਰਲੀ ਸੁੱਚ, ਚੁੱਪ, ਧਨ-ਪਦਾਰਥ ਅਤੇ ਚਤੁਰਾਈ ਆਪਣੇ ਆਪ ਮਨੁੱਖ ਨੂੰ ਸਚਿਆਰਾ ਨਹੀਂ ਬਣਾਉਂਦੇ। ਜਵਾਬ ਹੈ ਹੁਕਮ ਅਤੇ ਰਜ਼ਾ ਅਨੁਸਾਰ ਜੀਵਨ ਤੋਰਨਾ।","directSense":"The first four lines test several ways people might seek inner resolution. Repetition cannot by itself secure purity; imposed silence cannot guarantee inner stillness; accumulating more cannot satisfy craving; and a store of clever strategies is not enough. The fifth line brings the purpose into focus: becoming truthful and breaking the barrier of falsehood. The final line answers with walking in Hukam. Chalaṇa describes a way of living; treating the answer as mere agreement with a sentence would miss that movement.","directSensePa":"ਪਹਿਲੀਆਂ ਚਾਰ ਤੁਕਾਂ ਮਨ ਦੀ ਗੁੰਝਲ ਸੁਲਝਾਉਣ ਦੇ ਕੁਝ ਜਤਨਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਪਰਖਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ। ਵਾਰ-ਵਾਰ ਕੀਤਾ ਬਾਹਰਲਾ ਕਰਮ ਆਪਣੇ ਆਪ ਅੰਦਰਲੀ ਸੁੱਚ ਨਹੀਂ ਬਣਾ ਦਿੰਦਾ; ਮੂੰਹ ਦੀ ਚੁੱਪ ਮਨ ਦਾ ਟਿਕਾਉ ਨਹੀਂ ਬਣ ਜਾਂਦੀ; ਇਕੱਠਾ ਕਰਨ ਨਾਲ ਭੁੱਖ ਮੁੱਕਣੀ ਪੱਕੀ ਨਹੀਂ; ਚਤੁਰਾਈ ਵੀ ਕਾਫ਼ੀ ਨਹੀਂ। ਪੰਜਵੀਂ ਤੁਕ ਸਚਿਆਰਾ ਹੋਣ ਦਾ ਸਵਾਲ ਪੁੱਛਦੀ ਹੈ। ਅਖ਼ੀਰ ਵਿਚ ਹੁਕਮ ਅਨੁਸਾਰ ‘ਚਲਣਾ’ ਜੀਵਨ ਦੇ ਤਰੀਕੇ ਵੱਲ ਲੈ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹੈ।","context":"The opening Salok affirms the True One. Pauri 1 asks about a truthful human life. Pauri 2 then unfolds Hukam rather than changing the subject. Read the question and answer together before isolating any of the opening negations.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੋਚੈ · ਸੋਚਿ","note":"A disputed interpretive checkpoint: Sahib Singh reads purification/cleanliness here; the English translation displayed by SriGranth reads thinking. The two routes must be named, not blended invisibly."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਿਵ · ਸਚਿਆਰਾ","note":"How? Truthful/true in life. The question supplies the aim of the preceding lines."},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਲਿ","note":"A barrier or dividing wall in this line’s imagery, not an instruction to build a literal structure."},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਲਣਾ","note":"To walk or proceed; the response is expressed as lived orientation."}],"pronunciation":"Do not replace ਸੋਚੈ, ਸੋਚਿ and ਸੋਚੀ with one uniform spelling. Their endings differ in the original. Hear the paired questions beginning ਕਿਵ and ask a teacher about the concluding phrase’s grammar before assigning a fixed recitation pause.","interpretations":"Sahib Singh explicitly argues for a purification reading of ਸੋਚੈ, distinguishing it from the intellectual strategies mentioned later. SriGranth’s displayed Sant Singh Khalsa English gives a thinking reading. This draft’s short meaning follows the former and discloses the latter; it does not claim all traditions agree. Hukam should not be reduced to a license for passivity. The practical connection to responsible action is an interpretive application, while the scripture’s explicit answer is to walk in Hukam.","reflection":"Identify one outer practice you rely on. Does it help you live truthfully, or have you begun to treat the action itself as proof of inner change? Keep the practice and examine its relationship to conduct rather than dismissing every practice as useless.","reflectionPa":"ਆਪਣੀ ਕੋਈ ਬਾਹਰਲੀ ਰੀਤ ਵੇਖੋ। ਕੀ ਉਹ ਸੱਚੇ ਵਰਤਾਓ ਵਿਚ ਮਦਦ ਕਰਦੀ ਹੈ ਜਾਂ ਅਸੀਂ ਸਿਰਫ਼ ਕਰ ਲੈਣ ਨੂੰ ਹੀ ਅੰਦਰਲੀ ਤਬਦੀਲੀ ਦਾ ਸਬੂਤ ਮੰਨ ਰਹੇ ਹਾਂ? ਰੀਤ ਨੂੰ ਝੱਟ ਰੱਦ ਕਰਨ ਦੀ ਥਾਂ ਉਸ ਦਾ ਜੀਵਨ ਨਾਲ ਜੋੜ ਪਰਖੀਏ।","teachBack":"Explain both readings of ਸੋਚੈ, say which this draft uses, and show how the fifth and sixth lines guide your reading of the whole Pauri.","teachBackPa":"‘ਸੋਚੈ’ ਦੇ ਦੋ ਪੜ੍ਹੇ ਗਏ ਅਰਥ ਦੱਸੋ। ਇਹ ਮਸੌਦਾ ਕਿਹੜਾ ਅਰਥ ਲੈਂਦਾ ਹੈ? ਪੰਜਵੀਂ ਤੇ ਛੇਵੀਂ ਤੁਕ ਪੂਰੀ ਪਉੜੀ ਨੂੰ ਸਮਝਣ ਵਿਚ ਕਿਵੇਂ ਮਦਦ ਕਰਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ?","sources":[{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0001.html","label":"Darpan · Ang 1 · Pauri 1, especially ਸੋਚੈ discussion"},{"url":"https://www.srigranth.org/servlet/gurbani.gurbani?Action=Page&Param=1","label":"SriGranth · Ang 1 · contrasting English reading of ਸੋਚੈ"}],"status":"draft","unitId":"pauri01","passageIds":["pauri01.line01","pauri01.line02","pauri01.line03","pauri01.line04","pauri01.line05","pauri01.line06"],"sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri01.line01","ang":1,"sourceLine":5,"sha256":"5c0c71b676dc697820dff6ab1cda77b5d491c75b46c2c48adbfe7134e4ba7fc6"},{"passageId":"pauri01.line02","ang":1,"sourceLine":5,"sha256":"0e12e72beb1bb30783a53eb36cd5c6147ae3bf1b3200c78d48dbbfcd5a9830e6"},{"passageId":"pauri01.line03","ang":1,"sourceLine":5,"sha256":"8bcfd795b72ba6e62842fc98485e1661e38003d69ea66cbe85bfa3b138cad26b"},{"passageId":"pauri01.line04","ang":1,"sourceLine":6,"sha256":"5530b0114c2dd6f9a07cbcc5e719e3b04b98bec494194def0d0d0b69999a3565"},{"passageId":"pauri01.line05","ang":1,"sourceLine":6,"sha256":"89bfefa054887bd52501faefc35355b82c94b91193ce8c51c8a9c981fc14479b"},{"passageId":"pauri01.line06","ang":1,"sourceLine":7,"sha256":"ebcd7c74f4cb7876211467c8b1bd2b2d2d93e2540243f6201e91703c4f69e769"}],"humanReviewed":false,"researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete"},"pauri02":{"id":"pauri02","pauri":2,"meaningEn":"All beings and experiences are within Hukam, though Hukam cannot be contained in our descriptions. Understanding it loosens the claim of ego-centred ownership.","meaningPa":"ਸਾਰੇ ਜੀਵ ਅਤੇ ਜੀਵਨ ਦੇ ਹਾਲ ਹੁਕਮ ਅੰਦਰ ਹਨ, ਪਰ ਹੁਕਮ ਸਾਡੇ ਬਿਆਨ ਵਿਚ ਪੂਰਾ ਨਹੀਂ ਸਮਾ ਸਕਦਾ। ਹੁਕਮ ਦੀ ਸੂਝ ਨਾਲ ਹਉਮੈ ਦਾ ਆਪਣਾ ਹੀ ਦਾਅਵਾ ਢਿੱਲਾ ਪੈਂਦਾ ਹੈ।","directSense":"Forms and living beings arise within Hukam; honour, differing conditions, pain, pleasure, grace and wandering are brought within its scope. The fifth line excludes no one. The sixth distinguishes universal inclusion in Hukam from understanding it: that understanding changes the language of haumai. Being subject to an order and consciously recognizing it are therefore not identical. The opening also limits our explanatory confidence—Hukam is not exhausted by our account of it.","directSensePa":"ਆਕਾਰ ਅਤੇ ਜੀਵ ਹੁਕਮ ਵਿਚ ਉਪਜਦੇ ਹਨ। ਵਡਿਆਈ, ਉੱਚਾ-ਨੀਵਾਂ ਹਾਲ, ਦੁੱਖ-ਸੁੱਖ, ਬਖ਼ਸ਼ਿਸ਼ ਅਤੇ ਭਟਕਣਾ ਵੀ ਇਸੇ ਵਿਚ ਆਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ। ਪੰਜਵੀਂ ਤੁਕ ਕਿਸੇ ਨੂੰ ਬਾਹਰ ਨਹੀਂ ਰੱਖਦੀ। ਛੇਵੀਂ ਤੁਕ ਹੁਕਮ ਅੰਦਰ ਹੋਣ ਅਤੇ ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਬੁੱਝਣ ਵਿਚ ਫ਼ਰਕ ਖੋਲ੍ਹਦੀ ਹੈ: ਬੁੱਝਣ ਨਾਲ ਹਉਮੈ ਵਾਲਾ ਕਹਿਣਾ ਬਦਲਦਾ ਹੈ। ਪਹਿਲੀ ਤੁਕ ਇਹ ਵੀ ਯਾਦ ਕਰਾਉਂਦੀ ਹੈ ਕਿ ਹੁਕਮ ਸਾਡੀ ਵਿਆਖਿਆ ਤੋਂ ਵੱਡਾ ਹੈ।","context":"This is the expansion of Pauri 1’s final answer. Pauri 3 moves into the many ways people sing of the Divine. The original Pauri 2 lesson, its six bilingual line explanations and three contextual connections remain available alongside this section-level draft.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹੁਕਮੀ · ਹੁਕਮਿ · ਹੁਕਮੈ","note":"Related forms repeated through the Pauri. The app preserves each spelling; a single English noun cannot display every grammatical relation."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬੁਝੈ","note":"Understands or realizes. The conditional ਜੇ directs attention to recognition, not merely reciting a definition."},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਉਮੈ","note":"The self-asserting ‘I’-orientation. An interpretive gloss, not a diagnosis or a command to erase a person’s dignity."}],"pronunciation":"Keep ਜੀਅ distinct in the written text and notice the different endings in the Hukam forms. The original detailed lesson’s Roman aids are approximate; this visual guide supplies neither pronunciation assessment nor recitation timing.","interpretations":"Hukam is often glossed as order, command or will. Each is partial. The Pauri’s high/low and pain/pleasure language must not be used to label another person’s suffering as deserved or to justify social oppression; those are further claims, not supplied by a line-by-line description here. A reading of haumai as self-centred ownership should also be kept distinct from ordinary identity, agency and the practical responsibility to help.","reflection":"When a plan fails, distinguish what happened, what was outside your control, and what responsible action remains possible. Acceptance of a fact and approval of harm are different responses.","reflectionPa":"ਯੋਜਨਾ ਨਾ ਬਣੇ ਤਾਂ ਜੋ ਹੋਇਆ, ਜੋ ਆਪਣੇ ਵੱਸੋਂ ਬਾਹਰ ਸੀ ਅਤੇ ਜੋ ਜ਼ਿੰਮੇਵਾਰ ਕਦਮ ਹੁਣ ਵੀ ਚੁੱਕ ਸਕਦੇ ਹਾਂ—ਇਨ੍ਹਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਵੱਖਰਾ ਵੇਖੀਏ। ਹਕੀਕਤ ਨੂੰ ਮੰਨਣਾ, ਨੁਕਸਾਨ ਨੂੰ ਠੀਕ ਮੰਨਣਾ ਨਹੀਂ।","teachBack":"If everyone is already within Hukam, what changes when Hukam is understood? Explain without turning acceptance into an excuse not to act.","teachBackPa":"ਜਦੋਂ ਸਭ ਪਹਿਲਾਂ ਹੀ ਹੁਕਮ ਅੰਦਰ ਹਨ ਤਾਂ ਹੁਕਮ ਬੁੱਝਣ ਨਾਲ ਕੀ ਬਦਲਦਾ ਹੈ? ਮੰਨਣ ਨੂੰ ਕਰਮ ਛੱਡਣ ਦਾ ਬਹਾਨਾ ਬਣਾਏ ਬਿਨਾਂ ਸਮਝਾਓ।","sources":[{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0001.html","label":"Darpan · Ang 1 · Pauri 2"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0466.html","label":"Retained contextual source · Ang 466 · Guru Angad Dev Ji’s salok on haumai"},{"url":"https://srec.gurmat.info/articles/sri-guru-granth-sahib/japji-sahib/","label":"SREC · Japji · Pauri 2 comparison"}],"status":"draft","unitId":"pauri02","passageIds":["pauri02.line01","pauri02.line02","pauri02.line03","pauri02.line04","pauri02.line05","pauri02.line06"],"sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri02.line01","ang":1,"sourceLine":7,"sha256":"a27ab546255bbc9aa3e38646b07384b36771635073e4dcd287aee17d22274021"},{"passageId":"pauri02.line02","ang":1,"sourceLine":8,"sha256":"5ef06ee61163baddd39d4303c8acea55cb9651b5e4933e2b7ffd1a11c1c1f6fe"},{"passageId":"pauri02.line03","ang":1,"sourceLine":8,"sha256":"8c439481992a967f62096b37d75aa31141dff30402f14e7336a42b466ac38797"},{"passageId":"pauri02.line04","ang":1,"sourceLine":9,"sha256":"73b6dc0c710f9b101a69109f68837f600537c42f51cd0212c980a503086fc04e"},{"passageId":"pauri02.line05","ang":1,"sourceLine":9,"sha256":"5274917537ffc83a89f7eeba9ce1bf63c7bd15c50802b47f06f6ec20bb7bf1a6"},{"passageId":"pauri02.line06","ang":1,"sourceLine":10,"sha256":"135ba3f6a5997077616ce884c747ea2d0decbb679f17e7540cab49d8fdfef665"}],"humanReviewed":false,"researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete"},"pauri03":{"pauri":3,"titleEn":"Many voices, an inexhaustible Giver","titlePa":"ਅਨੇਕਾਂ ਸੁਰ, ਬੇਅੰਤ ਦਾਤਾਰ","meaningEn":"People praise the One through strength, gifts, wisdom, creation and presence, yet no account contains the whole. The Giver keeps giving; creation moves within Hukam.","meaningPa":"ਕੋਈ ਕਰਤਾਰ ਦੀ ਤਾਕਤ, ਕੋਈ ਦਾਤਾਂ, ਕੋਈ ਗਿਆਨ ਤੇ ਰਚਨਾ ਗਾਉਂਦਾ ਹੈ; ਪਰ ਕੋਈ ਵਰਣਨ ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਪੂਰਾ ਨਹੀਂ ਘੇਰ ਸਕਦਾ। ਦਾਤਾਰ ਦਿੰਦਾ ਰਹਿੰਦਾ ਹੈ ਅਤੇ ਸਾਰੀ ਕਾਰ ਹੁਕਮ ਵਿੱਚ ਚੱਲਦੀ ਹੈ।","directSense":"The repeated opening turns our attention from one speaker to another. They sing of power, generosity, beauty, difficult knowledge, life and death, distance and nearness. These many descriptions do not exhaust the subject. The second movement contrasts the continuing gift with the limits of those receiving it. The final lines return to Hukam and describe the One as flourishing beyond anxiety. This is an original passage summary, not a word-for-word translation.","directSensePa":"ਪਹਿਲਾਂ ਵੱਖ-ਵੱਖ ਮਨੁੱਖਾਂ ਦੇ ਗਾਉਣ ਦਾ ਜ਼ਿਕਰ ਹੈ। ਫਿਰ ਬਾਣੀ ਦਾਤਾਰ ਦੀ ਬੇਅੰਤ ਦਾਤ ਅਤੇ ਲੈਣ ਵਾਲਿਆਂ ਦੀ ਸੀਮਾ ਵੱਲ ਧਿਆਨ ਮੋੜਦੀ ਹੈ। ਅੰਤ ਵਿੱਚ ਮੁੜ ਹੁਕਮ ਅਤੇ ਨਿਰਭਰਤਾ ਤੋਂ ਪਰੇ ਕਰਤਾਰ ਦਾ ਖ਼ਿਆਲ ਆਉਂਦਾ ਹੈ।","context":"Pauri 2 placed every being within Hukam. Pauri 3 now lets a crowd of human descriptions be heard without allowing any one description to become the measure of the One. Pauri 4 will ask what a receiver can offer such a Giver.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗਾਵੈ ਕੋ","note":"The recurring wording introduces someone who sings or praises; follow the repeated grammatical opening across the first eight lines."},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਾਰ","note":"Sahib Singh reads this as beautiful here, rather than the number four. Source: Darpan, Ang 1."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾਣੁ","note":"Strength or capacity. The first line places human capacity beside the power being praised."},{"gurmukhi":"ਵੇਪਰਵਾਹੁ","note":"Beyond anxiety or dependence. Reading this as cruelty or neglect would conflict with the preceding picture of giving."}],"pronunciation":"Reading practice: notice the different endings in ਗਾਵੈ and ਗਾਵਨਿ when the latter appears later in Japji. Keep ਹਾਦਰਾ ਹਦੂਰਿ as the printed two-word phrase. This note supplies no certified recitation or timing.","interpretations":"The contrast between distance and immediate presence reports different descriptions. This draft reads that contrast as a lesson in the limits of the speaker's perspective, not as permission to decide that only one's own perspective is complete. That is an interpretive inference from the sequence. No surveyed consensus of traditional commentaries is claimed.","reflection":"Name one gift you tend to count as entirely your own achievement. Consider who or what made it possible, then choose one way to share its benefit.","reflectionPa":"ਕਿਹੜੀ ਦਾਤ ਨੂੰ ਤੁਸੀਂ ਸਿਰਫ਼ ਆਪਣੀ ਕਮਾਈ ਮੰਨ ਲੈਂਦੇ ਹੋ? ਉਸ ਦੇ ਪਿੱਛੇ ਮਿਲੇ ਸਹਾਰੇ ਯਾਦ ਕਰਕੇ ਉਸ ਦਾ ਕੁਝ ਲਾਭ ਸਾਂਝਾ ਕਰੋ।","teachBack":"Why does a long list of ways to praise end with the limits of the receiver rather than a complete definition of the Giver?","teachBackPa":"ਇੰਨੇ ਵਰਣਨਾਂ ਤੋਂ ਬਾਅਦ ਵੀ ਦਾਤਾਰ ਨੂੰ ਪੂਰਾ ਕਿਉਂ ਨਹੀਂ ਮਾਪਿਆ ਜਾ ਸਕਦਾ?","sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Original Gurmukhi corpus — Japji Pauri 3, Ang 1–2","role":"Primary scripture anchor; exact preserved passage IDs and hashes listed separately"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0001.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Guru Granth Darpan — Ang 1","role":"Consulted interpretive reference; short attributed notes only"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0002.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Guru Granth Darpan — Ang 2","role":"Consulted interpretive reference; short attributed notes only"}],"status":"draft","unitId":"pauri03","passageIds":["pauri03.line01","pauri03.line02","pauri03.line03","pauri03.line04","pauri03.line05","pauri03.line06","pauri03.line07","pauri03.line08","pauri03.line09","pauri03.line10","pauri03.line11","pauri03.line12","pauri03.line13","pauri03.line14"],"angs":[1,2],"sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri03.line01","ang":1,"sourceLine":10,"sha256":"92a9744b7f2bbcd7325e76dba02cc92dc5a44074505beddb86953b9576187f31"},{"passageId":"pauri03.line02","ang":1,"sourceLine":11,"sha256":"0a836a4cc455f4dcb772a1b18cdfa00522deec106dbd4d86a99aa330f0dd3db9"},{"passageId":"pauri03.line03","ang":1,"sourceLine":11,"sha256":"816055bb82db927d5b1e6c98aff7349d5481398ba401d15616c27452339c2d8c"},{"passageId":"pauri03.line04","ang":1,"sourceLine":11,"sha256":"bd33d70538c82585bf0c2adeed523314a85441758b72f9264228140b8d4e173f"},{"passageId":"pauri03.line05","ang":1,"sourceLine":12,"sha256":"7b9f7dc8d2f8d57d854b6f9c31aeebb1f94cfe6ce96e621d9551a626bf834009"},{"passageId":"pauri03.line06","ang":1,"sourceLine":12,"sha256":"5c1b4e4e7d39c0bc67f65ccfe9edd6159fc86848a1260efd46ba376d6446416a"},{"passageId":"pauri03.line07","ang":1,"sourceLine":12,"sha256":"5857bc61483883b936ae5f0d778d6534824f891dd6e653cdb6a70fd0e42b5201"},{"passageId":"pauri03.line08","ang":2,"sourceLine":1,"sha256":"286d40f858aab213e418d0497432f5e7199a39c75caa7a4abf3a0d8c6faa79d1"},{"passageId":"pauri03.line09","ang":2,"sourceLine":1,"sha256":"75cc8682ec02a86bb62b1e70df0e93123f2b1cf1cb644e9138cb7236b39b129e"},{"passageId":"pauri03.line10","ang":2,"sourceLine":1,"sha256":"7342f3444ccd1c7db10baf0dbf1cb4b0b2f64dc977320cf38d23ae4ebe278c27"},{"passageId":"pauri03.line11","ang":2,"sourceLine":2,"sha256":"6ae080d43e79dda59a80249b3338b889d7cd8ead221e66fa96ae7113caa3ba68"},{"passageId":"pauri03.line12","ang":2,"sourceLine":2,"sha256":"37054cb27296b87bd2c40d19997220572cc1d4220ee17b3ba966f70b74e9a734"},{"passageId":"pauri03.line13","ang":2,"sourceLine":2,"sha256":"21dd65dedb651f4190943abab7d10e254f887e3a95d0b6951ed26fb30f12a8db"},{"passageId":"pauri03.line14","ang":2,"sourceLine":3,"sha256":"16ede2c3a7d2273a11ed34013e96cd005c04d2a2bf197edf22e7df913783e966"}],"researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","humanReviewed":false,"reviewNeeds":["Qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review of meaning and grammar","Qualified santhiya review of pronunciation notes","Broader comparison of traditional commentaries"],"id":"pauri03"},"pauri04":{"pauri":4,"titleEn":"What can we offer the Giver?","titlePa":"ਦਾਤਾਰ ਅੱਗੇ ਕੀ ਭੇਟ ਰੱਖੀਏ?","meaningEn":"Before the eternal Giver, turn from endless asking toward loving remembrance and contemplation in Amrit Vela. Nearness and liberation cannot be purchased; grace remains central.","meaningPa":"ਸਦਾ-ਥਿਰ ਦਾਤਾਰ ਅੱਗੇ ਕੇਵਲ ਮੰਗਦੇ ਰਹਿਣ ਦੀ ਥਾਂ ਅੰਮ੍ਰਿਤ ਵੇਲੇ ਨਾਮ ਅਤੇ ਵਡਿਆਈ ਦੀ ਪਿਆਰ ਨਾਲ ਵਿਚਾਰ ਕਰੀਏ। ਰੱਬ ਨਾਲ ਨੇੜਤਾ ਕੋਈ ਸੌਦਾ ਨਹੀਂ; ਮਿਹਰ ਦਾ ਸਥਾਨ ਕੇਂਦਰ ਵਿੱਚ ਹੈ।","directSense":"The passage begins with the enduring One and the relationship of love, then shows beings continually asking for gifts. Two questions follow: what could be placed before the Giver, and what speech could express the desired relationship? The answer directs attention to Amrit Vela, Naam and contemplation of greatness. The clothing image and the opening of liberation follow; their detailed translation is an interpretive checkpoint rather than a settled one-word equivalence.","directSensePa":"ਦਾਤਾਂ ਮੰਗਣ ਦੇ ਜ਼ਿਕਰ ਪਿੱਛੋਂ ਦੋ ਸਵਾਲ ਉੱਠਦੇ ਹਨ: ਕੀ ਭੇਟ ਕਰੀਏ ਅਤੇ ਕੀ ਬੋਲੀਏ? ਬਾਣੀ ਨਾਮ, ਪ੍ਰੇਮ ਤੇ ਵਿਚਾਰ ਵੱਲ ਮੋੜਦੀ ਹੈ। ਕਪੜੇ ਵਾਲੀ ਤੁਕ ਦੇ ਅਰਥਾਂ ਵਿੱਚ ਟੀਕਾਕਾਰਾਂ ਦਾ ਫ਼ਰਕ ਵੱਖਰਾ ਦਰਸਾਇਆ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ।","context":"Pauri 3 established that giving has no end. This Pauri changes the question from obtaining more to the quality of our response. It prepares Pauri 5's joining of singing, listening and love.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਫੇਰਿ ਕਿ","note":"Then what? The question depends on the preceding recognition that the gifts already come from the One."},{"gurmukhi":"ਅੰਮ੍ਰਿਤ ਵੇਲਾ","note":"The life-giving or ambrosial time. Dawn is the received practice in the consulted explanations; this draft specifies no mandatory minute or duration."},{"gurmukhi":"ਵੀਚਾਰੁ","note":"Contemplation or consideration. It matters that remembrance is paired with attention to meaning and greatness."},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਦਰੀ","note":"Through the gracious gaze; do not turn this into a reward formula controlled by the learner."}],"pronunciation":"Keep ਭਾਉ, ਨਾਉ and ਨਾਇ visibly distinct while reading. Do not substitute a familiar spelling for the source form. Ask a qualified teacher about articulation; these notes are not an audio model.","interpretations":"Sahib Singh and SREC understand ਕਰਮੀ and ਕਪੜਾ here through grace and a robe of praise. The English translation displayed by Sri Granth instead connects earlier actions with bodily existence. These are genuinely different explanations; this draft does not combine them into an asserted consensus. Both place liberation with grace. Human review must examine the grammar and wider Gurbani parallels before choosing a detailed teaching emphasis.","reflection":"During one quiet period, begin without asking for an outcome. Attend to the words, name what evokes gratitude, and notice how the quality of your asking changes.","reflectionPa":"ਕਿਸੇ ਸ਼ਾਂਤ ਵੇਲੇ ਪਹਿਲਾਂ ਕੁਝ ਮੰਗਣ ਦੀ ਥਾਂ ਬਾਣੀ ਦੇ ਅਰਥ ਵੱਲ ਧਿਆਨ ਦਿਓ। ਜੋ ਕ੍ਰਿਤੱਗਤਾ ਉੱਭਰੇ, ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਵੇਖੋ।","teachBack":"How is an offering of loving attention different from treating recitation as payment for a desired result?","teachBackPa":"ਪ੍ਰੇਮ ਨਾਲ ਯਾਦ ਕਰਨਾ ਅਤੇ ਮਨਚਾਹੇ ਫਲ ਲਈ ਪਾਠ ਨੂੰ ਸੌਦਾ ਬਣਾਉਣਾ ਕਿਵੇਂ ਵੱਖਰੇ ਹਨ?","sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Original Gurmukhi corpus — Japji Pauri 4, Ang 2","role":"Primary scripture anchor; exact preserved passage IDs and hashes listed separately"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0002.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Guru Granth Darpan — Ang 2","role":"Consulted interpretive reference; short attributed notes only"},{"url":"https://srec.gurmat.info/articles/sri-guru-granth-sahib/japji-sahib/","label":"Sikh Research and Education Center — Japji, Pauri 4","role":"Short comparison of grace/robe reading"},{"url":"https://www.srigranth.org/servlet/gurbani.gurbani?Action=Page&Param=2&g=1&h=0&k=1&p=0&r=0&t=1","label":"Sri Granth — Ang 2, Pauri 4","role":"Contrasting displayed English reading; no modern translation imported"}],"status":"draft","unitId":"pauri04","passageIds":["pauri04.line01","pauri04.line02","pauri04.line03","pauri04.line04","pauri04.line05","pauri04.line06","pauri04.line07"],"angs":[2],"sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri04.line01","ang":2,"sourceLine":3,"sha256":"866202ede96f44a82e3e373071828181681f5cdd73431c4c57586d7ddefc7b45"},{"passageId":"pauri04.line02","ang":2,"sourceLine":3,"sha256":"62e266de07e094b6d07b757b5627e3e1a681596a8483adfad75de42334a74b9a"},{"passageId":"pauri04.line03","ang":2,"sourceLine":4,"sha256":"f5e5c20ca9ab1d22ea8b5788878c7b54faccd5005c4331c27a3047d04341c5fb"},{"passageId":"pauri04.line04","ang":2,"sourceLine":4,"sha256":"fb6037993c41ac0ad14b6c8a30d4f679b8982dca86d884f263ea13af69f2f1ad"},{"passageId":"pauri04.line05","ang":2,"sourceLine":5,"sha256":"56643feeed338eecf3ab31e9b01efaad080f8087659ca7a311f5eef4098cf9a7"},{"passageId":"pauri04.line06","ang":2,"sourceLine":5,"sha256":"abb1353a9569c880efb1938156001c5558406deb773ec75edd173edffc8d6936"},{"passageId":"pauri04.line07","ang":2,"sourceLine":6,"sha256":"66dc6f90d54521bbbf17273a05023be8295d5c1e26f4b8df5e4d22ed8cc38a33"}],"researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","humanReviewed":false,"reviewNeeds":["Qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review of meaning and grammar","Qualified santhiya review of pronunciation notes","Broader comparison of traditional commentaries"],"id":"pauri04"},"pauri05":{"pauri":5,"titleEn":"Sing, listen, hold love","titlePa":"ਗਾਉਣਾ, ਸੁਣਨਾ ਅਤੇ ਪ੍ਰੇਮ","meaningEn":"The One is not something we can manufacture. Through the Guru, join praise and listening with love, and remember the one Giver who sustains every being.","meaningPa":"ਕਰਤਾਰ ਸਾਡਾ ਬਣਾਇਆ ਹੋਇਆ ਨਹੀਂ। ਗੁਰੂ ਦੀ ਸਿੱਖਿਆ ਨਾਲ ਗਾਉਣਾ, ਸੁਣਨਾ ਅਤੇ ਮਨ ਦਾ ਪ੍ਰੇਮ ਇਕੱਠੇ ਹੋਣ; ਸਭ ਜੀਵਾਂ ਦੇ ਇੱਕ ਦਾਤਾਰ ਨੂੰ ਨਾ ਭੁੱਲੀਏ।","directSense":"The opening denies that the One can be set up or produced by human making. The passage then moves into service and praise: sing, listen and keep love in the mind. The Guru is named in relation to sound, knowledge and divine figures familiar to the audience. Rather than ending in a catalogue, the passage becomes a prayer for one understanding: all beings have one Giver, whom the speaker asks not to forget.","directSensePa":"ਆਰੰਭ ਕਰਤਾਰ ਨੂੰ ਮਨੁੱਖੀ ਬਣਾਵਟ ਤੋਂ ਪਰੇ ਦੱਸਦਾ ਹੈ। ਅੱਗੇ ਗਾਇਨ, ਸਰਵਣ ਅਤੇ ਪ੍ਰੇਮ ਦਾ ਜੋੜ ਹੈ। ਅੰਤ ਵਿੱਚ ਬਹੁਤੀਆਂ ਗੱਲਾਂ ਵਿਚੋਂ ਇੱਕ ਸਮਝ ਮੰਗੀ ਜਾਂਦੀ ਹੈ: ਸਭ ਜੀਵਾਂ ਦਾ ਦਾਤਾਰ ਇੱਕ ਹੈ।","context":"Pauri 4 asked for fitting speech before the Giver. Here speech is joined to listening and love. Pauri 6 will repeat the closing prayer, showing that it is a shared anchor rather than a spare ending.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਿਰੰਜਨੁ","note":"Unstained. The term describes the One's freedom from the taint or entanglement named by the image."},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਾਵੀਐ ਸੁਣੀਐ","note":"An invitation to sing and listen. Notice that neither activity is left alone; the following instruction concerns love in the mind."},{"gurmukhi":"ਗੁਰਾ","note":"Sahib Singh reads this as an address to the Guru: a request for understanding. Source: Darpan, Ang 2."},{"gurmukhi":"ਇਕ / ਇਕੁ","note":"The source has two endings. Sahib Singh connects ਇਕ to ਬੁਝਾਈ and ਇਕੁ to ਦਾਤਾ. Preserve both forms. Source: Darpan, Ang 2."}],"pronunciation":"Give the final prayer room as a complete thought. Printed distinctions such as ਗੁਰੁ, ਗੁਰ and ਗੁਰਾ belong to the text; reading aids must not silently flatten them into one spelling.","interpretations":"The line naming ਈਸਰੁ, ਗੋਰਖੁ, ਬਰਮਾ and ਪਾਰਬਤੀ requires care. This draft treats it in the surrounding movement toward the Guru and one Giver, rather than using an isolated line to assert that Sikh teaching simply duplicates another system. The exact force of each identification remains a specialist-review item.","reflection":"When listening to another person today, notice whether you are preparing your reply or receiving what they say. Then return to the difference between merely hearing a sound and hearing with love.","reflectionPa":"ਅੱਜ ਕਿਸੇ ਨੂੰ ਸੁਣਦੇ ਵੇਲੇ ਵੇਖੋ ਕਿ ਤੁਸੀਂ ਜਵਾਬ ਬਣਾਉਂਦੇ ਹੋ ਜਾਂ ਧਿਆਨ ਨਾਲ ਸੁਣਦੇ ਹੋ। ਪ੍ਰੇਮ ਨਾਲ ਸੁਣਨ ਦੀ ਗੁਣਵੱਤਾ ਨੂੰ ਪਛਾਣੋ।","teachBack":"What keeps singing or listening from becoming a purely mechanical act in this Pauri?","teachBackPa":"ਇਸ ਪਉੜੀ ਅਨੁਸਾਰ ਗਾਉਣ ਤੇ ਸੁਣਨ ਨੂੰ ਨਿਰੀ ਰਸਮ ਬਣਨ ਤੋਂ ਕੀ ਬਚਾਉਂਦਾ ਹੈ?","sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Original Gurmukhi corpus — Japji Pauri 5, Ang 2","role":"Primary scripture anchor; exact preserved passage IDs and hashes listed separately"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0002.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Guru Granth Darpan — Ang 2","role":"Consulted interpretive reference; short attributed notes only"}],"status":"draft","unitId":"pauri05","passageIds":["pauri05.line01","pauri05.line02","pauri05.line03","pauri05.line04","pauri05.line05","pauri05.line06","pauri05.line07","pauri05.line08","pauri05.line09","pauri05.line10","pauri05.line11"],"angs":[2],"sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri05.line01","ang":2,"sourceLine":6,"sha256":"ab896868c0680782f28db4ccdd8c8f5bd6785cac99e35af229d0e45eb879674b"},{"passageId":"pauri05.line02","ang":2,"sourceLine":7,"sha256":"00543d38222a35aa4a124f6a5af27a5a2e940202f64e91d2b0ba7dd85b39abe2"},{"passageId":"pauri05.line03","ang":2,"sourceLine":7,"sha256":"05927207d6e1a1e2c4b1f4873238de1b029cab2fb41dbcb7f8bd0202a5b084b8"},{"passageId":"pauri05.line04","ang":2,"sourceLine":7,"sha256":"899c4983c2697577c0655f07d984615e5e01737898e2dafbbbfc838d8b17847e"},{"passageId":"pauri05.line05","ang":2,"sourceLine":8,"sha256":"b2584941f005a8a2213c9c9de3165a5eaf2ae179995f882b296317ed532bc989"},{"passageId":"pauri05.line06","ang":2,"sourceLine":8,"sha256":"a1d9ad341ac988a0c086879e95572c22c2a991e7afc9e7521cbe095d3179e4a2"},{"passageId":"pauri05.line07","ang":2,"sourceLine":8,"sha256":"c790ac8de178a93c126d00b3073b36d92e2cd476d2d465957abf2ac9f4aec13d"},{"passageId":"pauri05.line08","ang":2,"sourceLine":9,"sha256":"4d156471ebff5ab934382050100bf0e6d0e3f168dbff583d5458616356101565"},{"passageId":"pauri05.line09","ang":2,"sourceLine":9,"sha256":"bf1e97362dbd7e84e2632381a6f7e5763765094de16c2a00ded09b94a74811b3"},{"passageId":"pauri05.line10","ang":2,"sourceLine":10,"sha256":"0044b3b13dceba920f7064a72dda3253af5d660c4e997d997833adf23d49b46a"},{"passageId":"pauri05.line11","ang":2,"sourceLine":10,"sha256":"5c722acd0a1dff39c88f240d1f9b2598177efaffcc10ba46f9d36891f47c1e53"}],"researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","humanReviewed":false,"reviewNeeds":["Qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review of meaning and grammar","Qualified santhiya review of pronunciation notes","Broader comparison of traditional commentaries"],"id":"pauri05"},"pauri06":{"pauri":6,"titleEn":"The jewels of understanding","titlePa":"ਮਤਿ ਦੇ ਅੰਦਰਲੇ ਰਤਨ","meaningEn":"An outward ritual is not enough by itself. Receiving the Guru's teaching opens the riches of understanding; keep remembering the one Giver of all life.","meaningPa":"ਕੇਵਲ ਬਾਹਰਲੀ ਰਸਮ ਹੀ ਕਾਫ਼ੀ ਨਹੀਂ। ਗੁਰੂ ਦੀ ਸਿੱਖਿਆ ਮਨ ਵਿੱਚ ਵਸੇ ਤਾਂ ਸਮਝ ਦੇ ਰਤਨ ਪਰਗਟ ਹੁੰਦੇ ਹਨ; ਸਭ ਜੀਵਾਂ ਦੇ ਇੱਕ ਦਾਤਾਰ ਦੀ ਯਾਦ ਬਣੀ ਰਹੇ।","directSense":"Pilgrimage bathing is placed under a question about what is pleasing to the One. The passage then widens to the whole created world and asks what can be received apart from grace. Its image of precious stones locates treasure in understanding, under the condition of hearing the Guru's instruction. The same prayer that ended Pauri 5 returns, carrying the reader back to one Giver for everyone.","directSensePa":"ਤੀਰਥ ਦੇ ਇਸ਼ਨਾਨ ਦੀ ਕੀਮਤ ਬਾਰੇ ਸਵਾਲ ਕਰਨ ਤੋਂ ਬਾਅਦ ਬਾਣੀ ਮਤਿ ਦੇ ਰਤਨਾਂ ਦੀ ਤਸਵੀਰ ਪੇਸ਼ ਕਰਦੀ ਹੈ। ਗੁਰੂ ਦੀ ਸਿੱਖਿਆ ਸੁਣਨ ਨਾਲ ਜੁੜੀ ਇਹ ਅੰਦਰਲੀ ਦੌਲਤ ਇੱਕ ਦਾਤਾਰ ਦੀ ਯਾਦ ਨਾਲ ਸੰਬੰਧਿਤ ਹੈ।","context":"The repeated final two lines connect Pauris 5 and 6. The question is not which outward display is largest, but whether the teaching enters understanding. Pauri 7 extends that challenge to reputation and extraordinary longevity.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੇ","note":"If: the opening and the jewels line are conditional. Notice what must be true rather than reading an automatic guarantee."},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਤਿ","note":"Understanding, judgment or the mind's discernment; the jewel image points to its transformation."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਿਖ","note":"Here Sahib Singh identifies the word as instruction; in Pauri 15 the same printed form refers to disciples. Source: Darpan, Ang 3."}],"pronunciation":"Read ਸਿਖ in its full phrase ਜੇ ਇਕ ਗੁਰ ਕੀ ਸਿਖ ਸੁਣੀ, rather than deciding its meaning from the modern noun 'Sikh' alone. Pronunciation and grammar are related but not identical tasks.","interpretations":"This draft understands the precious stones as an image for cultivated insight, not as a promise of material wealth. The passage challenges automatic spiritual credit from ritual; that does not authorize contempt for people who visit a sacred place. This is an application of the passage's conditional reasoning, not a separate scriptural command.","reflection":"Choose one teaching you already know but seldom practise. Name a small action that would show it has entered your judgment rather than remaining something you can repeat.","reflectionPa":"ਕਿਹੜੀ ਸਿੱਖਿਆ ਤੁਹਾਨੂੰ ਯਾਦ ਹੈ ਪਰ ਜੀਵਨ ਵਿੱਚ ਘੱਟ ਉਤਰਦੀ ਹੈ? ਅੱਜ ਉਸ ਲਈ ਇੱਕ ਛੋਟਾ ਕੰਮ ਚੁਣੋ।","teachBack":"Why does this Pauri move from an outward place of bathing to jewels within understanding?","teachBackPa":"ਬਾਹਰਲੇ ਤੀਰਥ ਤੋਂ ਮਤਿ ਦੇ ਅੰਦਰਲੇ ਰਤਨਾਂ ਵੱਲ ਧਿਆਨ ਕਿਉਂ ਮੋੜਿਆ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ?","sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Original Gurmukhi corpus — Japji Pauri 6, Ang 2","role":"Primary scripture anchor; exact preserved passage IDs and hashes listed separately"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0002.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Guru Granth Darpan — Ang 2","role":"Consulted interpretive reference; short attributed notes only"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0003.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Guru Granth Darpan — Ang 3, comparison of ਸਿਖ in Pauris 6 and 15","role":"Short grammatical note"}],"status":"draft","unitId":"pauri06","passageIds":["pauri06.line01","pauri06.line02","pauri06.line03","pauri06.line04","pauri06.line05"],"angs":[2],"sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri06.line01","ang":2,"sourceLine":11,"sha256":"a697fb318e7df44581c400a39431613f7de4acf834c43c3089a05f48e997eb28"},{"passageId":"pauri06.line02","ang":2,"sourceLine":11,"sha256":"7d7c8636f9ef94c37ded4b962252312bab0953dd1fcf81fc0948e94cae645c8a"},{"passageId":"pauri06.line03","ang":2,"sourceLine":12,"sha256":"d9be33ed54948b5b4fc104cd5df2ce4a5a7c288ae5a6ab58cd30cef64a8b230f"},{"passageId":"pauri06.line04","ang":2,"sourceLine":12,"sha256":"0044b3b13dceba920f7064a72dda3253af5d660c4e997d997833adf23d49b46a"},{"passageId":"pauri06.line05","ang":2,"sourceLine":13,"sha256":"7cbd7502bd565d81874804020229e415a56b1628b512d169211b993ca8e9b246"}],"researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","humanReviewed":false,"reviewNeeds":["Qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review of meaning and grammar","Qualified santhiya review of pronunciation notes","Broader comparison of traditional commentaries"],"id":"pauri06"},"pauri07":{"pauri":7,"titleEn":"Reputation is not the final measure","titlePa":"ਨਾਮਣਾ ਅੰਤਿਮ ਕਸੌਟੀ ਨਹੀਂ","meaningEn":"Even immense lifespan, fame and followers do not establish spiritual worth. The gracious One gives virtue to those who lack it and deepens it in those who have it.","meaningPa":"ਬਹੁਤ ਲੰਮੀ ਉਮਰ, ਸੰਸਾਰਕ ਸ਼ੋਭਾ ਅਤੇ ਵੱਡੀ ਪੈਰਵੀ ਆਤਮਕ ਉੱਚਤਾ ਦੀ ਗਾਰੰਟੀ ਨਹੀਂ। ਮਿਹਰ ਨਾਲ ਗੁਣਹੀਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਵੀ ਗੁਣ ਪੈਦਾ ਹੁੰਦੇ ਹਨ ਅਤੇ ਗੁਣਵਾਨ ਨੂੰ ਵੀ ਗੁਣ ਮਿਲਦੇ ਹਨ।","directSense":"The Pauri builds an imagined case: a life stretching across ages, recognition everywhere, universal following and an excellent reputation. It then overturns the assumption that those achievements are sufficient. Without the gracious gaze, public greatness does not settle the person's standing. The closing movement emphasizes the gift of qualities to both the one lacking them and the one already possessing them.","directSensePa":"ਪਹਿਲੀਆਂ ਤੁਕਾਂ ਲੰਮੀ ਉਮਰ ਅਤੇ ਬਹੁਤ ਵੱਡੇ ਨਾਮਣੇ ਦੀ ਕਲਪਨਾ ਕਰਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ। ਫਿਰ ਇਹ ਮੰਨਤਾ ਟੁੱਟਦੀ ਹੈ ਕਿ ਅਜਿਹੀ ਸ਼ੋਭਾ ਹੀ ਕਾਫ਼ੀ ਹੈ। ਅੰਤ ਗੁਣਾਂ ਦੀ ਦਾਤ ਅਤੇ ਮਿਹਰ ਵੱਲ ਮੁੜਦਾ ਹੈ।","context":"Pauri 6 questioned the sufficiency of ritual. Pauri 7 questions the sufficiency of outward success. Pauris 8–11 next describe the deep change associated with listening, shifting the learner away from public measurement.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਆਰਜਾ","note":"Lifespan. The exaggerated span tests whether more time alone produces the life being sought."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਸੁ ਕੀਰਤਿ","note":"Praise and renown in the world; compare this outward recognition with the later emphasis on virtues."},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਿਰਗੁਣਿ","note":"In this sentence, the person lacking qualities. Do not assume that every use of a similar form has the same grammatical referent."}],"pronunciation":"Observe ਨਿਰਗੁਣਿ and ਗੁਣੁ without rewriting their endings. This lesson does not prescribe a universal rule that every written final vowel receives an identical full spoken value; obtain santhiya guidance for recitation.","interpretations":"The small-creature image reverses human prestige; it should not become a label for a social group or a licence to humiliate someone. This draft reads the closing gift of virtues as leaving the door to change open. It does not equate poverty, illness or lack of recognition with divine rejection.","reflection":"Think of a good action that would matter even if nobody knew you had done it. Let its value be tested by the action itself, not by the response it earns.","reflectionPa":"ਅਜਿਹਾ ਚੰਗਾ ਕੰਮ ਸੋਚੋ ਜਿਸ ਦੀ ਖ਼ਬਰ ਕਿਸੇ ਨੂੰ ਨਾ ਵੀ ਹੋਵੇ ਤਾਂ ਵੀ ਉਹ ਮਹੱਤਵ ਰੱਖੇ। ਉਸ ਦੀ ਕੀਮਤ ਸ਼ੋਭਾ ਨਾਲ ਨਾ ਮਾਪੋ।","teachBack":"What is the difference between having a good reputation and growing in the qualities named at the end?","teachBackPa":"ਚੰਗਾ ਨਾਮ ਹੋਣ ਅਤੇ ਅਸਲ ਗੁਣ ਵਧਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਕੀ ਫ਼ਰਕ ਹੈ?","sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Original Gurmukhi corpus — Japji Pauri 7, Ang 2","role":"Primary scripture anchor; exact preserved passage IDs and hashes listed separately"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0002.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Guru Granth Darpan — Ang 2","role":"Consulted interpretive reference; short attributed notes only"}],"status":"draft","unitId":"pauri07","passageIds":["pauri07.line01","pauri07.line02","pauri07.line03","pauri07.line04","pauri07.line05","pauri07.line06","pauri07.line07"],"angs":[2],"sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri07.line01","ang":2,"sourceLine":13,"sha256":"a9db24780d509751a306c64f698e68c85d1a735377c752082a36ab602fa2bf92"},{"passageId":"pauri07.line02","ang":2,"sourceLine":14,"sha256":"4eb265e9ff3d042ef2977c43527478413b255138573f98d41c431af210830294"},{"passageId":"pauri07.line03","ang":2,"sourceLine":14,"sha256":"ec4927f6f4cf18bad2d5a84def2873e83b06625cd6f63bc8cdb2c764b688a8c1"},{"passageId":"pauri07.line04","ang":2,"sourceLine":15,"sha256":"35832a58cca1a8a1a1e68fc9c2493d0cf40027a8c20e962ce5742e2c40ba6a4c"},{"passageId":"pauri07.line05","ang":2,"sourceLine":15,"sha256":"f1f03db6ffca488b68650990f10fc3793753ea56c9411e3742e017dd577ac0cb"},{"passageId":"pauri07.line06","ang":2,"sourceLine":15,"sha256":"5908e478511615f82d44e7e6cdda40b8f72de4101ac75082332e14d227294c06"},{"passageId":"pauri07.line07","ang":2,"sourceLine":16,"sha256":"b5ac1d3ab151b58db214905c99a89915de8caf31a48ad576c3ab4bfba35ef17d"}],"researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","humanReviewed":false,"reviewNeeds":["Qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review of meaning and grammar","Qualified santhiya review of pronunciation notes","Broader comparison of traditional commentaries"],"id":"pauri07"},"pauri08":{"pauri":8,"titleEn":"Listening opens the horizon","titlePa":"ਸੁਣਨ ਨਾਲ ਵਿਸ਼ਾਲ ਹੁੰਦੀ ਸੁਰਤਿ","meaningEn":"Attentive listening to Naam transforms awareness and opens a wider view of existence. The repeated refrain speaks of the devotee's flourishing and release from the grip of suffering and wrongdoing.","meaningPa":"ਨਾਮ ਵਿੱਚ ਧਿਆਨ ਜੋੜ ਕੇ ਸੁਣਨਾ ਸੁਰਤਿ ਨੂੰ ਬਦਲਦਾ ਅਤੇ ਜੀਵਨ ਦੀ ਦ੍ਰਿਸ਼ਟੀ ਵਿਸ਼ਾਲ ਕਰਦਾ ਹੈ। ਮੁੜ ਆਉਣ ਵਾਲੀ ਟੇਕ ਭਗਤ ਦੇ ਖਿੜਾਉ ਅਤੇ ਦੁੱਖ-ਪਾਪ ਦੀ ਪਕੜ ਟੁੱਟਣ ਦੀ ਗੱਲ ਕਰਦੀ ਹੈ।","directSense":"This begins four Pauris organized around ਸੁਣਿਐ. Spiritual figures are named, followed by earth, its support, the sky, lands, worlds and depths. The scale widens beyond ordinary preoccupations. The verse concerning ਕਾਲੁ and the two-line refrain express the transformative force of listening. The Pauri does not describe a playback device, a minimum listening duration or a technique for controlling physical events.","directSensePa":"ਇਥੋਂ ਸੁਣਿਐ ਵਾਲੀਆਂ ਚਾਰ ਪਉੜੀਆਂ ਸ਼ੁਰੂ ਹੁੰਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ। ਪਹਿਲਾਂ ਆਤਮਕ ਹਸਤੀਆਂ, ਫਿਰ ਧਰਤੀ ਤੇ ਅਕਾਸ਼ ਸਮੇਤ ਵਿਸ਼ਾਲ ਰਚਨਾ ਦਾ ਜ਼ਿਕਰ ਹੈ। ਟੇਕ ਇਸ ਸੁਣਨ ਨੂੰ ਅੰਦਰਲੇ ਖਿੜਾਉ ਅਤੇ ਦੁੱਖ-ਪਾਪ ਤੋਂ ਮੁਕਤੀ ਨਾਲ ਜੋੜਦੀ ਹੈ।","context":"The learner has just been asked to set aside fame as the measure of a life. These Pauris move inward to listening. Pauri 16 will return to ਧਵਲ imagery, so this first appearance should not be turned into a final cosmological explanation.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਣਿਐ","note":"Sahib Singh explains the recurring form through listening with attention joined to Naam. Source: Darpan, Ang 2."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਲੁ","note":"Time or death in this religious setting. The verse needs theological interpretation, not a claim of bodily immortality."},{"gurmukhi":"ਵਿਗਾਸੁ","note":"Flourishing or opening into joy. Notice its contrast with the constriction expressed by suffering and wrongdoing."}],"pronunciation":"Notice the whole vowel pattern of ਸੁਣਿਐ and its repeated place at the start of lines. The guide's visual pace is a study convenience, not the pronunciation or duration of this word.","interpretations":"For this draft, listening means receptive attention that can change a life; it is more than sound entering the ear. The language of freedom from death is presented as a religious claim requiring careful study, not a medical promise or proof that a devout person will never suffer. A full comparison of traditional readings is pending.","reflection":"Read one line without immediately translating it into what you already believe. Make room for a question before deciding you understand.","reflectionPa":"ਇੱਕ ਤੁਕ ਪੜ੍ਹ ਕੇ ਤੁਰੰਤ ਆਪਣੀ ਪਹਿਲਾਂ ਵਾਲੀ ਧਾਰਨਾ ਨਾ ਥੋਪੋ। ਸਮਝਣ ਤੋਂ ਪਹਿਲਾਂ ਇੱਕ ਸਵਾਲ ਲਈ ਥਾਂ ਰੱਖੋ।","teachBack":"How could listening change the listener without giving the listener control over the universe?","teachBackPa":"ਸੁਣਨ ਨਾਲ ਮਨੁੱਖ ਬਦਲ ਸਕਦਾ ਹੈ; ਕੀ ਇਸ ਦਾ ਅਰਥ ਇਹ ਹੈ ਕਿ ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਸਾਰੀ ਰਚਨਾ ਉੱਤੇ ਕਾਬੂ ਮਿਲ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹੈ? ਕਿਉਂ ਨਹੀਂ?","sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Original Gurmukhi corpus — Japji Pauri 8, Ang 2","role":"Primary scripture anchor; exact preserved passage IDs and hashes listed separately"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0002.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Guru Granth Darpan — Ang 2","role":"Consulted interpretive reference; short attributed notes only"}],"status":"draft","unitId":"pauri08","passageIds":["pauri08.line01","pauri08.line02","pauri08.line03","pauri08.line04","pauri08.line05","pauri08.line06"],"angs":[2],"sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri08.line01","ang":2,"sourceLine":16,"sha256":"dfd7a353c5b0d176bcbefb116e1fc5b9302031e60c0dd030eaf3a6f4e70ef333"},{"passageId":"pauri08.line02","ang":2,"sourceLine":17,"sha256":"a7a82f0faecfabec5df7744f6c9c685125d34541477f28ef449449ffdf203c85"},{"passageId":"pauri08.line03","ang":2,"sourceLine":17,"sha256":"c8d590ec06bac426c83fec9409bdb3ce9b8df9917b6a0aff8fba3bf5043a4467"},{"passageId":"pauri08.line04","ang":2,"sourceLine":17,"sha256":"2194109c98669a0327e617d024d1e74f1c8c0c368691d930555df69e69e96202"},{"passageId":"pauri08.line05","ang":2,"sourceLine":18,"sha256":"c45d2e50e96796ab1f749ac1e0c6a7bb4e1d3ad17251e4c92dc79bbb24df2b22"},{"passageId":"pauri08.line06","ang":2,"sourceLine":18,"sha256":"4b1e21c070c1c73e3d734aeb11488339eba4dd2cc2c0031d6e43cc500b66fae9"}],"researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","humanReviewed":false,"reviewNeeds":["Qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review of meaning and grammar","Qualified santhiya review of pronunciation notes","Broader comparison of traditional commentaries"],"id":"pauri08"},"pauri09":{"pauri":9,"titleEn":"Listening can change the speaker","titlePa":"ਸੁਣਨ ਨਾਲ ਬੋਲਣ ਵਾਲਾ ਵੀ ਬਦਲਦਾ ਹੈ","meaningEn":"Listening opens understanding and can turn a life away from harmful conduct toward praise. Religious learning finds its purpose in transformation, not in possessing impressive names or information.","meaningPa":"ਸੁਣਨ ਨਾਲ ਸਮਝ ਖੁੱਲ੍ਹਦੀ ਹੈ ਅਤੇ ਮੰਦੇ ਜੀਵਨ ਵਾਲਾ ਵੀ ਸਿਫ਼ਤਿ ਵੱਲ ਮੁੜ ਸਕਦਾ ਹੈ। ਧਾਰਮਿਕ ਜਾਣਕਾਰੀ ਦੀ ਕਦਰ ਜੀਵਨ ਦੇ ਬਦਲਾਅ ਵਿੱਚ ਹੈ, ਕੇਵਲ ਵੱਡੇ ਨਾਮ ਜਾਣਨ ਵਿੱਚ ਨਹੀਂ।","directSense":"The second listening Pauri names ਈਸਰੁ, ਬਰਮਾ and ਇੰਦੁ, then brings the movement close to the listener: the one called ਮੰਦੁ begins to praise. It turns next to the way of union, the body's mystery, and religious books. The same refrain as Pauri 8 joins these lines to the devotee's flourishing. Read the list as part of this movement rather than as a promise of instant mastery of every subject.","directSensePa":"ਦੂਜੀ ਸੁਣਿਐ ਪਉੜੀ ਵਿੱਚ ਜਾਣੀਆਂ-ਪਛਾਣੀਆਂ ਦੇਵ ਹਸਤੀਆਂ, ਜੋਗ ਅਤੇ ਧਾਰਮਿਕ ਗ੍ਰੰਥਾਂ ਦਾ ਜ਼ਿਕਰ ਹੈ। ਵਿਚਕਾਰ ਮੰਦੇ ਮਨੁੱਖ ਦੇ ਸਾਲਾਹ ਵੱਲ ਮੁੜਨ ਦੀ ਗੱਲ ਬਦਲਾਅ ਨੂੰ ਸਾਡੇ ਆਪਣੇ ਜੀਵਨ ਨਾਲ ਜੋੜਦੀ ਹੈ।","context":"Pauri 8 opened a wide horizon. Pauri 9 asks what listening can do within the one who speaks and acts. Pauri 10 will name generosity, contentment and understanding, making the ethical direction even clearer.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮੁਖਿ","note":"At or through the mouth. Watch how the sentence links listening with a changed kind of speech."},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੰਦੁ","note":"The one described as bad or impaired in conduct, rather than a permanently excluded class of people."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋਗ ਜੁਗਤਿ","note":"The way or discipline of union; the paired words invite attention to a lived way, not just a label."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਾਸਤ ਸਿਮ੍ਰਿਤਿ ਵੇਦ","note":"Named bodies of religious learning. Their presence in the verse does not make this lesson a survey of their contents."}],"pronunciation":"Keep ਬਰਮਾ as it appears in the preserved text; do not silently replace it with a modern Sanskrit spelling. Notice the distinct consonant sequences in ਸਾਸਤ and ਸਿਮ੍ਰਿਤਿ and seek a trained reader's guidance.","interpretations":"This lesson's claim about transformation follows the line joining ਮੰਦੁ to praise. It does not claim that a brief listening session confers supernatural knowledge, anatomy expertise or the status of a named deity. Exactly how the opening list functions in different commentarial traditions remains to be compared.","reflection":"Choose one harsh phrase that comes easily to you. Pause before using it and try words that are truthful without making another person smaller.","reflectionPa":"ਆਪਣੀ ਇੱਕ ਕਠੋਰ ਬੋਲੀ ਪਛਾਣੋ। ਉਸ ਦੀ ਥਾਂ ਅਜਿਹੇ ਸੱਚੇ ਬੋਲ ਚੁਣੋ ਜੋ ਦੂਜੇ ਨੂੰ ਨੀਵਾਂ ਨਾ ਕਰਨ।","teachBack":"Why is the change in the person called ਮੰਦੁ important in a Pauri that also names sacred books and powerful figures?","teachBackPa":"ਵੱਡੀਆਂ ਹਸਤੀਆਂ ਤੇ ਗ੍ਰੰਥਾਂ ਦੇ ਜ਼ਿਕਰ ਵਿਚ ਮੰਦੁ ਦਾ ਬਦਲਣਾ ਕਿਉਂ ਮਹੱਤਵਪੂਰਨ ਹੈ?","sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Original Gurmukhi corpus — Japji Pauri 9, Ang 2–3","role":"Primary scripture anchor; exact preserved passage IDs and hashes listed separately"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0002.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Guru Granth Darpan — Ang 2","role":"Consulted interpretive reference; short attributed notes only"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0003.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Guru Granth Darpan — Ang 3","role":"Consulted interpretive reference; short attributed notes only"}],"status":"draft","unitId":"pauri09","passageIds":["pauri09.line01","pauri09.line02","pauri09.line03","pauri09.line04","pauri09.line05","pauri09.line06"],"angs":[2,3],"sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri09.line01","ang":2,"sourceLine":18,"sha256":"db6fa74cdcf01d38285bf2aa3bfbf04801205a6a12781160d3a2881ba5432183"},{"passageId":"pauri09.line02","ang":2,"sourceLine":19,"sha256":"143ba67754590203bf6e7d3bd2de0f156242c93a7c8efba71a5c4be10a68d483"},{"passageId":"pauri09.line03","ang":2,"sourceLine":19,"sha256":"5465c852719b2c33c98116940a3bfaf404793aa90c06079764cd12df74b71168"},{"passageId":"pauri09.line04","ang":2,"sourceLine":19,"sha256":"c4ef62e19d237200dd43ff31d17ce50d7e8c158e2904a31fa5e791dec28d2211"},{"passageId":"pauri09.line05","ang":2,"sourceLine":19,"sha256":"c45d2e50e96796ab1f749ac1e0c6a7bb4e1d3ad17251e4c92dc79bbb24df2b22"},{"passageId":"pauri09.line06","ang":3,"sourceLine":1,"sha256":"5cad024c6c1503a7e5a29ce04b3528b6c97da9acc07ba3b1396cd0651a8857b6"}],"researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","humanReviewed":false,"reviewNeeds":["Qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review of meaning and grammar","Qualified santhiya review of pronunciation notes","Broader comparison of traditional commentaries"],"id":"pauri09"},"pauri10":{"pauri":10,"titleEn":"Listening ripens into qualities","titlePa":"ਸੁਣਨਾ ਗੁਣਾਂ ਵਿੱਚ ਫਲਦਾ ਹੈ","meaningEn":"Deep listening ripens into generosity, contentment, understanding and steady attention. It turns the search for cleansing and honor toward an inwardly changed life.","meaningPa":"ਧਿਆਨ ਨਾਲ ਸੁਣਨਾ ਦਾਨੀ ਸੁਭਾਉ, ਸੰਤੋਖ, ਗਿਆਨ ਅਤੇ ਸਹਜ ਧਿਆਨ ਵੱਲ ਲੈ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹੈ। ਸੁੱਚਤਾ ਅਤੇ ਮਾਣ ਦੀ ਭਾਲ ਅੰਦਰਲੇ ਬਦਲੇ ਹੋਏ ਜੀਵਨ ਵੱਲ ਮੁੜਦੀ ਹੈ।","directSense":"The third listening Pauri names qualities, then places listening beside the image of bathing at sixty-eight sacred places and the honor associated with learning. Its next line names attention established in ਸਹਜਿ. The refrain remains unchanged. The movement is from recognized religious achievements toward the kind of person who is being formed.","directSensePa":"ਇਸ ਪਉੜੀ ਵਿੱਚ ਸੁਣਨ ਦੇ ਨਾਲ ਗੁਣਾਂ ਦਾ ਸਪਸ਼ਟ ਜ਼ਿਕਰ ਹੈ। ਤੀਰਥ ਇਸ਼ਨਾਨ ਅਤੇ ਪੜ੍ਹਾਈ ਦੇ ਮਾਣ ਦੀਆਂ ਜਾਣੀਆਂ ਤਸਵੀਰਾਂ ਅੱਗੇ ਸਹਜ ਧਿਆਨ ਆਉਂਦਾ ਹੈ। ਧਿਆਨ ਇਸ ਗੱਲ ਉੱਤੇ ਹੈ ਕਿ ਮਨੁੱਖ ਕਿਹੋ ਜਿਹਾ ਬਣਦਾ ਹੈ।","context":"This continues Pauris 8 and 9 without changing the refrain. It also recalls Pauri 6's question about pilgrimage: outward activity alone is not the complete measure. Pauri 11 will carry the listening sequence toward finding a way through what seemed unfathomable.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਤੁ","note":"Sahib Singh reads this as generosity in its pairing with contentment, distinguishing it from ਸਤਿ. Source: Darpan, Ang 3."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਤੋਖੁ","note":"Contentment. In this lesson it is considered beside giving, rather than as permission to ignore preventable injustice."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਹਜਿ","note":"In steadiness or natural poise. The ending relates the word to the setting in which attention becomes established."},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਠਸਠਿ","note":"Sixty-eight. It belongs to the pilgrimage image; the app does not convert it into a count of repetitions."}],"pronunciation":"Keep the written distinction between ਸਤੁ and ਸਤਿ. A font or reading aid must not erase the lower vowel mark. A qualified teacher should review the spoken treatment rather than relying on Roman spelling.","interpretations":"The meaning of ਸਤੁ is a particular lexical decision, not evidence that every translator using another English word is careless. This draft follows the cited reading while leaving broader comparison open. Our practical connection between generosity and reduced possessiveness is an educational inference, separate from the source text.","reflection":"Try one act of giving that does not seek acknowledgment. Observe whether contentment makes giving easier, and whether giving changes the feeling of 'not enough'.","reflectionPa":"ਇੱਕ ਨੇਕੀ ਬਿਨਾ ਸ਼ੋਭਾ ਦੀ ਆਸ ਦੇ ਕਰੋ। ਵੇਖੋ ਕਿ ਸੰਤੋਖ ਅਤੇ ਦੇਣ ਦੀ ਇੱਛਾ ਇਕ-ਦੂਜੇ ਨਾਲ ਕਿਵੇਂ ਜੁੜਦੇ ਹਨ।","teachBack":"What would distinguish knowledge that changes a life from information collected mainly for status?","teachBackPa":"ਜੀਵਨ ਬਦਲਣ ਵਾਲੇ ਗਿਆਨ ਅਤੇ ਕੇਵਲ ਮਾਣ ਲਈ ਇਕੱਠੀ ਕੀਤੀ ਜਾਣਕਾਰੀ ਵਿੱਚ ਕੀ ਫ਼ਰਕ ਹੈ?","sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Original Gurmukhi corpus — Japji Pauri 10, Ang 3","role":"Primary scripture anchor; exact preserved passage IDs and hashes listed separately"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0003.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Guru Granth Darpan — Ang 3","role":"Consulted interpretive reference; short attributed notes only"}],"status":"draft","unitId":"pauri10","passageIds":["pauri10.line01","pauri10.line02","pauri10.line03","pauri10.line04","pauri10.line05","pauri10.line06"],"angs":[3],"sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri10.line01","ang":3,"sourceLine":1,"sha256":"13dcdafd0ace7de0c890bf43ad7597d4f8346519b862e50a401c5c43d2a962f1"},{"passageId":"pauri10.line02","ang":3,"sourceLine":1,"sha256":"fe631457d03657e23283e330c2dabaab62574f25199af13c632d997cd219da4d"},{"passageId":"pauri10.line03","ang":3,"sourceLine":2,"sha256":"a6b4304a5a484450eeb2db6a258d0d143f46c5e846e0cbff7cd449fc9cda82f6"},{"passageId":"pauri10.line04","ang":3,"sourceLine":2,"sha256":"7bd6dca9857ea125bb93546384129d2dca5d9d47874a0cef5e9506a935d7459f"},{"passageId":"pauri10.line05","ang":3,"sourceLine":2,"sha256":"c45d2e50e96796ab1f749ac1e0c6a7bb4e1d3ad17251e4c92dc79bbb24df2b22"},{"passageId":"pauri10.line06","ang":3,"sourceLine":3,"sha256":"5826facf9af42fb3f2e4c4f3006a8949bf982afc6ea3d0efb6b6ae7517c45604"}],"researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","humanReviewed":false,"reviewNeeds":["Qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review of meaning and grammar","Qualified santhiya review of pronunciation notes","Broader comparison of traditional commentaries"],"id":"pauri10"},"pauri11":{"pauri":11,"titleEn":"A way through the unfathomable","titlePa":"ਅਥਾਹ ਵਿੱਚ ਰਾਹ ਦੀ ਸੂਝ","meaningEn":"Listening deepens acquaintance with virtues and gives direction where understanding was absent. What felt like an unfathomable expanse becomes something through which one can find a way.","meaningPa":"ਸੁਣਨ ਨਾਲ ਗੁਣਾਂ ਦੀ ਸੂਝ ਡੂੰਘੀ ਹੁੰਦੀ ਅਤੇ ਗਿਆਨਹੀਣ ਮਨ ਨੂੰ ਰਾਹ ਮਿਲਦਾ ਹੈ। ਜੋ ਜੀਵਨ ਅਥਾਹ ਤੇ ਅਣਸਮਝ ਲੱਗਦਾ ਸੀ, ਉਸ ਵਿੱਚ ਤੁਰਨ ਦੀ ਸਮਝ ਪੈਦਾ ਹੁੰਦੀ ਹੈ।","directSense":"The last ਸੁਣਿਐ Pauri begins with the image of entering the depths of virtues. It names figures of spiritual and worldly authority, then speaks of those without sight finding a path and of gaining a sounding in what seemed beyond sounding. The recurring refrain completes the four-Pauri sequence. Its images are about finding depth and direction, not about possessing an exhaustive inventory of creation.","directSensePa":"ਸੁਣਿਐ ਦੀ ਲੜੀ ਦੇ ਅੰਤ ਵਿੱਚ ਗੁਣਾਂ ਦੀ ਡੂੰਘਾਈ, ਰਾਹ ਲੱਭਣ ਅਤੇ ਅਸਗਾਹ ਦੀ ਥਾਹ ਦੀਆਂ ਤਸਵੀਰਾਂ ਆਉਂਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ। ਚਾਰਾਂ ਪਉੜੀਆਂ ਦੀ ਸਾਂਝੀ ਟੇਕ ਇਸ ਵਿਚਾਰ ਨੂੰ ਪੂਰਾ ਕਰਦੀ ਹੈ।","context":"Pauris 8–11 have moved through cosmic scale, learning, ethical qualities and direction. Pauri 12 will shift from ਸੁਣਿਐ to ਮੰਨੇ: hearing is followed by the question of inward acceptance and trust.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਰਾ ਗੁਣਾ","note":"An image of reservoirs or pools of qualities. Read it with ਗਾਹ, the movement into their depth."},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਾਥ","note":"Sahib Singh distinguishes this feminine noun, meaning a sounding or understanding of depth, from ਹਾਥੁ, a hand. Source: Darpan, Ang 3."},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਸਗਾਹੁ","note":"Unfathomable: something whose depth cannot readily be sounded."}],"pronunciation":"Do not add a final ਔਂਕੜ to ਹਾਥ in the displayed line. Preserve the source even when a familiar everyday word suggests a different spelling or meaning.","interpretations":"This draft reads the sight-and-path image spiritually, as lack of understanding giving way to direction. It does not equate physical blindness with moral deficiency or promise restoration of vision. The distinction protects both the verse's imagery and the dignity of readers with disabilities.","reflection":"Identify a decision that feels too large to solve at once. Instead of claiming complete certainty, name the next truthful and compassionate step available to you.","reflectionPa":"ਜਿਹੜਾ ਫ਼ੈਸਲਾ ਬਹੁਤ ਵੱਡਾ ਲੱਗਦਾ ਹੈ, ਉਸ ਲਈ ਪੂਰੀ ਪੱਕੀ ਜਾਣਕਾਰੀ ਦਾ ਦਾਅਵਾ ਨਾ ਕਰੋ। ਅਗਲਾ ਸੱਚਾ ਤੇ ਦਇਆਲੂ ਕਦਮ ਪਛਾਣੋ।","teachBack":"How does having a trustworthy direction differ from knowing the full depth of everything?","teachBackPa":"ਸਹੀ ਦਿਸ਼ਾ ਮਿਲਣ ਅਤੇ ਹਰ ਚੀਜ਼ ਦਾ ਪੂਰਾ ਅੰਤ ਜਾਣ ਲੈਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਕੀ ਫ਼ਰਕ ਹੈ?","sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Original Gurmukhi corpus — Japji Pauri 11, Ang 3","role":"Primary scripture anchor; exact preserved passage IDs and hashes listed separately"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0003.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Guru Granth Darpan — Ang 3","role":"Consulted interpretive reference; short attributed notes only"}],"status":"draft","unitId":"pauri11","passageIds":["pauri11.line01","pauri11.line02","pauri11.line03","pauri11.line04","pauri11.line05","pauri11.line06"],"angs":[3],"sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri11.line01","ang":3,"sourceLine":3,"sha256":"cbdfac645afad246e01f11fd1ea57a5ed1647b742bf2437ddfa970d3bc0a0cc2"},{"passageId":"pauri11.line02","ang":3,"sourceLine":3,"sha256":"31ce7a4144bfa65fd5c5430e58ffa462d47d9d0168d8778567e0dfd6481e17f0"},{"passageId":"pauri11.line03","ang":3,"sourceLine":3,"sha256":"bacfd5e65da5b0ef05bda34aeed38a8cd44648b155a39842b1edd0ac0377ce78"},{"passageId":"pauri11.line04","ang":3,"sourceLine":4,"sha256":"5486fb1fa1e8cc9cd6efe2a81fc025752131d5d3537fe1342677897c58632bcf"},{"passageId":"pauri11.line05","ang":3,"sourceLine":4,"sha256":"c45d2e50e96796ab1f749ac1e0c6a7bb4e1d3ad17251e4c92dc79bbb24df2b22"},{"passageId":"pauri11.line06","ang":3,"sourceLine":4,"sha256":"2ec37711be08079fdee061c8e0b1bab65933cfc3cb1d568207f1d74ad5c276e8"}],"researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","humanReviewed":false,"reviewNeeds":["Qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review of meaning and grammar","Qualified santhiya review of pronunciation notes","Broader comparison of traditional commentaries"],"id":"pauri11"},"pauri12":{"pauri":12,"titleEn":"What description cannot contain","titlePa":"ਜਿਹੜੀ ਅਵਸਥਾ ਵਰਣਨ ਤੋਂ ਪਰੇ ਹੈ","meaningEn":"The inward state of one who truly accepts Naam cannot be fully captured in speech or writing. This understanding asks for lived trust, not only an account of someone else's experience.","meaningPa":"ਜਿਸ ਦਾ ਮਨ ਨਾਮ ਵਿੱਚ ਪਤੀਜ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹੈ, ਉਸ ਦੀ ਅੰਦਰਲੀ ਅਵਸਥਾ ਬੋਲ ਜਾਂ ਲਿਖਤ ਵਿੱਚ ਪੂਰੀ ਨਹੀਂ ਸਮਾ ਸਕਦੀ। ਇਸ ਨੂੰ ਸਿਰਫ਼ ਸੁਣੀ ਗੱਲ ਦੀ ਥਾਂ ਆਪਣੀ ਲਗਨ ਨਾਲ ਜਾਣਨਾ ਪੈਂਦਾ ਹੈ।","directSense":"The first Pauri in this sequence stresses the limits of describing the one who has accepted or trusted. Speaking may leave the speaker regretting an inadequate account; paper, pen and discussion do not contain the state. The closing refrain points to the purity of Naam and to inwardly knowing through acceptance. The claim is not that writing is useless: the written Pauri itself teaches while acknowledging its limits.","directSensePa":"ਇਥੇ ਕਹਿਣ, ਲਿਖਣ ਅਤੇ ਵਿਚਾਰ ਕਰਨ ਦੀ ਸੀਮਾ ਸਾਹਮਣੇ ਆਉਂਦੀ ਹੈ। ਬਾਣੀ ਲਿਖਤ ਨੂੰ ਰੱਦ ਨਹੀਂ ਕਰਦੀ; ਲਿਖਤ ਰਾਹੀਂ ਹੀ ਉਸ ਅਨੁਭਵ ਵੱਲ ਸੰਕੇਤ ਕਰਦੀ ਹੈ ਜੋ ਨਿਰੀ ਜਾਣਕਾਰੀ ਤੋਂ ਵੱਧ ਹੈ।","context":"After four Pauris of listening, four Pauris explore acceptance and trust. Pauri 12 first guards against reducing this to an impressive verbal description. Pauris 13–15 will describe its effects in awareness, direction and relationship.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮੰਨੇ","note":"Sahib Singh distinguishes 'of the one who accepts' here from ਮੰਨੈ, 'through accepting', in the following Pauris. Source: Darpan, Ang 3."},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਤਿ","note":"Condition or state; the question concerns the person's way of being, not merely an opinion held."},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੰਨਿ / ਮਨਿ","note":"The refrain prints two distinct words. Follow the complete sentence; visual similarity is not identity of meaning."}],"pronunciation":"Watch the doubled consonant sign in ਮੰਨਿ and the single consonant in ਮਨਿ. Keep their printed forms intact and ask for trained pronunciation guidance rather than guessing from English transliteration.","interpretations":"This draft uses 'acceptance' and 'trust' provisionally. Neither means accepting every claim without question or obeying a human teacher without discernment. The object and context are Naam. An authentic experience also cannot be verified merely because someone says it is beyond words; that caution is our application, not a translation.","reflection":"Recall a skill or relationship that you understand differently through living it than through reading about it. Use that distinction to ask what 'knowing' might require here, without equating the two experiences.","reflectionPa":"ਕੋਈ ਅਜਿਹੀ ਗੱਲ ਯਾਦ ਕਰੋ ਜੋ ਜੀ ਕੇ ਸਮਝ ਆਈ, ਸਿਰਫ਼ ਪੜ੍ਹ ਕੇ ਨਹੀਂ। ਉਸ ਫ਼ਰਕ ਨਾਲ ਇਥੇ ਜਾਣਨ ਦੇ ਭਾਵ ਨੂੰ ਵਿਚਾਰੋ।","teachBack":"Why can this Pauri use words to teach while warning that words cannot contain the whole state?","teachBackPa":"ਬਾਣੀ ਸ਼ਬਦਾਂ ਰਾਹੀਂ ਸਿਖਾਉਂਦੀ ਹੋਈ ਸ਼ਬਦਾਂ ਦੀ ਸੀਮਾ ਕਿਵੇਂ ਦੱਸਦੀ ਹੈ?","sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Original Gurmukhi corpus — Japji Pauri 12, Ang 3","role":"Primary scripture anchor; exact preserved passage IDs and hashes listed separately"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0003.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Guru Granth Darpan — Ang 3","role":"Consulted interpretive reference; short attributed notes only"}],"status":"draft","unitId":"pauri12","passageIds":["pauri12.line01","pauri12.line02","pauri12.line03","pauri12.line04","pauri12.line05","pauri12.line06"],"angs":[3],"sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri12.line01","ang":3,"sourceLine":5,"sha256":"9eef5b7afddf216c1ff032b1a8f218e6ca1c28a0ac4fb08fc1dcfd8807d06a1c"},{"passageId":"pauri12.line02","ang":3,"sourceLine":5,"sha256":"550927bb142636c42d326a14e5ca02b50034359f4bcffc269c7017879b45aba7"},{"passageId":"pauri12.line03","ang":3,"sourceLine":5,"sha256":"bf177841024117e04f6e3dc00535cbe10e166a64280fcf8d90364d4a71095ac1"},{"passageId":"pauri12.line04","ang":3,"sourceLine":5,"sha256":"4cd135b0811138b819fd506d77ee25b6556e262fde324a1043c24e57c889a000"},{"passageId":"pauri12.line05","ang":3,"sourceLine":6,"sha256":"4347c1cccd40cc451316af51f9704e63f6983687b2f83a5e1e217b82aa8fee30"},{"passageId":"pauri12.line06","ang":3,"sourceLine":6,"sha256":"31f6ba87d3e82a9f67a2fe664ffd203ec40dcd3f1e216ff218a304c36b86139e"}],"researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","humanReviewed":false,"reviewNeeds":["Qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review of meaning and grammar","Qualified santhiya review of pronunciation notes","Broader comparison of traditional commentaries"],"id":"pauri12"},"pauri13":{"pauri":13,"titleEn":"Trust awakens discernment","titlePa":"ਮੰਨਣ ਨਾਲ ਜਾਗਦੀ ਸੂਝ","meaningEn":"When Naam is inwardly accepted, awareness and discernment awaken. The Pauri speaks of freedom from the blows of degradation and the claim of death, within its spiritual language of liberation.","meaningPa":"ਨਾਮ ਵਿੱਚ ਮਨ ਪਤੀਜਣ ਨਾਲ ਸੁਰਤਿ ਅਤੇ ਬੁੱਧਿ ਜਾਗਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ। ਬਾਣੀ ਆਤਮਕ ਮੁਕਤੀ ਦੀ ਭਾਸ਼ਾ ਵਿੱਚ ਵਿਕਾਰਾਂ ਦੀ ਮਾਰ ਅਤੇ ਜਮ ਦੀ ਪਕੜ ਤੋਂ ਛੁਟਕਾਰੇ ਦੀ ਗੱਲ ਕਰਦੀ ਹੈ।","directSense":"The repeated ਮੰਨੈ introduces effects: awakened awareness, understanding extending across the worlds, freedom from humiliating blows and from accompanying ਜਮ. The refrain returns to Naam and inward acceptance. These are theological and spiritual images; this draft does not turn them into guarantees against accidents, disease or bodily death.","directSensePa":"ਮੰਨੈ ਦੀ ਦੁਹਰਾਈ ਸੁਰਤਿ, ਬੁੱਧਿ ਅਤੇ ਸੁਧਿ ਦੇ ਬਦਲਾਅ ਨੂੰ ਜੋੜਦੀ ਹੈ। ਚੋਟਾਂ ਅਤੇ ਜਮ ਵਾਲੀਆਂ ਤੁਕਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਆਤਮਕ ਸੰਦਰਭ ਵਿੱਚ ਪੜ੍ਹਨਾ ਹੈ, ਸਰੀਰਕ ਹਾਨੀ ਤੋਂ ਪੱਕੀ ਛੋਟ ਦੇ ਵਾਅਦੇ ਵਜੋਂ ਨਹੀਂ।","context":"Pauri 12 said that the accepted person's condition cannot be fully described. Pauri 13 nevertheless offers signs of its direction: wakefulness and release, rather than a claim of superior social rank. Pauri 14 continues with the image of a path.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਰਤਿ","note":"Awareness or attentive consciousness. Notice that it appears with ਬੁਧਿ rather than replacing discernment."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਧਿ","note":"Awareness or understanding of something; it is not the same word as ਸੁਰਤਿ despite the related semantic field."},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੁਹਿ","note":"At the face or mouth; in the blows image it contributes to the sense of abasement."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਮ","note":"The figure of death and judgment. A full account of its uses across Gurbani is beyond this draft lesson."}],"pronunciation":"Read ਸੁਰਤਿ, ਸੁਧਿ and ਬੁਧਿ carefully as separate words; preserve each consonant and vowel mark. The notes identify contrasts to study, not a complete santhiya lesson.","interpretations":"The reference to all worlds should not be presented as omniscience in astronomy or prediction of events. Our reading emphasizes a transformed way of seeing life. Traditional accounts may develop the liberation imagery further; the draft does not claim that one psychological explanation exhausts it.","reflection":"When a strong emotion arises, name it before acting. Consider whether remembering your deeper commitments makes your next choice more awake and less automatic.","reflectionPa":"ਤਿੱਖੀ ਭਾਵਨਾ ਉੱਠੇ ਤਾਂ ਪਹਿਲਾਂ ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਪਛਾਣੋ। ਵੇਖੋ ਕਿ ਆਪਣੀ ਮੁੱਖ ਸਿੱਖਿਆ ਯਾਦ ਕਰਨ ਨਾਲ ਅਗਲਾ ਕੰਮ ਹੋਰ ਸੁਚੇਤ ਹੁੰਦਾ ਹੈ ਜਾਂ ਨਹੀਂ।","teachBack":"Why should trust in this Pauri be connected with awakened discernment rather than with abandoning thought?","teachBackPa":"ਇਥੇ ਮੰਨਣ ਨੂੰ ਬੁੱਧਿ ਦੇ ਜਾਗਣ ਨਾਲ ਕਿਉਂ ਜੋੜਿਆ ਹੈ, ਸੋਚ ਛੱਡ ਦੇਣ ਨਾਲ ਕਿਉਂ ਨਹੀਂ?","sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Original Gurmukhi corpus — Japji Pauri 13, Ang 3","role":"Primary scripture anchor; exact preserved passage IDs and hashes listed separately"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0003.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Guru Granth Darpan — Ang 3","role":"Consulted interpretive reference; short attributed notes only"}],"status":"draft","unitId":"pauri13","passageIds":["pauri13.line01","pauri13.line02","pauri13.line03","pauri13.line04","pauri13.line05","pauri13.line06"],"angs":[3],"sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri13.line01","ang":3,"sourceLine":6,"sha256":"b5b6448d48770ad74e695ff84fa87f0705fd528688297468c1bda066e1288a44"},{"passageId":"pauri13.line02","ang":3,"sourceLine":7,"sha256":"4634c77633d0a66875f23178372d5d83788277bc71d898f2d866a2bc246dc826"},{"passageId":"pauri13.line03","ang":3,"sourceLine":7,"sha256":"e9379a8f7191dd34f58a0503eb1a9b0c1c95f7031052cf9bb3179a67bf7d6ad8"},{"passageId":"pauri13.line04","ang":3,"sourceLine":7,"sha256":"306dc324ecc05ed3c5e72cf6ff999d3e293183fdde6f0e744d452b0eafb319c4"},{"passageId":"pauri13.line05","ang":3,"sourceLine":7,"sha256":"4347c1cccd40cc451316af51f9704e63f6983687b2f83a5e1e217b82aa8fee30"},{"passageId":"pauri13.line06","ang":3,"sourceLine":8,"sha256":"6288abbadb7f243619906ccfa22a76c3d90a40fdfad80109f1177e270e3a13f2"}],"researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","humanReviewed":false,"reviewNeeds":["Qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review of meaning and grammar","Qualified santhiya review of pronunciation notes","Broader comparison of traditional commentaries"],"id":"pauri13"},"pauri14":{"pauri":14,"titleEn":"A settled relationship with dharam","titlePa":"ਧਰਮ ਨਾਲ ਦ੍ਰਿੜ੍ਹ ਸੰਬੰਧ","meaningEn":"Deep acceptance gives steadiness on the path and a living relationship with dharam. The point is a life anchored in the teaching, not immunity from every difficulty.","meaningPa":"ਨਾਮ ਵਿੱਚ ਪਤੀਜਿਆ ਮਨ ਜੀਵਨ ਦੇ ਰਾਹ ਵਿੱਚ ਦ੍ਰਿੜ੍ਹ ਹੁੰਦਾ ਅਤੇ ਧਰਮ ਨਾਲ ਸੱਚਾ ਸੰਬੰਧ ਜੋੜਦਾ ਹੈ। ਇਹ ਹਰ ਮੁਸ਼ਕਲ ਮਿਟ ਜਾਣ ਦਾ ਦਾਅਵਾ ਨਹੀਂ, ਸਿੱਖਿਆ ਵਿੱਚ ਟਿਕੇ ਜੀਵਨ ਦੀ ਗੱਲ ਹੈ।","directSense":"The Pauri speaks of an unobstructed way, departure with honor, the relation to paths, and connection with ਧਰਮ. The recurring refrain again points to Naam rather than to a badge of membership. The unusual wording of the third line deserves grammatical attention; a short modern paraphrase cannot settle every implication.","directSensePa":"ਰਾਹ, ਰੋਕ, ਪਤਿ ਅਤੇ ਧਰਮ ਨਾਲ ਸੰਬੰਧ ਦੀਆਂ ਗੱਲਾਂ ਇਕ ਲੜੀ ਵਿੱਚ ਆਉਂਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ। ਤੀਜੀ ਤੁਕ ਦਾ ਸ਼ਬਦ-ਜੋੜ ਖ਼ਾਸ ਧਿਆਨ ਮੰਗਦਾ ਹੈ; ਇੱਕ ਛੋਟਾ ਅਰਥ ਇਸ ਦੀ ਪੂਰੀ ਟੀਕਾ ਨਹੀਂ।","context":"Awareness in Pauri 13 is followed by direction in Pauri 14. Pauri 15 will extend the result into family and the Guru-disciple relationship, so the sequence is not simply about a private feeling of certainty.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਰਗਿ","note":"On or in the path. The source form carries a relationship, not merely the noun 'path' in isolation."},{"gurmukhi":"ਠਾਕ","note":"An impediment or obstruction."},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਤਿ","note":"Honor or dignity in this context; not automatically wealth, office or popularity."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੇਤੀ ਸਨਬੰਧੁ","note":"Connection with: attend to the relational wording rather than treating dharam only as a category."}],"pronunciation":"The source distinguishes ਮਾਰਗਿ from ਮਗੁ and ਪੰਥੁ. Keep these forms; do not 'correct' the unfamiliar line into ordinary contemporary Punjabi while reciting.","interpretations":"Sahib Singh reads the path-language through a firm relation to dharam, without being diverted by competing routes. Source: Darpan, Ang 3. This draft does not use that reading to insult other communities or claim that sincere people face no obstacles. The full comparison of commentarial explanations remains open.","reflection":"Identify one principle you want to keep when distracted by approval or fear. Write the next small decision in which that principle will matter.","reflectionPa":"ਇੱਕ ਅਸੂਲ ਪਛਾਣੋ ਜੋ ਡਰ ਜਾਂ ਸ਼ੋਭਾ ਦੀ ਖਿੱਚ ਵਿੱਚ ਵੀ ਨਹੀਂ ਛੱਡਣਾ ਚਾਹੁੰਦੇ। ਅਗਲਾ ਛੋਟਾ ਫ਼ੈਸਲਾ ਉਸ ਨਾਲ ਜੋੜੋ।","teachBack":"What is the difference between a steadfast path and a life in which nothing difficult ever happens?","teachBackPa":"ਰਾਹ ਵਿੱਚ ਦ੍ਰਿੜ੍ਹ ਹੋਣ ਅਤੇ ਜੀਵਨ ਵਿੱਚ ਕੋਈ ਔਖ ਨਾ ਆਉਣ ਵਿੱਚ ਕੀ ਫ਼ਰਕ ਹੈ?","sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Original Gurmukhi corpus — Japji Pauri 14, Ang 3","role":"Primary scripture anchor; exact preserved passage IDs and hashes listed separately"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0003.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Guru Granth Darpan — Ang 3","role":"Consulted interpretive reference; short attributed notes only"}],"status":"draft","unitId":"pauri14","passageIds":["pauri14.line01","pauri14.line02","pauri14.line03","pauri14.line04","pauri14.line05","pauri14.line06"],"angs":[3],"sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri14.line01","ang":3,"sourceLine":8,"sha256":"347156e723501140f323602191c1f00be3a286b3cdb4e2658612fff1d34753ed"},{"passageId":"pauri14.line02","ang":3,"sourceLine":8,"sha256":"2b7433e321a804dbad3e3836e053ae9ba83ffda9696f3dbee415d839769dbcf9"},{"passageId":"pauri14.line03","ang":3,"sourceLine":9,"sha256":"bca7d319ef33293ffedb189ddeb5649d9cd164678913156e998355cf11bcea87"},{"passageId":"pauri14.line04","ang":3,"sourceLine":9,"sha256":"3cb56f5434fefab54aa087c4a89d0658a8e5a67bfa51c7c445d3a5081a7eb7c1"},{"passageId":"pauri14.line05","ang":3,"sourceLine":9,"sha256":"4347c1cccd40cc451316af51f9704e63f6983687b2f83a5e1e217b82aa8fee30"},{"passageId":"pauri14.line06","ang":3,"sourceLine":9,"sha256":"4d6c7f225eeba9dd401f7e0879c43297a58e2538edd7d5c40b00dba2e2b7de81"}],"researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","humanReviewed":false,"reviewNeeds":["Qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review of meaning and grammar","Qualified santhiya review of pronunciation notes","Broader comparison of traditional commentaries"],"id":"pauri14"},"pauri15":{"pauri":15,"titleEn":"Liberation has a relational reach","titlePa":"ਮੁਕਤੀ ਦਾ ਸੰਬੰਧ ਹੋਰਨਾਂ ਨਾਲ ਵੀ","meaningEn":"Acceptance opens toward liberation and gives support to family and fellow learners. The Guru's teaching carries a person beyond restless dependence; its benefit is not kept only for oneself.","meaningPa":"ਨਾਮ ਵਿੱਚ ਪਤੀਜਣਾ ਮੁਕਤੀ ਵੱਲ ਰਾਹ ਖੋਲ੍ਹਦਾ ਅਤੇ ਪਰਵਾਰ ਤੇ ਸਿੱਖਾਂ ਲਈ ਵੀ ਸਹਾਰਾ ਬਣਦਾ ਹੈ। ਗੁਰੂ ਦੀ ਸਿੱਖਿਆ ਦਾ ਲਾਭ ਕੇਵਲ ਆਪਣੇ ਤੱਕ ਸੀਮਤ ਨਹੀਂ ਰਹਿੰਦਾ।","directSense":"The final Pauri of this group moves through a doorway, a family receiving support, and the image of crossing while others are helped across. Wandering in supplication is contrasted with this settled support. The refrain completes the four Pauris of acceptance. The text names relationship, so a purely solitary reading would miss part of its movement.","directSensePa":"ਮੋਖ ਦੇ ਦੁਆਰ ਤੋਂ ਗੱਲ ਪਰਵਾਰ ਅਤੇ ਗੁਰੂ-ਸਿੱਖ ਦੇ ਸੰਬੰਧ ਵੱਲ ਵਧਦੀ ਹੈ। ਆਪ ਤਰਨਾ ਅਤੇ ਹੋਰਨਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਤਾਰਨਾ ਇਕੱਠੇ ਆਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ। ਮੰਨੈ ਦੀ ਲੜੀ ਹੋਰਨਾਂ ਤੋਂ ਕੱਟੀ ਹੋਈ ਸਾਧਨਾ ਉੱਤੇ ਖ਼ਤਮ ਨਹੀਂ ਹੁੰਦੀ।","context":"Pauris 12–14 explored the limits of description, awakened awareness and steadiness. Pauri 15 makes the relational dimension explicit. Pauri 16 then speaks of the accepted ones before turning back toward the immeasurability of creation.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮੋਖੁ ਦੁਆਰੁ","note":"The doorway of liberation. A doorway is an opening, not an object the learner can buy or own."},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਰਵਾਰੈ","note":"To or for the family; the form directs the reader to those receiving support."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਰੈ / ਤਾਰੇ","note":"Crossing and helping across: watch the change between the related verb forms."},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਿਖ","note":"Begging or dependence in this image. Do not use the verse to shame someone who needs practical help."}],"pronunciation":"Keep ਗੁਰੁ ਸਿਖ as the printed two-word sequence. The vocabulary discussion is not permission to merge or respell it in the original line.","interpretations":"Helping one's family is not interpreted here as automatic inherited salvation or spiritual control over relatives. Our application is that a changed life can become dependable support for others, while each person remains a learner. The precise Guru-disciple grammar merits qualified review; no review has yet been granted.","reflection":"Ask what would make you a steadier presence for one family member: patient attention, honest speech, a kept commitment or practical help. Choose one without demanding a spiritual response from them.","reflectionPa":"ਪਰਵਾਰ ਦੇ ਕਿਸੇ ਜੀਅ ਲਈ ਧੀਰਜ, ਸੱਚਾ ਬੋਲ ਜਾਂ ਨਿਭਾਇਆ ਵਾਅਦਾ ਸਹਾਰਾ ਕਿਵੇਂ ਬਣ ਸਕਦਾ ਹੈ? ਬਿਨਾ ਬਦਲੇ ਦੀ ਮੰਗ ਇੱਕ ਕੰਮ ਕਰੋ।","teachBack":"How does this Pauri connect inward acceptance with the way a person supports other people?","teachBackPa":"ਮਨ ਦੇ ਪਤੀਜਣ ਅਤੇ ਹੋਰਨਾਂ ਲਈ ਸਹਾਰਾ ਬਣਨ ਦਾ ਸੰਬੰਧ ਇਸ ਪਉੜੀ ਵਿੱਚ ਕਿਵੇਂ ਦਿਖਦਾ ਹੈ?","sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Original Gurmukhi corpus — Japji Pauri 15, Ang 3","role":"Primary scripture anchor; exact preserved passage IDs and hashes listed separately"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0003.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Guru Granth Darpan — Ang 3","role":"Consulted interpretive reference; short attributed notes only"}],"status":"draft","unitId":"pauri15","passageIds":["pauri15.line01","pauri15.line02","pauri15.line03","pauri15.line04","pauri15.line05","pauri15.line06"],"angs":[3],"sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri15.line01","ang":3,"sourceLine":10,"sha256":"08a3ab70de4cb928950a938e4bb9e2eedb5216029d96f67e1e0ae8e4e08dcc26"},{"passageId":"pauri15.line02","ang":3,"sourceLine":10,"sha256":"410862edf225a332a3113e49eb66abb94559bf31c278767c1ebb3580f96f284c"},{"passageId":"pauri15.line03","ang":3,"sourceLine":10,"sha256":"66dbbc55d3666159ab15c5c6c4ebc11aa2f8348af2c623f859e63cd3c539a5a1"},{"passageId":"pauri15.line04","ang":3,"sourceLine":10,"sha256":"1474691319c7a05fa7016ea22fe802d8300b243590ad36caf2ed78f1bb8d15bb"},{"passageId":"pauri15.line05","ang":3,"sourceLine":11,"sha256":"4347c1cccd40cc451316af51f9704e63f6983687b2f83a5e1e217b82aa8fee30"},{"passageId":"pauri15.line06","ang":3,"sourceLine":11,"sha256":"05fe58f9a3baec7be74bc80ad34f131afb45a1cfd235dd1cc8434395eb91db0d"}],"researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","humanReviewed":false,"reviewNeeds":["Qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review of meaning and grammar","Qualified santhiya review of pronunciation notes","Broader comparison of traditional commentaries"],"id":"pauri15"},"pauri16":{"pauri":16,"titleEn":"Compassion, order and the limits of counting","titlePa":"ਦਇਆ, ਧਰਮ ਅਤੇ ਗਿਣਤੀ ਦੀ ਸੀਮਾ","meaningEn":"The accepted ones keep their attention on the One, yet no spiritual standing measures the whole creation. Dharam is joined to compassion and contentment; the vast creative unfolding calls forth humility.","meaningPa":"ਪਰਵਾਣ ਜਨਾਂ ਦਾ ਧਿਆਨ ਇਕ ਵਿੱਚ ਹੈ, ਪਰ ਆਤਮਕ ਉੱਚਤਾ ਵੀ ਸਾਰੀ ਰਚਨਾ ਨੂੰ ਮਾਪ ਲੈਣ ਦਾ ਦਾਅਵਾ ਨਹੀਂ। ਧਰਮ ਦਇਆ ਤੇ ਸੰਤੋਖ ਨਾਲ ਜੁੜਦਾ ਹੈ ਅਤੇ ਬੇਅੰਤ ਰਚਨਾ ਅੱਗੇ ਨਿਮਰਤਾ ਉੱਭਰਦੀ ਹੈ।","directSense":"The opening honors the ਪੰਚ and their focused attention. It then insists that the Creator's work has no calculable total. The bull image is recast through dharam, compassion and contentment; questions about its support expose the inadequacy of treating the image as a complete physical explanation. Diverse beings, an unfinishable account, power, beauty and giving follow. A single utterance is associated with a vast unfolding, and the Pauri ends in humble address to the Formless One.","directSensePa":"ਪੰਚ ਜਨਾਂ ਦੀ ਵਡਿਆਈ ਤੋਂ ਬਾਅਦ ਰਚਨਾ ਦੀ ਬੇਅੰਤਤਾ ਆਉਂਦੀ ਹੈ। ਧੌਲ ਦੀ ਤਸਵੀਰ ਦਇਆ, ਧਰਮ ਅਤੇ ਸੰਤੋਖ ਨਾਲ ਜੁੜਦੀ ਹੈ। ਗਿਣਤੀ ਦਾ ਅੰਤ ਨਾ ਲੱਭ ਸਕਣ ਤੋਂ ਅੰਤਿਮ ਨਿਮਰ ਅਰਦਾਸ ਵੱਲ ਗੱਲ ਵਧਦੀ ਹੈ।","context":"This is a hinge in Japji: the listening-and-acceptance sequence gives way to sustained attention to the uncountable. Its last four lines recur in Pauris 17 and 19; Pauri 18 changes one of those lines, a difference worth noticing.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪੰਚ","note":"Sahib Singh relates these accepted ones to the preceding listening-and-acceptance sequence, rather than a headcount. Source: Darpan, Ang 3."},{"gurmukhi":"ਦਇਆ ਕਾ ਪੂਤੁ","note":"Child of compassion: the relational image makes compassion central to the account of dharam."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਵਾਉ","note":"Utterance or command in the creation image. It is not a measured sound frequency supplied by the text."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੂਤੁ","note":"An estimate or measure; the surrounding questions challenge the adequacy of such a measure."}],"pronunciation":"Distinguish ਧੌਲੁ from ਧਵਲੈ as printed rather than forcing both into a single modern spelling. Keep the pauses of the questions visible; no recording-specific breath or timing map has been checked.","interpretations":"This draft reads the bull passage as a challenge to an inadequate explanatory picture and an invitation toward compassion-grounded order. It does not claim that the Pauri states a modern theory of gravity or proves a Big Bang model. The creation utterance is scriptural language; mapping it to contemporary physics would be an additional claim needing its own argument.","reflection":"Consider a rule you help uphold at home or work. Does compassion shape how it is applied, or has the rule become detached from the people it should serve?","reflectionPa":"ਘਰ ਜਾਂ ਕੰਮ ਦਾ ਕੋਈ ਨਿਯਮ ਸੋਚੋ। ਕੀ ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਲਾਗੂ ਕਰਦਿਆਂ ਦਇਆ ਨਾਲ ਸੰਬੰਧ ਬਣਿਆ ਰਹਿੰਦਾ ਹੈ?","teachBack":"Why does a Pauri honoring spiritually accepted people immediately warn that creation cannot be fully counted?","teachBackPa":"ਪਰਵਾਣ ਜਨਾਂ ਦੀ ਵਡਿਆਈ ਤੋਂ ਤੁਰੰਤ ਬਾਅਦ ਰਚਨਾ ਦਾ ਅੰਤ ਨਾ ਪੈਣ ਦੀ ਗੱਲ ਕਿਉਂ ਆਉਂਦੀ ਹੈ?","sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Original Gurmukhi corpus — Japji Pauri 16, Ang 3","role":"Primary scripture anchor; exact preserved passage IDs and hashes listed separately"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0003.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Guru Granth Darpan — Ang 3","role":"Consulted interpretive reference; short attributed notes only"}],"status":"draft","unitId":"pauri16","passageIds":["pauri16.line01","pauri16.line02","pauri16.line03","pauri16.line04","pauri16.line05","pauri16.line06","pauri16.line07","pauri16.line08","pauri16.line09","pauri16.line10","pauri16.line11","pauri16.line12","pauri16.line13","pauri16.line14","pauri16.line15","pauri16.line16","pauri16.line17","pauri16.line18","pauri16.line19","pauri16.line20","pauri16.line21","pauri16.line22","pauri16.line23","pauri16.line24"],"angs":[3],"sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri16.line01","ang":3,"sourceLine":11,"sha256":"4a9f9ab7cfce542d68ced126f198d27686312d76e1b5aec1051dea415815bb65"},{"passageId":"pauri16.line02","ang":3,"sourceLine":12,"sha256":"ac05fbe8ae3aa2fa03cfd6668dc4ff8b1a9979384d340a8d49c8a6f7c2019755"},{"passageId":"pauri16.line03","ang":3,"sourceLine":12,"sha256":"b1f3f81a51a389dd98e5cf5aa31b8eee13b1ed03a6c2c4946ff3ebdf1b015f62"},{"passageId":"pauri16.line04","ang":3,"sourceLine":12,"sha256":"40babb569ce3f35f1a7a5d0a4b02b44901ff8251fd9a2107953b3c53cc2c641e"},{"passageId":"pauri16.line05","ang":3,"sourceLine":12,"sha256":"f215d65c28f6ba81caebf675ed4381133352fec20ae4dada9567fa4a0903ae73"},{"passageId":"pauri16.line06","ang":3,"sourceLine":13,"sha256":"088167300a655b15f6dd7886effa6638d52f7c27a0b694faff1f2a22e057b4ac"},{"passageId":"pauri16.line07","ang":3,"sourceLine":13,"sha256":"c0aa6e25b9b2803ce3af2e7318f1bad62178ea32ab200fdde1a0c885fb38502e"},{"passageId":"pauri16.line08","ang":3,"sourceLine":13,"sha256":"a611dd664293d083fa7a12d2869043df1bd3683281b341952ef357f046f88931"},{"passageId":"pauri16.line09","ang":3,"sourceLine":14,"sha256":"9756a4facd0b12114a9adf34c92865c4dfc50b6359a72974fbdae6bf8559c64f"},{"passageId":"pauri16.line10","ang":3,"sourceLine":14,"sha256":"18a0714d32abc3e026b797c49a27cc2e1ba769c9fd8262d2c0e21d9b0c352fcb"},{"passageId":"pauri16.line11","ang":3,"sourceLine":14,"sha256":"b0e525b21e68fb767c0bb2bb1cd57682fb7ce1135a6f233199b0503504d9b9ca"},{"passageId":"pauri16.line12","ang":3,"sourceLine":14,"sha256":"e3487c77c6977e6c37eb973c031e2e744bb2a99ef4f363c2b6010a8a861d2a20"},{"passageId":"pauri16.line13","ang":3,"sourceLine":15,"sha256":"7c5d69e993cc5c3a4cfcadf3f2016dfa031d63465572c3de4502a81eb2b41a5c"},{"passageId":"pauri16.line14","ang":3,"sourceLine":15,"sha256":"e8bc3733627ca865b48f66d0da493be9c2eace1713a74697f2b2ddabf605675c"},{"passageId":"pauri16.line15","ang":3,"sourceLine":15,"sha256":"b0053e951401beda2b0de4e96a1d4bddfa562e6be90ff53cd0239da1616562a5"},{"passageId":"pauri16.line16","ang":3,"sourceLine":15,"sha256":"4bc5e1c7b3a9da5ac3fb2099a53d315a0040be4cf9ef29485307cc0e3751affa"},{"passageId":"pauri16.line17","ang":3,"sourceLine":16,"sha256":"947ce6663cf7431ee7fd7fae2f3e67ceda8d4f3dffdcf07340bd4a59423cc9cb"},{"passageId":"pauri16.line18","ang":3,"sourceLine":16,"sha256":"6a65010a898827c67992f11a6a71b2da0abeee7af81333c55a0f50b41d408450"},{"passageId":"pauri16.line19","ang":3,"sourceLine":16,"sha256":"5796ea589ea7e9956ebe389d8a21a0c49ac3785c8cec25656cce1fb6064cf978"},{"passageId":"pauri16.line20","ang":3,"sourceLine":17,"sha256":"75728a11a32fe165dab733d1eb4f4d786bf2d0bca532f44e07e55afbb2388f79"},{"passageId":"pauri16.line21","ang":3,"sourceLine":17,"sha256":"0d4dd90694b39855d7666f046e902c5e8d61e4522bcbc6bcac7d5e860cf1754e"},{"passageId":"pauri16.line22","ang":3,"sourceLine":17,"sha256":"b8702c7ad37d05bf96677065aca5f693362c22c0a11d709c5183b201f61467e4"},{"passageId":"pauri16.line23","ang":3,"sourceLine":18,"sha256":"197eab99080bd5abf387096b4dc6dd63ae7f27d5dd1b59d892310f6d2d6bf167"},{"passageId":"pauri16.line24","ang":3,"sourceLine":18,"sha256":"e4650b153dfacad5d836838a7a9fa31a3ea786cd62d3a7e46445a40e2486d208"}],"researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","humanReviewed":false,"reviewNeeds":["Qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review of meaning and grammar","Qualified santhiya review of pronunciation notes","Broader comparison of traditional commentaries"],"id":"pauri16"},"pauri17":{"pauri":17,"titleEn":"Countless ways of seeking","titlePa":"ਖੋਜ ਤੇ ਸਾਧਨਾ ਦੇ ਅਣਗਿਣਤ ਰੂਪ","meaningEn":"Countless people practise devotion, study, generosity, courage and silence. Even this great variety cannot be fully counted; the speaker returns to humility before the Formless One.","meaningPa":"ਅਣਗਿਣਤ ਮਨੁੱਖ ਭਗਤੀ, ਪਾਠ, ਦਾਨ, ਬਹਾਦਰੀ ਅਤੇ ਮੌਨ ਦੇ ਰਾਹਾਂ ਵਿੱਚ ਲੱਗੇ ਹਨ। ਇਹ ਵਿਸ਼ਾਲਤਾ ਵੀ ਗਿਣਤੀ ਵਿੱਚ ਪੂਰੀ ਨਹੀਂ ਆਉਂਦੀ; ਬੋਲਣ ਵਾਲਾ ਨਿਰੰਕਾਰ ਅੱਗੇ ਨਿਮਰ ਹੁੰਦਾ ਹੈ।","directSense":"A repeated ਅਸੰਖ leads through many forms of religious and ethical life: remembrance, love, worship, austerity, texts, yogic detachment, contemplation, giving, courage and silence. The list does not end by ranking its members. Instead, it turns into the same humble address that closed Pauri 16. The act of naming many paths also reveals the speaker's inability to complete the account.","directSensePa":"ਅਸੰਖ ਦੀ ਦੁਹਰਾਈ ਨਾਲ ਵੱਖ-ਵੱਖ ਸਾਧਨਾਵਾਂ ਅਤੇ ਮਨੁੱਖੀ ਗੁਣਾਂ ਦੀ ਲੜੀ ਬਣਦੀ ਹੈ। ਅੰਤ ਵਿੱਚ ਕੋਈ ਦਰਜਾਬੰਦੀ ਨਹੀਂ, ਸਗੋਂ ਆਪਣੀ ਸੀਮਾ ਮੰਨਦੀ ਨਿਮਰਤਾ ਹੈ।","context":"This develops Pauri 16's uncountability through lives usually admired as religious or virtuous. Pauri 18 will place harmful conduct within the same vast human world, preventing an account made only from ideal examples.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਸੰਖ","note":"Beyond counting or countless. It repeats as a refrain within the list, keeping the list open."},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਉ","note":"Love; its early place in the list is worth noticing beside more visible practices."},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੋਨਿ","note":"Those keeping silence. The Pauri can name their practice without making it an automatic guarantee of realization."},{"gurmukhi":"ਲਿਵ","note":"Absorbed or sustained attention; it belongs to a complete phrase rather than a numerical concentration target."}],"pronunciation":"Give each repeated ਅਸੰਖ its place without making speed the goal. Preserve the text's distinct ਭਾਉ and ਭਖ forms; similar-looking words in the list are not interchangeable.","interpretations":"The catalogue is descriptive, so this draft does not infer that every practice listed is either independently sufficient or condemned. It invites the learner to notice a world larger than their own chosen practice. The lesson's emphasis on respectful humility is an inference from the closing address, not a claim of exhaustive religious pluralism research.","reflection":"Notice a sincere practice unlike your own. Before comparing its appearance with yours, ask what disciplined care or generosity might be present in it.","reflectionPa":"ਆਪਣੇ ਤੋਂ ਵੱਖਰੀ ਕੋਈ ਸੱਚੀ ਸਾਧਨਾ ਵੇਖੋ। ਪਹਿਲਾਂ ਤੁਲਨਾ ਕਰਨ ਦੀ ਥਾਂ ਉਸ ਵਿੱਚ ਮੌਜੂਦ ਧਿਆਨ ਜਾਂ ਨੇਕੀ ਨੂੰ ਪਛਾਣੋ।","teachBack":"Why does the catalogue of devoted lives end in humility rather than in a ranking of those lives?","teachBackPa":"ਸਾਧਕਾਂ ਦੀ ਲੰਮੀ ਲੜੀ ਦਾ ਅੰਤ ਦਰਜਾਬੰਦੀ ਦੀ ਥਾਂ ਨਿਮਰਤਾ ਵਿੱਚ ਕਿਉਂ ਹੁੰਦਾ ਹੈ?","sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Original Gurmukhi corpus — Japji Pauri 17, Ang 3–4","role":"Primary scripture anchor; exact preserved passage IDs and hashes listed separately"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0003.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Guru Granth Darpan — Ang 3","role":"Consulted interpretive reference; short attributed notes only"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0004.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Guru Granth Darpan — Ang 4","role":"Consulted interpretive reference; short attributed notes only"}],"status":"draft","unitId":"pauri17","passageIds":["pauri17.line01","pauri17.line02","pauri17.line03","pauri17.line04","pauri17.line05","pauri17.line06","pauri17.line07","pauri17.line08","pauri17.line09","pauri17.line10","pauri17.line11","pauri17.line12"],"angs":[3,4],"sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri17.line01","ang":3,"sourceLine":18,"sha256":"f3911f1e1bcf164aee868a67b1afb4e9f14224cf32005b3260d9212c7631f47f"},{"passageId":"pauri17.line02","ang":3,"sourceLine":19,"sha256":"806806de855bf243b13b2183c6113e8e011887caa593c4c08a11e7bc0fac257b"},{"passageId":"pauri17.line03","ang":3,"sourceLine":19,"sha256":"e435a0b1900a539aab7f8b650aa43692a627e3be936943b8133e897c3f980042"},{"passageId":"pauri17.line04","ang":3,"sourceLine":19,"sha256":"ef7b5a90e63aba73d475e0ae500d3a9fa81d468134eb542b40dc17a7ab6437bb"},{"passageId":"pauri17.line05","ang":4,"sourceLine":1,"sha256":"cb99be92355cba6bacf43353d819ff15538c54c6aef54c26eb9740f3c0d44f15"},{"passageId":"pauri17.line06","ang":4,"sourceLine":1,"sha256":"177489e81e14d6f47c2959755402308ae5187ad219db17126ab7a95a4858cbee"},{"passageId":"pauri17.line07","ang":4,"sourceLine":1,"sha256":"93532a7152fb29a1a0595d1032d8b15453da71d3845d1d6f062672a413b583a4"},{"passageId":"pauri17.line08","ang":4,"sourceLine":2,"sha256":"988b1e87d35747c92e72f7e4113654b44b72927bfd0aedc3f0857d18fdf91ed5"},{"passageId":"pauri17.line09","ang":4,"sourceLine":2,"sha256":"0d4dd90694b39855d7666f046e902c5e8d61e4522bcbc6bcac7d5e860cf1754e"},{"passageId":"pauri17.line10","ang":4,"sourceLine":2,"sha256":"b8702c7ad37d05bf96677065aca5f693362c22c0a11d709c5183b201f61467e4"},{"passageId":"pauri17.line11","ang":4,"sourceLine":2,"sha256":"197eab99080bd5abf387096b4dc6dd63ae7f27d5dd1b59d892310f6d2d6bf167"},{"passageId":"pauri17.line12","ang":4,"sourceLine":3,"sha256":"26d972f6a9e83bee995a6de8f3f019fd2cd360436442d7572d487ee796aadc56"}],"researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","humanReviewed":false,"reviewNeeds":["Qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review of meaning and grammar","Qualified santhiya review of pronunciation notes","Broader comparison of traditional commentaries"],"id":"pauri17"},"pauri18":{"pauri":18,"titleEn":"Name wrongdoing without self-righteousness","titlePa":"ਬੁਰਾਈ ਪਛਾਣੀਏ, ਆਪਣਾ ਅਹੰਕਾਰ ਨਾ ਵਧਾਈਏ","meaningEn":"Deception, exploitation, violence and slander also occur beyond counting. Guru Nanak names the harm while speaking humbly, rather than claiming a place above everyone else.","meaningPa":"ਧੋਖਾ, ਹੱਕ ਮਾਰਨਾ, ਹਿੰਸਾ ਅਤੇ ਨਿੰਦਾ ਵੀ ਅਣਗਿਣਤ ਹਨ। ਗੁਰੂ ਨਾਨਕ ਸਾਹਿਬ ਬੁਰਾਈ ਨੂੰ ਸਪਸ਼ਟ ਕਰਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਵੀ ਨਿਮਰ ਸੁਰ ਰੱਖਦੇ ਹਨ, ਹੋਰਨਾਂ ਤੋਂ ਉੱਚਾ ਹੋਣ ਦਾ ਦਾਅਵਾ ਨਹੀਂ ਕਰਦੇ।","directSense":"The repeated ਅਸੰਖ now accompanies a troubling list: profound ignorance, theft, domination, killing, falsehood and slander. The line about Nanak changes the pattern found in Pauris 16 and 17. After naming harmful acts, the voice still does not become a claim of personal supremacy. The final address to the Formless One remains.","directSensePa":"ਇਥੇ ਅਸੰਖ ਨਾਲ ਮਨੁੱਖ ਦੇ ਹਾਨੀਕਾਰਕ ਕੰਮ ਗਿਣਾਏ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ। ਪਿਛਲੀਆਂ ਪਉੜੀਆਂ ਦੀ ਟੇਕ ਵਿੱਚ ਇੱਕ ਮਹੱਤਵਪੂਰਨ ਬਦਲਾਅ ਨਾਨਕੁ ਨੀਚੁ ਵਾਲੀ ਤੁਕ ਹੈ। ਬੁਰਾਈ ਦੱਸਣ ਨਾਲ ਆਪਣੀ ਵਡਿਆਈ ਨਹੀਂ ਬਣਾਈ ਜਾਂਦੀ।","context":"Read with Pauri 17: the world includes admirable effort and destructive action. Pauri 19 then questions whether even the word 'countless' can contain the whole account. The sequence combines moral seriousness with epistemic humility.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਰਾਮਖੋਰ","note":"The context concerns taking or living on what is not rightfully one's own; do not redirect this term at an ethnic or religious group."},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਮਰ ਕਰਿ ਜਾਹਿ ਜੋਰ","note":"The line joins commands with coercive force, naming abuse of power among the harmful actions."},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਾਨਕੁ ਨੀਚੁ","note":"Sahib Singh reads ਨੀਚੁ as describing Nanak, a humble self-reference. Source: Darpan, Ang 4."}],"pronunciation":"Retain the written ending in ਨਾਨਕੁ and its relation to ਨੀਚੁ. Do not move words between lines to make a different speaker or target.","interpretations":"Humility does not make murder, coercion or theft harmless; the passage names them plainly. Our application distinguishes condemning an action from claiming personal purity. Historically charged vocabulary needs contextual handling: this draft does not use ਮਲੇਛ as a label for a present-day community. A scholar should review its lexical and historical treatment.","reflection":"If you must confront a wrong, state the act and its effects clearly. Ask what you are responsible for repairing, without making the confrontation a performance of your own goodness.","reflectionPa":"ਕਿਸੇ ਗ਼ਲਤੀ ਦਾ ਵਿਰੋਧ ਕਰਨਾ ਹੋਵੇ ਤਾਂ ਕੰਮ ਅਤੇ ਉਸ ਦਾ ਨੁਕਸਾਨ ਸਪਸ਼ਟ ਕਰੋ। ਨਾਲ ਹੀ ਆਪਣੀ ਮੁਰੰਮਤ ਦੀ ਜ਼ਿੰਮੇਵਾਰੀ ਵੀ ਵੇਖੋ।","teachBack":"How can the Pauri condemn harmful action while refusing self-righteousness?","teachBackPa":"ਬੁਰਾਈ ਨੂੰ ਬੁਰਾ ਕਹਿਣਾ ਅਤੇ ਆਪਣੇ ਆਪ ਨੂੰ ਸਭ ਤੋਂ ਚੰਗਾ ਮੰਨਣਾ ਕਿਵੇਂ ਵੱਖਰੇ ਹਨ?","sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Original Gurmukhi corpus — Japji Pauri 18, Ang 4","role":"Primary scripture anchor; exact preserved passage IDs and hashes listed separately"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0004.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Guru Granth Darpan — Ang 4","role":"Consulted interpretive reference; short attributed notes only"}],"status":"draft","unitId":"pauri18","passageIds":["pauri18.line01","pauri18.line02","pauri18.line03","pauri18.line04","pauri18.line05","pauri18.line06","pauri18.line07","pauri18.line08","pauri18.line09","pauri18.line10","pauri18.line11","pauri18.line12"],"angs":[4],"sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri18.line01","ang":4,"sourceLine":3,"sha256":"6151379bae6012d8f701a9942226305289127f8f35b667f1d843ab313a3765df"},{"passageId":"pauri18.line02","ang":4,"sourceLine":3,"sha256":"3c85258f30323efec2366666094c08265a342723c31cda2810d55b388775e8f3"},{"passageId":"pauri18.line03","ang":4,"sourceLine":4,"sha256":"a962ff4e2d5079b3ade88530bca23249e9f460c1c875650bf2c5096ed8e3c033"},{"passageId":"pauri18.line04","ang":4,"sourceLine":4,"sha256":"8071420f471c65ab3d5bf7cb61998fbac6969df91ee8c109cd4632becf154f69"},{"passageId":"pauri18.line05","ang":4,"sourceLine":4,"sha256":"af7b12e44f5b4605ff3abde15f1d218cdd073664074dc63a61c83f173e1cb4c3"},{"passageId":"pauri18.line06","ang":4,"sourceLine":4,"sha256":"8e9edbade8621454469a3b57bde10a1990d513b5cd8b78f819c6e0db1a01a64a"},{"passageId":"pauri18.line07","ang":4,"sourceLine":5,"sha256":"8e6d1d915dd375eb3568d1261b306e3b7f952f090d257d95d3ffe19edca04612"},{"passageId":"pauri18.line08","ang":4,"sourceLine":5,"sha256":"ed411c0afbad42c1040edef85d9abb79149a589593d603f202a7ad0f14553a70"},{"passageId":"pauri18.line09","ang":4,"sourceLine":5,"sha256":"72368906b6f6be5055c42d4394b7ccf3173b38c58ffb1dcf2f4104db936153a9"},{"passageId":"pauri18.line10","ang":4,"sourceLine":6,"sha256":"b8702c7ad37d05bf96677065aca5f693362c22c0a11d709c5183b201f61467e4"},{"passageId":"pauri18.line11","ang":4,"sourceLine":6,"sha256":"197eab99080bd5abf387096b4dc6dd63ae7f27d5dd1b59d892310f6d2d6bf167"},{"passageId":"pauri18.line12","ang":4,"sourceLine":6,"sha256":"79791ef72ed220190e1945404730a41b82838f99a4f66081dfda95db30fbcc87"}],"researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","humanReviewed":false,"reviewNeeds":["Qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review of meaning and grammar","Qualified santhiya review of pronunciation notes","Broader comparison of traditional commentaries"],"id":"pauri18"},"pauri19":{"pauri":19,"titleEn":"Language is necessary and limited","titlePa":"ਅੱਖਰ ਲੋੜੀਂਦੇ ਵੀ, ਸੀਮਤ ਵੀ","meaningEn":"Names, places and worlds exceed our counting, yet letters let us speak, learn and praise. The words point toward the One throughout creation; they do not contain or govern the Creator.","meaningPa":"ਨਾਮ, ਥਾਂ ਅਤੇ ਲੋਕ ਸਾਡੀ ਗਿਣਤੀ ਤੋਂ ਪਰੇ ਹਨ; ਫਿਰ ਵੀ ਅੱਖਰਾਂ ਰਾਹੀਂ ਅਸੀਂ ਬੋਲਦੇ, ਸਿੱਖਦੇ ਅਤੇ ਸਾਲਾਹ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਾਂ। ਅੱਖਰ ਕਰਤਾਰ ਵੱਲ ਸੰਕੇਤ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ, ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਆਪਣੇ ਅੰਦਰ ਬੰਨ੍ਹ ਨਹੀਂ ਲੈਂਦੇ।","directSense":"The Pauri begins with countless names and places, then questions the adequacy of calling them countless. It does not therefore abandon language: letters make naming, praise, knowledge, song and writing possible. The writer of the ordering is not subject to an inscription imposed by someone else. The lines about creation and Naam broaden the scope again, before the familiar humble ending.","directSensePa":"ਪਹਿਲਾਂ ਅਸੰਖ ਕਹਿਣ ਦੀ ਵੀ ਸੀਮਾ ਹੈ, ਫਿਰ ਅਖਰੀ ਦੀ ਦੁਹਰਾਈ ਨਾਲ ਭਾਸ਼ਾ ਦੀ ਲੋੜ ਹੈ। ਸਿਰਜਣਹਾਰ ਨੂੰ ਲਿਖਤ ਦਾ ਬੰਦੀ ਨਹੀਂ ਬਣਾਇਆ ਜਾਂਦਾ। ਅੰਤ ਮੁੜ ਨਿਮਰਤਾ ਨਾਲ ਨਿਰੰਕਾਰ ਨੂੰ ਸੰਬੋਧਨ ਕਰਦਾ ਹੈ।","context":"Pauris 17 and 18 supplied unfinishable lists. Pauri 19 reflects on the words used to make those lists. It also recalls Pauri 12's limits of description, while making explicit that limited language can still serve remembrance and learning.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਾਵ / ਨਾਉ","note":"Sahib Singh distinguishes the names in the opening list from ਨਾਉ in the creation passage. Source: Darpan, Ang 4."},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਖਰੀ","note":"Through letters or words. Its repeated grammatical role organizes the middle of the Pauri."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਨਿ / ਤਿਸੁ","note":"A relative pair: the one who… that one. Keep the clause together when trying to identify its subject."},{"gurmukhi":"ਵਿਣੁ","note":"Without; the final statement about no place excludes an outside beyond the reach being described."}],"pronunciation":"Keep ਨਾਵ, ਨਾਉ and ਨਾਵੈ distinct in the source. Their visual and grammatical differences are part of the study; a reading tool must not normalize them into one familiar word.","interpretations":"The lesson infers that careful language can serve truth without possessing it. That is not a claim that every description is equally accurate. The scope of ਨਾਉ in the creation lines is a theological question; a future comparative lesson should show several commentaries rather than reducing it to a modern slogan about energy or information.","reflection":"Write one belief you hold strongly, then add what your sentence leaves out. This is an exercise in precision and humility, not in giving up the search for truth.","reflectionPa":"ਆਪਣਾ ਇੱਕ ਪੱਕਾ ਵਿਚਾਰ ਲਿਖੋ, ਫਿਰ ਵੇਖੋ ਕਿ ਉਸ ਇੱਕ ਵਾਕ ਤੋਂ ਕੀ ਰਹਿ ਗਿਆ। ਇਹ ਸੱਚ ਦੀ ਭਾਲ ਛੱਡਣਾ ਨਹੀਂ, ਆਪਣੀ ਭਾਸ਼ਾ ਦੀ ਹੱਦ ਪਛਾਣਨਾ ਹੈ।","teachBack":"Why does the Pauri defend the use of letters immediately after exposing the limits of description?","teachBackPa":"ਵਰਣਨ ਦੀ ਸੀਮਾ ਦੱਸਣ ਤੋਂ ਬਾਅਦ ਅੱਖਰਾਂ ਦੀ ਲੋੜ ਕਿਉਂ ਦਰਸਾਈ ਗਈ ਹੈ?","sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Original Gurmukhi corpus — Japji Pauri 19, Ang 4","role":"Primary scripture anchor; exact preserved passage IDs and hashes listed separately"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0004.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Guru Granth Darpan — Ang 4","role":"Consulted interpretive reference; short attributed notes only"}],"status":"draft","unitId":"pauri19","passageIds":["pauri19.line01","pauri19.line02","pauri19.line03","pauri19.line04","pauri19.line05","pauri19.line06","pauri19.line07","pauri19.line08","pauri19.line09","pauri19.line10","pauri19.line11","pauri19.line12","pauri19.line13","pauri19.line14","pauri19.line15"],"angs":[4],"sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri19.line01","ang":4,"sourceLine":7,"sha256":"bab966af5f109922177eb25b19cf94889d8b64927678b045d1170c76ff1e2151"},{"passageId":"pauri19.line02","ang":4,"sourceLine":7,"sha256":"e82f819d9e868e0449cbe7abb36769af097a45b6e2f6a8a4da3816afbf1db7f2"},{"passageId":"pauri19.line03","ang":4,"sourceLine":7,"sha256":"0f86f5b0d35fc9e2e4902c411959f7cfbf1cacbf1d161b884f8bdb062dbafea6"},{"passageId":"pauri19.line04","ang":4,"sourceLine":7,"sha256":"531e51580cf62e86bc14b4126a6c5d0b9495b93a8b1f712487e4f3f9c7785df7"},{"passageId":"pauri19.line05","ang":4,"sourceLine":8,"sha256":"405525dcdb7cf790719a1e01a3d9b9ffdf661d4bee17b208f9e7cf5b9f819fb4"},{"passageId":"pauri19.line06","ang":4,"sourceLine":8,"sha256":"be2f04fe1fe33f1d1815f53b0ed27118c70baa660f6743c9f1474e682f728331"},{"passageId":"pauri19.line07","ang":4,"sourceLine":8,"sha256":"9471bd23acbf9e6e133665bd1b099bf294b252531154b21e68e9858448d3a62b"},{"passageId":"pauri19.line08","ang":4,"sourceLine":9,"sha256":"c1b51ba522762cf3d8b621d1d302609690117979814c427402eae1fc0030ed7a"},{"passageId":"pauri19.line09","ang":4,"sourceLine":9,"sha256":"18a5cd5a2824da2b93da64f05066130fe18a699e8ebb633399a16e6ec0604c8b"},{"passageId":"pauri19.line10","ang":4,"sourceLine":9,"sha256":"8fa0cfc3456e495517374d55ab5953c8ca147e133e59221a8fbaf819c0eb3668"},{"passageId":"pauri19.line11","ang":4,"sourceLine":10,"sha256":"1a5fd214499a548d25fa77dad19b449556ca8815a26eb724fd88c93e5c1f2f60"},{"passageId":"pauri19.line12","ang":4,"sourceLine":10,"sha256":"0d4dd90694b39855d7666f046e902c5e8d61e4522bcbc6bcac7d5e860cf1754e"},{"passageId":"pauri19.line13","ang":4,"sourceLine":10,"sha256":"b8702c7ad37d05bf96677065aca5f693362c22c0a11d709c5183b201f61467e4"},{"passageId":"pauri19.line14","ang":4,"sourceLine":10,"sha256":"197eab99080bd5abf387096b4dc6dd63ae7f27d5dd1b59d892310f6d2d6bf167"},{"passageId":"pauri19.line15","ang":4,"sourceLine":11,"sha256":"bfa900940007424b14970be566b3a82b078be4c34e8699cdba7bc014c3095b22"}],"researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","humanReviewed":false,"reviewNeeds":["Qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review of meaning and grammar","Qualified santhiya review of pronunciation notes","Broader comparison of traditional commentaries"],"id":"pauri19"},"pauri20":{"pauri":20,"titleEn":"Different stains need different cleansing","titlePa":"ਵੱਖਰੀ ਮੈਲ ਦਾ ਵੱਖਰਾ ਧੋਣਾ","meaningEn":"Water and soap wash bodily dirt, but the mind's wrongdoing calls for transformation through loving Naam. Good and bad are not merely labels: our actions bear consequences within Hukam.","meaningPa":"ਸਰੀਰ ਅਤੇ ਕੱਪੜੇ ਦੀ ਮੈਲ ਪਾਣੀ ਤੇ ਸਾਬਣ ਨਾਲ ਧੁਲਦੀ ਹੈ; ਮਤਿ ਦੀ ਮੈਲ ਨਾਮ ਦੇ ਪ੍ਰੇਮ ਨਾਲ ਬਦਲਦੀ ਹੈ। ਪੁੰਨ-ਪਾਪ ਨਿਰੇ ਨਾਮ ਨਹੀਂ; ਆਪਣੇ ਕਰਮਾਂ ਦੇ ਫਲ ਹੁਕਮ ਵਿੱਚ ਭੋਗੇ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ।","directSense":"The Pauri begins with ordinary cleaning: dirt on the body, then soiled clothing. It changes the object to ਮਤਿ, the understanding stained by harmful action, and changes the cleansing to the love or color of Naam. It then refuses to leave virtue and wrongdoing at the level of naming. Doing, recording, sowing and eating form a sequence of consequence, ending again in Hukam.","directSensePa":"ਆਮ ਧੋਣ ਦੀਆਂ ਦੋ ਤਸਵੀਰਾਂ ਤੋਂ ਬਾਅਦ ਗੱਲ ਮਤਿ ਵੱਲ ਮੁੜਦੀ ਹੈ। ਨਾਮ ਦੇ ਰੰਗ ਨਾਲ ਧੋਣ ਦੀ ਗੱਲ ਪਿੱਛੋਂ ਕਰਮ, ਲੇਖਾ, ਬੀਜ ਅਤੇ ਫਲ ਦੀ ਲੜੀ ਹੈ। ਅੰਤ ਹੁਕਮ ਨੂੰ ਇਸ ਜ਼ਿੰਮੇਵਾਰੀ ਨਾਲ ਜੋੜਦਾ ਹੈ।","context":"The great accounts of creation in Pauris 16–19 now return to the learner's conduct. This also revisits Pauri 1's question about becoming truthful: outward cleaning alone cannot perform the work of inward change. Pauri 21 continues with the inward pilgrimage image.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਤਿ","note":"Understanding or judgment: the problem is not dirt on the skin but the orientation from which choices are made."},{"gurmukhi":"ਰੰਗਿ","note":"In the color or love of Naam. The image suggests being imbued, not merely adding a label."},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਖਣੁ","note":"Sahib Singh treats this as a noun concerning naming or saying. Source: Darpan, Ang 4."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬੀਜਿ / ਖਾਹੁ","note":"Sowing and eating: the agricultural sequence makes the relation of action and result tangible."}],"pronunciation":"Observe ਧੋਤੈ, ਧੋਇ and ਧੋਪੈ as distinct printed forms in the cleansing sequence. This lesson does not alter the words to match a modern Punjabi paraphrase.","interpretations":"The moral argument does not justify blaming a suffering person for an illness or an unknown past. That would add a causal claim the passage does not establish about that person. Our application also treats remembrance and repair as compatible: reciting words should not become an excuse to leave a preventable harm unaddressed.","reflection":"Think of one repeated action whose consequences you already recognize. Pair remembrance with a concrete repair or changed habit, rather than stopping at the label 'good' or 'bad'.","reflectionPa":"ਆਪਣੀ ਇੱਕ ਦੁਹਰਾਈ ਗ਼ਲਤੀ ਪਛਾਣੋ ਜਿਸ ਦਾ ਅਸਰ ਤੁਹਾਨੂੰ ਪਤਾ ਹੈ। ਨਾਮ ਦੀ ਯਾਦ ਨਾਲ ਕੋਈ ਅਮਲੀ ਸੁਧਾਰ ਜਾਂ ਮੁਰੰਮਤ ਵੀ ਜੋੜੋ।","teachBack":"How does the sowing image keep the idea of Hukam from becoming an excuse for avoiding responsibility?","teachBackPa":"ਬੀਜਣ ਤੇ ਖਾਣ ਦੀ ਤਸਵੀਰ ਹੁਕਮ ਨੂੰ ਜ਼ਿੰਮੇਵਾਰੀ ਤੋਂ ਬਚਣ ਦਾ ਬਹਾਨਾ ਬਣਨ ਤੋਂ ਕਿਵੇਂ ਰੋਕਦੀ ਹੈ?","sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Original Gurmukhi corpus — Japji Pauri 20, Ang 4","role":"Primary scripture anchor; exact preserved passage IDs and hashes listed separately"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0004.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Guru Granth Darpan — Ang 4","role":"Consulted interpretive reference; short attributed notes only"}],"status":"draft","unitId":"pauri20","passageIds":["pauri20.line01","pauri20.line02","pauri20.line03","pauri20.line04","pauri20.line05","pauri20.line06","pauri20.line07","pauri20.line08","pauri20.line09","pauri20.line10"],"angs":[4],"sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri20.line01","ang":4,"sourceLine":11,"sha256":"3422ed2f5c1ce7a5b296bc341cc6b1ec209d17e2024bf22bd667bf649613ccba"},{"passageId":"pauri20.line02","ang":4,"sourceLine":11,"sha256":"0bbf0fedf95cb4e8bd2bdeb086bd3336707b7dae0f7e90f5f6999ba7c96277b8"},{"passageId":"pauri20.line03","ang":4,"sourceLine":12,"sha256":"056b6ca4f4da329357d1e40d355ff9f2fc1c9b5eeea14b6fd36939dbcc7d1bfb"},{"passageId":"pauri20.line04","ang":4,"sourceLine":12,"sha256":"4a0b27ace932003ded3639e82dc356a7ee44aa0f41bc096c1e0be5a7babee6b2"},{"passageId":"pauri20.line05","ang":4,"sourceLine":12,"sha256":"6972f43522350da943df5fc1db5e5b79bbf6c9bce5277a5dca7aaecffa0aea2d"},{"passageId":"pauri20.line06","ang":4,"sourceLine":13,"sha256":"a3d6055beea1f500e87d66fcb737d73ccfaca399f5b9cbed656ad8ee463b70e7"},{"passageId":"pauri20.line07","ang":4,"sourceLine":13,"sha256":"fb41642dbadb3cd72cacf44e4c53dec046a4f8e7085336f5707670d9e144ced8"},{"passageId":"pauri20.line08","ang":4,"sourceLine":13,"sha256":"9b17d7f3b4b50d1a30ff8611e164acdf6bf29072db671088947771eeac8068ca"},{"passageId":"pauri20.line09","ang":4,"sourceLine":13,"sha256":"e2acf49effffff82c0d7342aeb6e260d058151c7a75786a645ba40782fc6879b"},{"passageId":"pauri20.line10","ang":4,"sourceLine":14,"sha256":"f14cdc47dddf1f91061a9ec49485188b013effbdecc06a21ae654d391e8d79fe"}],"researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","humanReviewed":false,"reviewNeeds":["Qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review of meaning and grammar","Qualified santhiya review of pronunciation notes","Broader comparison of traditional commentaries"],"id":"pauri20"},"pauri21":{"pauri":21,"meaningEn":"Outer religious acts cannot measure spiritual depth. Listening, receiving the teaching and loving within turn us toward the Giver of virtue; the Creator alone knows creation’s beginning.","meaningPa":"ਬਾਹਰਲੇ ਧਾਰਮਿਕ ਕਰਮਾਂ ਨਾਲ ਅੰਦਰਲੀ ਅਵਸਥਾ ਨਹੀਂ ਮਾਪੀ ਜਾ ਸਕਦੀ। ਸੁਣਨ, ਮੰਨਣ ਅਤੇ ਮਨ ਵਿੱਚ ਪਿਆਰ ਵਸਾਉਣ ਨਾਲ ਅੰਦਰਲਾ ਤੀਰਥ ਖੁਲ੍ਹਦਾ ਹੈ; ਰਚਨਾ ਦਾ ਮੁੱਢ ਕਰਤਾਰ ਆਪ ਜਾਣਦਾ ਹੈ।","directSense":"The opening compares pilgrimage, austerity and giving with an inward pilgrimage formed through listening, acceptance and love. The speaker attributes virtue to the Divine rather than presenting devotion as a personal achievement. The question then changes scale: what time, date, season or month marked creation? Religious specialists do not possess an exhaustive answer merely through their status. The final lines return to praise while refusing the claim that one person’s cleverness can contain the Creator. Humility is therefore part of both devotion and inquiry.","context":"Pauri 20 used washing to distinguish outer cleaning from inner transformation. Pauri 21 continues that image, then opens the sustained reflection on divine immeasurability in Pauris 22–26. Read the change of subject as a challenge to spiritual self-certainty, not as an invitation to invent a creation date.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅੰਤਰਗਤਿ","note":"Points inward; notice its place beside ਤੀਰਥਿ, a pilgrimage-place image."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਵਣੁ","note":"Repeated questioning word: which or what? Its recurrence drives the inquiry."},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਪੇ","note":"The emphasis falls on the Creator knowing, not on a human claimant."}],"pronunciation":"Keep ਵੇਲਾ and ਵਖਤੁ visible as different written words within the parallel question. They are not spelling errors to normalize. Final written vowel marks remain part of the source; a qualified teacher should check recitation.","interpretations":"The contrast does not require dismissing generosity or compassion. This draft reads it as rejecting the use of outward acts as a complete measure of spiritual attainment. The creation questions address the limits of claim-making; assigning them a modern cosmological calculation would be a further interpretation, not a translation.","reflection":"When doing a helpful act today, notice whether you also want proof that it makes you spiritually superior. Let the act stand without turning it into a rank.","teachBack":"Why does this Pauri place an inward pilgrimage and questions about creation beside one another?","commentaryNotes":[{"source":"darpan4","note":"Sahib Singh reads the inward pilgrimage through listening, acceptance and love; he treats virtue as divine gift."}],"status":"draft","reviewStatus":"Research-started original draft; qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review pending","scholarReview":false,"pronunciationReview":false,"unitId":"pauri21","passageIds":["pauri21.line01","pauri21.line02","pauri21.line03","pauri21.line04","pauri21.line05","pauri21.line06","pauri21.line07","pauri21.line08","pauri21.line09","pauri21.line10","pauri21.line11","pauri21.line12","pauri21.line13","pauri21.line14","pauri21.line15","pauri21.line16","pauri21.line17","pauri21.line18"],"angs":[4,5],"sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Primary text: frozen Open Granth/Shabad OS import, pauri21; Ang 4, 5","role":"public-domain original Gurbani; source occurrence IDs bound separately","anchor":"pauri21"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0004.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Sri Guru Granth Darpan, Ang 4; Pauri 21","role":"consulted commentary; short attributed notes only","anchor":"Pauri 21"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0005.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Sri Guru Granth Darpan, Ang 5; Pauri 21","role":"consulted commentary; short attributed notes only","anchor":"Pauri 21"}],"researchScope":"Original close-reading draft with selected commentary checkpoints. Not a complete survey of traditions, line-by-line translation, approved pronunciation course, or human scholarly review.","directSensePa":"ਪਉੜੀ ਪਹਿਲਾਂ ਤੀਰਥ, ਤਪ ਅਤੇ ਦਾਨ ਦੇ ਨਾਲ ਸੁਣਨ, ਮੰਨਣ ਤੇ ਮਨ ਵਿੱਚ ਪਿਆਰ ਵਸਾਉਣ ਦੀ ਗੱਲ ਰੱਖਦੀ ਹੈ। ਅੰਦਰਲੇ ਬਦਲਾਅ ਨੂੰ ਆਪਣੀ ਕਮਾਈ ਦਾ ਮਾਣ ਬਣਾਉਣ ਦੀ ਥਾਂ ਗੁਣਾਂ ਦਾ ਮੂਲ ਕਰਤਾਰ ਨੂੰ ਮੰਨਿਆ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹੈ। ਫਿਰ ਰਚਨਾ ਦੇ ਸਮੇਂ ਬਾਰੇ ਸਵਾਲ ਆਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ। ਪੰਡਿਤ, ਕਾਜ਼ੀ ਜਾਂ ਜੋਗੀ ਹੋਣ ਨਾਲ ਹੀ ਪੂਰਾ ਭੇਤ ਹੱਥ ਨਹੀਂ ਆ ਜਾਂਦਾ। ਅੰਤ ਵਿੱਚ ਸਿਫ਼ਤ ਰਹਿੰਦੀ ਹੈ, ਪਰ ਆਪਣੀ ਅਕਲ ਨਾਲ ਸਭ ਕੁਝ ਘੇਰ ਲੈਣ ਦਾ ਦਾਅਵਾ ਨਹੀਂ ਰਹਿੰਦਾ।","reflectionPa":"ਅੱਜ ਕੋਈ ਭਲਾ ਕੰਮ ਕਰਦਿਆਂ ਵੇਖੋ ਕਿ ਨਾਲ ਆਪਣੇ ਉੱਚੇ ਹੋਣ ਦਾ ਸਬੂਤ ਤਾਂ ਨਹੀਂ ਮੰਗ ਰਹੇ। ਕੰਮ ਕਰੋ, ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਦਰਜਾ ਨਾ ਬਣਾਓ।","teachBackPa":"ਇਸ ਪਉੜੀ ਵਿੱਚ ਅੰਦਰਲਾ ਤੀਰਥ ਅਤੇ ਰਚਨਾ ਦੇ ਮੁੱਢ ਬਾਰੇ ਸਵਾਲ ਇਕੱਠੇ ਕਿਉਂ ਆਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ?","researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","editorialCoverage":"unit-level bilingual meaning and structured bilingual study draft; no claim of complete line-by-line exegesis","id":"pauri21","sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri21.line01","ang":4,"sourceLine":14,"sha256":"439cc95c4fd3c75097358c727497d5ec3dda64cae262b36487218b9abaf01745"},{"passageId":"pauri21.line02","ang":4,"sourceLine":14,"sha256":"211b73935650fc097b8fcfb3d42767ff5f462600c0aa5a992cedf2f9c626028d"},{"passageId":"pauri21.line03","ang":4,"sourceLine":15,"sha256":"8580aa94bd297d5b75e52b9fea01ef86cc26627087586632ae43deeb9e40c6e2"},{"passageId":"pauri21.line04","ang":4,"sourceLine":15,"sha256":"936b570760793bbf0e04fa0ddc975520e0c14c7415cd6b04f1d16995cadcd10d"},{"passageId":"pauri21.line05","ang":4,"sourceLine":15,"sha256":"45ab3ceeb7dbb67145eb9debb271cc1a9b2e430442bbaf1e1722842590fbe576"},{"passageId":"pauri21.line06","ang":4,"sourceLine":16,"sha256":"f228200736d557962a095cf78c8bb7a2cd2b8a1ae9f4079e5918adaef8501f21"},{"passageId":"pauri21.line07","ang":4,"sourceLine":16,"sha256":"43de055b24cf37aa5d3c02df11a49454a73d6891dc467733286d8f4fae610fb1"},{"passageId":"pauri21.line08","ang":4,"sourceLine":16,"sha256":"d530d2e432b72e19f91e4826480ddd9a629626240e42556eec6b55f073598828"},{"passageId":"pauri21.line09","ang":4,"sourceLine":16,"sha256":"ee1fb4431966f6535c7d9c1a161392a88b719b480245fbd97865303b3434ac0e"},{"passageId":"pauri21.line10","ang":4,"sourceLine":17,"sha256":"bd8ec8256e43d787294997f460fe140e29ac9d9ac5cd7fb2d28a3e6f7c24017a"},{"passageId":"pauri21.line11","ang":4,"sourceLine":17,"sha256":"dc04d99c5583e0fdfc9da5ff1d3d83583b2b0306446148691ba4897e657f93d1"},{"passageId":"pauri21.line12","ang":4,"sourceLine":18,"sha256":"97e0590a5a1bfb158b50f77c1b6f6255ce4656493a638ec4e2e2608e35d9bc60"},{"passageId":"pauri21.line13","ang":4,"sourceLine":18,"sha256":"d98e782476320fe40ce7c08ad8222d96e4ee431537e6f57582b15ba183aa7475"},{"passageId":"pauri21.line14","ang":4,"sourceLine":19,"sha256":"dc9034dec5dc403ce97e743de13b6d5082fbc9792560d6b8326cd97b651e7b1c"},{"passageId":"pauri21.line15","ang":4,"sourceLine":19,"sha256":"312a3e4a10527818cccbe1a44df0012d67c117c2b35fb10c634d8ffd0541e4f7"},{"passageId":"pauri21.line16","ang":5,"sourceLine":1,"sha256":"2944c6c27b7fc846f50a0d5ae8bd992d9ca54ef6f6f168e7cfa04c0c6cd45dee"},{"passageId":"pauri21.line17","ang":5,"sourceLine":1,"sha256":"f83643560e50feb215682fa09f24b2ca78294205bfe68b2410006afdb90f30a7"},{"passageId":"pauri21.line18","ang":5,"sourceLine":2,"sha256":"bc2d95376efa20000fef34383c07be4a41b79bd39c431bfef6f19915426a52ab"}],"humanReviewed":false},"pauri22":{"pauri":22,"meaningEn":"Creation reaches beyond our completed lists and measures. Many descriptions name its vastness, but the One source alone fully knows itself.","meaningPa":"ਰਚਨਾ ਦਾ ਵਿਸਥਾਰ ਸਾਡੀਆਂ ਗਿਣਤੀਆਂ ਅਤੇ ਹੱਦਾਂ ਤੋਂ ਪਰੇ ਹੈ। ਕਈ ਵਰਣਨ ਉਸ ਦੀ ਵਿਸ਼ਾਲਤਾ ਦੱਸਦੇ ਹਨ, ਪਰ ਆਪਣੇ ਆਪ ਨੂੰ ਪੂਰੀ ਤਰ੍ਹਾਂ ਉਹ ਇੱਕ ਕਰਤਾਰ ਹੀ ਜਾਣਦਾ ਹੈ।","directSense":"The Pauri sets depths beneath depths beside skies beyond skies. It brings inherited scriptural reckonings into the discussion, then asks whether an exhaustive account can be written at all. Numbers do not turn the limitless into something contained by the writer. The conclusion names divine greatness while leaving full self-knowledge with the Divine. The point of the numerical imagery is not a new inventory for the reader to memorize.","context":"Pauri 21 questioned certainty about creation’s starting date. Here the question becomes its extent. Together they loosen two forms of possession: claiming to know the first instant and claiming to have counted the whole.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਤਾਲ","note":"Depths or lower worlds within the passage’s cosmological imagery."},{"gurmukhi":"ਓੜਕ","note":"An end, limit or farthest reach."},{"gurmukhi":"ਲੇਖਾ","note":"An account or reckoning; its repetition turns counting itself into the subject."}],"pronunciation":"Notice the long vowels in ਪਾਤਾਲ and ਆਗਾਸ. Keep the repeated words distinct rather than rushing them into one sound; the repetition carries the image of further reaches. This is reading support, not an approved pronunciation guide.","interpretations":"This draft treats the listed numbers as part of a discussion about limits of reckoning. It does not present them as measured astronomy or claim that the Pauri predicts a specific modern physical theory.","reflection":"Name something you have learned well and one important question you still cannot answer about it. Practise saying both without embarrassment.","teachBack":"What changes when we hear this Pauri as questioning a complete count rather than providing a final count?","commentaryNotes":[],"status":"draft","reviewStatus":"Research-started original draft; qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review pending","scholarReview":false,"pronunciationReview":false,"unitId":"pauri22","passageIds":["pauri22.line01","pauri22.line02","pauri22.line03","pauri22.line04","pauri22.line05"],"angs":[5],"sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Primary text: frozen Open Granth/Shabad OS import, pauri22; Ang 5","role":"public-domain original Gurbani; source occurrence IDs bound separately","anchor":"pauri22"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0005.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Sri Guru Granth Darpan, Ang 5; Pauri 22","role":"consulted commentary; short attributed notes only","anchor":"Pauri 22"}],"researchScope":"Original close-reading draft with selected commentary checkpoints. Not a complete survey of traditions, line-by-line translation, approved pronunciation course, or human scholarly review.","directSensePa":"ਪਾਤਾਲਾਂ ਤੋਂ ਹੇਠਾਂ ਹੋਰ ਪਾਤਾਲ ਅਤੇ ਆਕਾਸ਼ਾਂ ਤੋਂ ਅੱਗੇ ਹੋਰ ਆਕਾਸ਼ ਦੀ ਤਸਵੀਰ ਨਜ਼ਰ ਨੂੰ ਫੈਲਾਉਂਦੀ ਹੈ। ਵੱਖਰੇ ਧਾਰਮਿਕ ਵਰਣਨਾਂ ਦੀਆਂ ਗਿਣਤੀਆਂ ਦਾ ਜ਼ਿਕਰ ਕਰਕੇ ਪਉੜੀ ਪੁੱਛਦੀ ਹੈ ਕਿ ਪੂਰਾ ਲੇਖਾ ਲਿਖਿਆ ਵੀ ਜਾ ਸਕਦਾ ਹੈ ਜਾਂ ਨਹੀਂ। ਕਿਸੇ ਵੱਡੇ ਅੰਕ ਨਾਲ ਬੇਅੰਤ ਨੂੰ ਆਪਣੀ ਪਕੜ ਵਿੱਚ ਨਹੀਂ ਲਿਆ ਜਾ ਸਕਦਾ। ਅੰਤਲੀ ਤੁਕ ਪੂਰੀ ਪਛਾਣ ਉਸ ਇੱਕ ਕੋਲ ਰੱਖਦੀ ਹੈ। ਇਹ ਨਵੀਂ ਖਗੋਲੀ ਗਿਣਤੀ ਦੇਣ ਦਾ ਪਾਠ ਨਹੀਂ ਹੈ।","reflectionPa":"ਜਿਸ ਵਿਸ਼ੇ ਬਾਰੇ ਤੁਸੀਂ ਚੰਗਾ ਜਾਣਦੇ ਹੋ, ਉਸ ਵਿੱਚ ਇੱਕ ਅਜੇ ਅਣਜਾਣ ਗੱਲ ਵੀ ਦੱਸੋ। ਦੋਵੇਂ ਗੱਲਾਂ ਸਹਿਜ ਨਾਲ ਮੰਨੋ।","teachBackPa":"ਜੇ ਪਉੜੀ ਅੰਤਲੀ ਗਿਣਤੀ ਦੇਣ ਦੀ ਥਾਂ ਪੂਰੀ ਗਿਣਤੀ ਕਰਨ ਦੇ ਦਾਅਵੇ ਨੂੰ ਪੁੱਛਦੀ ਹੈ, ਤਾਂ ਸਾਡੀ ਪੜ੍ਹਤ ਕਿਵੇਂ ਬਦਲਦੀ ਹੈ?","researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","editorialCoverage":"unit-level bilingual meaning and structured bilingual study draft; no claim of complete line-by-line exegesis","id":"pauri22","sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri22.line01","ang":5,"sourceLine":2,"sha256":"412a374193422814ac388ece9fb6d75e86d046edcb43745ec9546a3e5d8ca9f6"},{"passageId":"pauri22.line02","ang":5,"sourceLine":3,"sha256":"3e51b452ba1411adf7116c82d3dfb83ef0a2f00bffbd0616bd68594010220097"},{"passageId":"pauri22.line03","ang":5,"sourceLine":3,"sha256":"0667ee2372015179c02635d0a682ec2488bce381f5e5e5a2e9355853264877b5"},{"passageId":"pauri22.line04","ang":5,"sourceLine":4,"sha256":"32dc18b32719a70df1693eb0b1e0c83db0043bff2e4722739be7d95b7f628eff"},{"passageId":"pauri22.line05","ang":5,"sourceLine":4,"sha256":"35ae48aa98eb27421e4aa413a20d8dd75387d0c2089ebc823db536dfd3a45497"}],"humanReviewed":false},"pauri23":{"pauri":23,"meaningEn":"Praising the Divine does not contain its vastness, just as rivers cannot measure the sea they enter. Remembrance gives even the smallest life a dignity that worldly riches cannot supply.","meaningPa":"ਸਿਫ਼ਤ ਕਰਨ ਨਾਲ ਕਰਤਾਰ ਦੀ ਵਿਸ਼ਾਲਤਾ ਦਾ ਅੰਤ ਨਹੀਂ ਮਿਲਦਾ, ਜਿਵੇਂ ਨਦੀਆਂ ਸਮੁੰਦਰ ਵਿੱਚ ਮਿਲ ਕੇ ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਮਾਪ ਨਹੀਂ ਲੈਂਦੀਆਂ। ਰੱਬ ਦੀ ਯਾਦ ਅੱਗੇ ਵੱਡੇ ਧਨ ਤੇ ਰਾਜ ਦਾ ਮਾਣ ਵੀ ਛੋਟਾ ਪੈਂਦਾ ਹੈ।","directSense":"The river-and-sea image keeps praise from becoming a claim to mastery. Entering the sea does not mean possessing its measure. The second image reverses ordinary social ranking: immense rulers and wealth are set beside an ant, and remembrance becomes the decisive condition. The tiny creature is a devotional comparison, not a biological claim about an insect’s religious beliefs. The Pauri asks what actually makes life weighty.","context":"After the counting problem of Pauri 22, this Pauri answers a possible objection: if praise cannot measure the Divine, does it have any value? Its images direct attention toward relationship and remembrance rather than ownership of knowledge.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਾਲਾਹਿ","note":"Praising; read in relation to the One being praised."},{"gurmukhi":"ਵਾਹ","note":"Streams or watercourses alongside ਨਦੀਆ."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੁਲਿ","note":"In comparison with; the comparison overturns an expected hierarchy."}],"pronunciation":"Observe the different written endings of ਸਾਲਾਹੀ and ਸਾਲਾਹਿ in the first line. Do not let similar-looking words lose their separate forms. The app does not prescribe final-vowel recitation.","interpretations":"The text’s comparison critiques wealth as a spiritual yardstick. It need not be read as condemning every person who has resources; that would add a universal judgment not made by this image.","reflection":"Give someone attention today without using income, job title or public recognition to decide how much attention they deserve.","teachBack":"How do the sea and ant images challenge two different kinds of pride?","commentaryNotes":[],"status":"draft","reviewStatus":"Research-started original draft; qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review pending","scholarReview":false,"pronunciationReview":false,"unitId":"pauri23","passageIds":["pauri23.line01","pauri23.line02","pauri23.line03","pauri23.line04"],"angs":[5],"sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Primary text: frozen Open Granth/Shabad OS import, pauri23; Ang 5","role":"public-domain original Gurbani; source occurrence IDs bound separately","anchor":"pauri23"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0005.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Sri Guru Granth Darpan, Ang 5; Pauri 23","role":"consulted commentary; short attributed notes only","anchor":"Pauri 23"}],"researchScope":"Original close-reading draft with selected commentary checkpoints. Not a complete survey of traditions, line-by-line translation, approved pronunciation course, or human scholarly review.","directSensePa":"ਨਦੀ ਸਮੁੰਦਰ ਵਿੱਚ ਮਿਲਦੀ ਹੈ, ਪਰ ਇਸ ਨਾਲ ਸਮੁੰਦਰ ਦੀ ਪੂਰੀ ਮਿਣਤੀ ਉਸ ਦੇ ਹੱਥ ਨਹੀਂ ਆ ਜਾਂਦੀ। ਇਸੇ ਤਰ੍ਹਾਂ ਸਿਫ਼ਤ ਸੰਬੰਧ ਬਣਾਉਂਦੀ ਹੈ, ਕਰਤਾਰ ਉੱਤੇ ਕਬਜ਼ਾ ਨਹੀਂ। ਅਗਲੀ ਤਸਵੀਰ ਵਿੱਚ ਵੱਡੇ ਰਾਜ ਅਤੇ ਧਨ ਦੇ ਸਾਹਮਣੇ ਇੱਕ ਕੀੜੀ ਰੱਖੀ ਜਾਂਦੀ ਹੈ। ਯਾਦ ਅਤੇ ਸੰਬੰਧ ਮੁੱਖ ਹੋ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ, ਦੁਨਿਆਵੀ ਆਕਾਰ ਨਹੀਂ। ਕੀੜੀ ਵਾਲੀ ਗੱਲ ਭਗਤੀ ਦੀ ਉਪਮਾ ਹੈ; ਇਸ ਨੂੰ ਕੀੜਿਆਂ ਦੇ ਧਾਰਮਿਕ ਵਿਚਾਰਾਂ ਬਾਰੇ ਵਿਗਿਆਨਕ ਦਾਅਵਾ ਨਹੀਂ ਬਣਾਉਣਾ।","reflectionPa":"ਕਿਸੇ ਨੂੰ ਧਿਆਨ ਦੇਣ ਵੇਲੇ ਉਸ ਦੇ ਅਹੁਦੇ, ਆਮਦਨ ਜਾਂ ਨਾਮਣੇ ਨੂੰ ਮਾਪ ਨਾ ਬਣਾਓ।","teachBackPa":"ਸਮੁੰਦਰ ਅਤੇ ਕੀੜੀ ਦੀਆਂ ਤਸਵੀਰਾਂ ਦੋ ਵੱਖਰੇ ਮਾਣਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਕਿਵੇਂ ਚੁਣੌਤੀ ਦਿੰਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ?","researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","editorialCoverage":"unit-level bilingual meaning and structured bilingual study draft; no claim of complete line-by-line exegesis","id":"pauri23","sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri23.line01","ang":5,"sourceLine":5,"sha256":"f72acded4092768e5a13e281cf1c25aab3f1f7ac97f225d84eed1cd3ac8286fd"},{"passageId":"pauri23.line02","ang":5,"sourceLine":5,"sha256":"37fac9f2fec8e626ca8486f57d8b5f335470a1fe63290b5da2d7f63b42bce619"},{"passageId":"pauri23.line03","ang":5,"sourceLine":6,"sha256":"28910b7dbf5345ef0ef0e2a9b9b648fcac731e10538b8d46cf4b0f0e3cb04077"},{"passageId":"pauri23.line04","ang":5,"sourceLine":6,"sha256":"7dc9d2fd2d70a4d76d0fdb31ec6f4efcf790d4332cdf6b077d561107aa25d2be"}],"humanReviewed":false},"pauri24":{"pauri":24,"meaningEn":"Neither divine qualities, giving nor creation can be brought to a final limit. Only the Divine fully knows its greatness; what we receive comes as grace.","meaningPa":"ਕਰਤਾਰ ਦੇ ਗੁਣਾਂ, ਦਾਤਾਂ ਅਤੇ ਰਚਨਾ ਦਾ ਅੰਤ ਨਹੀਂ ਪਾਇਆ ਜਾ ਸਕਦਾ। ਆਪਣੀ ਵਡਿਆਈ ਉਹ ਆਪ ਜਾਣਦਾ ਹੈ; ਮਿਲੀ ਹੋਈ ਦਾਤ ਨੂੰ ਮਿਹਰ ਸਮਝ ਕੇ ਸਵੀਕਾਰਿਆ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹੈ।","directSense":"The recurring ਅੰਤੁ ਨ gives the Pauri its shape: speaking, making, giving, seeing and hearing fail to close the account. Even the intention behind creation is not at human disposal. Images of height then ask who could stand at an equal vantage point to measure the One. The ending shifts from attempted measurement to receiving a gift. This is a change in posture, from evaluator to recipient.","context":"Pauris 21–23 questioned certainty, exhaustive counting and worldly scale. Pauri 24 gathers those concerns into a sustained refrain. Its close prepares the discussion of giving in Pauri 25.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅੰਤੁ","note":"End or limit, repeatedly denied here."},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਰਾਵਾਰੁ","note":"The far and near bounds; an image of the whole span."},{"gurmukhi":"ਦਾਤਿ","note":"A gift; the last word changes the emphasis from measuring to receiving."}],"pronunciation":"Take time with the recurring ਅੰਤੁ ਨ pattern; it organizes the sense. Preserve ਨਦਰੀ and ਕਰਮੀ as written. No generated audio or timing is offered as a pronunciation model.","interpretations":"Language about height expresses greatness in this reading. Turning it into a physical address above the atmosphere would be an added literalization. Acknowledging limits of description also need not forbid careful learning.","reflection":"Pause over one ordinary support in your life that you did not make alone. Notice the difference between receiving it and claiming sole credit for it.","teachBack":"Why might the Pauri end with a gift after so many lines about limits?","commentaryNotes":[],"status":"draft","reviewStatus":"Research-started original draft; qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review pending","scholarReview":false,"pronunciationReview":false,"unitId":"pauri24","passageIds":["pauri24.line01","pauri24.line02","pauri24.line03","pauri24.line04","pauri24.line05","pauri24.line06","pauri24.line07","pauri24.line08","pauri24.line09","pauri24.line10","pauri24.line11","pauri24.line12","pauri24.line13","pauri24.line14","pauri24.line15","pauri24.line16"],"angs":[5],"sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Primary text: frozen Open Granth/Shabad OS import, pauri24; Ang 5","role":"public-domain original Gurbani; source occurrence IDs bound separately","anchor":"pauri24"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0005.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Sri Guru Granth Darpan, Ang 5; Pauri 24","role":"consulted commentary; short attributed notes only","anchor":"Pauri 24"}],"researchScope":"Original close-reading draft with selected commentary checkpoints. Not a complete survey of traditions, line-by-line translation, approved pronunciation course, or human scholarly review.","directSensePa":"ਵਾਰ-ਵਾਰ ਆਉਂਦਾ ਅੰਤੁ ਨ ਪਉੜੀ ਦੀ ਚਾਲ ਬਣਾਉਂਦਾ ਹੈ। ਕਹਿਣ, ਕਰਨ, ਦੇਣ, ਵੇਖਣ ਅਤੇ ਸੁਣਨ ਨਾਲ ਵੀ ਪੂਰੀ ਹੱਦ ਨਹੀਂ ਬੱਝਦੀ। ਫਿਰ ਉਚਾਈ ਦੀ ਤਸਵੀਰ ਰਾਹੀਂ ਪੁੱਛਿਆ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹੈ ਕਿ ਉਸ ਇੱਕ ਦੇ ਬਰਾਬਰ ਹੋ ਕੇ ਕੌਣ ਮਾਪ ਸਕੇ। ਅੰਤ ਵਿੱਚ ਮਾਪਣ ਦੀ ਕੋਸ਼ਿਸ਼ ਤੋਂ ਦਾਤ ਪ੍ਰਾਪਤ ਕਰਨ ਵੱਲ ਮੋੜ ਆਉਂਦਾ ਹੈ। ਸਿੱਖਣ ਵਾਲਾ ਆਪਣੇ ਆਪ ਨੂੰ ਪੂਰਾ ਫੈਸਲਾ ਕਰਨ ਵਾਲਾ ਮੰਨਣ ਦੀ ਥਾਂ ਪ੍ਰਾਪਤ ਕਰਨ ਵਾਲਾ ਜਾਣਦਾ ਹੈ।","reflectionPa":"ਆਪਣੀ ਜ਼ਿੰਦਗੀ ਦਾ ਕੋਈ ਸਹਾਰਾ ਵੇਖੋ ਜੋ ਤੁਸੀਂ ਇਕੱਲੇ ਨਹੀਂ ਬਣਾਇਆ। ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਲੈਣ ਅਤੇ ਉਸ ਦਾ ਸਾਰਾ ਸਿਹਰਾ ਲੈਣ ਦਾ ਫ਼ਰਕ ਮਹਿਸੂਸ ਕਰੋ।","teachBackPa":"ਹੱਦਾਂ ਬਾਰੇ ਇੰਨੀ ਵਿਚਾਰ ਤੋਂ ਬਾਅਦ ਪਉੜੀ ਦਾਤ ਉੱਤੇ ਕਿਉਂ ਮੁੱਕਦੀ ਹੈ?","researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","editorialCoverage":"unit-level bilingual meaning and structured bilingual study draft; no claim of complete line-by-line exegesis","id":"pauri24","sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri24.line01","ang":5,"sourceLine":6,"sha256":"75405df60e0d05c6d1c8adbed26edd92e9a2293c739e2f27f9c3a313ca92cdfb"},{"passageId":"pauri24.line02","ang":5,"sourceLine":7,"sha256":"79e36d0b0d18021e4dee8b7c2b6266166468452da8c6c10a619cecea1c1b7a91"},{"passageId":"pauri24.line03","ang":5,"sourceLine":7,"sha256":"55ccdbe0bb61bc5a74357deab09fb1179eac598457d6aed450fd44b15b25aa8f"},{"passageId":"pauri24.line04","ang":5,"sourceLine":7,"sha256":"af03defe96556a79a853c550ab481b36732570e46137f0474e8f9ecc8041d747"},{"passageId":"pauri24.line05","ang":5,"sourceLine":8,"sha256":"66b582570e2385ef5d6cae4406e7595f7c19475cccce204489ee2fb012587dbb"},{"passageId":"pauri24.line06","ang":5,"sourceLine":8,"sha256":"b6ced4e66c9b23c322f3e3ac7ac77e4396126af8d2a584412a12b74e78f239a1"},{"passageId":"pauri24.line07","ang":5,"sourceLine":8,"sha256":"5f786462d138ed7bff60d9aa57ae4c53692c4398971ab01124329be5b25125f4"},{"passageId":"pauri24.line08","ang":5,"sourceLine":9,"sha256":"be9e6fdc29962bf0a26b131d3f44d90cf743bc496b2a1f1b6f678359dfc09b7d"},{"passageId":"pauri24.line09","ang":5,"sourceLine":9,"sha256":"e43117884a155fa17412451b60e263cdff2bb11e7d036c96be2d4d9570b98bba"},{"passageId":"pauri24.line10","ang":5,"sourceLine":9,"sha256":"824b61a65414dea8eb3fea3638bf2c4bdac438c413d1276e8499c5f022dc2618"},{"passageId":"pauri24.line11","ang":5,"sourceLine":9,"sha256":"05cb5b945ecbac2bde1556939eb94d2a1c8b52cbbd2186777587d3af5ceb1bd0"},{"passageId":"pauri24.line12","ang":5,"sourceLine":10,"sha256":"55a8cb28da1f07e03409385b5fa822fe3147f7ac0c25f51f4b35b34a490e0efc"},{"passageId":"pauri24.line13","ang":5,"sourceLine":10,"sha256":"34921e8c2425bb7420b7e4057b93172a45a62bcdad6d3cba6f7370c123548add"},{"passageId":"pauri24.line14","ang":5,"sourceLine":10,"sha256":"9094f75298b8bc613b43dae585290884d523192b8107292755fc7963f88d3c6f"},{"passageId":"pauri24.line15","ang":5,"sourceLine":10,"sha256":"438ace05b0ae79e8e72a660b4f09232184a4a11595b77dd5f87495633d4b904b"},{"passageId":"pauri24.line16","ang":5,"sourceLine":11,"sha256":"775e2d197bd841a2411e341bd33544af4a3b082a55c300badcf0025694009119"}],"humanReviewed":false},"pauri25":{"pauri":25,"meaningEn":"The Giver asks for no bargain, yet recipients may forget, consume or suffer. Freedom and the gift of praise come through divine will and generosity, not spiritual entitlement.","meaningPa":"ਦਾਤਾਰ ਬਿਨਾ ਲਾਲਚ ਦੇਂਦਾ ਹੈ, ਪਰ ਲੈਣ ਵਾਲੇ ਕਈ ਵਾਰ ਭੁੱਲ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ ਜਾਂ ਦੁੱਖ ਵਿੱਚ ਘਿਰ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ। ਛੁਟਕਾਰਾ ਅਤੇ ਸਿਫ਼ਤ ਦੀ ਦਾਤ ਰਜ਼ਾ ਤੇ ਮਿਹਰ ਨਾਲ ਮਿਲਦੇ ਹਨ, ਆਪਣੇ ਹੱਕ ਦੇ ਦਾਅਵੇ ਨਾਲ ਨਹੀਂ।","directSense":"The Pauri contrasts an uncalculating Giver with varied recipients: powerful petitioners, people consumed by harmful habits, those who deny what they receive, and those enduring hunger and pain. Its difficult statement that these too are gifts must be heard within this devotional address, not used to pronounce another person’s suffering good. Release is placed within ਭਾਣਾ, and the closing identifies praise itself as a gift greater than royal status.","context":"Pauri 24 ended with grace and gift; this Pauri examines receiving. It brings the cosmic discussion close to human gratitude, appetite, vulnerability and freedom. The regal ending recalls Pauri 23’s challenge to wealth as the measure of worth.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਮਾਇ","note":"Greedy expectation or self-interested demand, denied of the Giver."},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੁਕਰੁ","note":"Denial or disowning, here after receiving."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬੰਦਿ ਖਲਾਸੀ","note":"Release from confinement or bondage; consider the spiritual setting."}],"pronunciation":"ਭਾਣੈ and ਬਖਸੇ are different words carrying different roles in the passage. Avoid substituting everyday spellings into the scripture. The precise recited realization of final vowels remains for human review.","interpretations":"This draft does not explain why any particular person suffers or treat poverty as deserved. Receiving a passage’s first-person devotional language is different from assigning a divine purpose to someone else’s pain. Interpretive discussion of suffering needs special care and qualified review.","reflection":"Pair gratitude with a concrete act that reduces another person’s hardship. Do not use acceptance as a reason to withhold help.","teachBack":"How can someone receive this Pauri as a personal prayer without using it to minimize a neighbour’s suffering?","commentaryNotes":[{"source":"darpan5","note":"Sahib Singh interprets hardship here as capable of turning a person toward living in divine will; this is a theological reading, not an explanation of any individual’s suffering."}],"status":"draft","reviewStatus":"Research-started original draft; qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review pending","scholarReview":false,"pronunciationReview":false,"unitId":"pauri25","passageIds":["pauri25.line01","pauri25.line02","pauri25.line03","pauri25.line04","pauri25.line05","pauri25.line06","pauri25.line07","pauri25.line08","pauri25.line09","pauri25.line10","pauri25.line11","pauri25.line12","pauri25.line13","pauri25.line14","pauri25.line15","pauri25.line16","pauri25.line17"],"angs":[5],"sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Primary text: frozen Open Granth/Shabad OS import, pauri25; Ang 5","role":"public-domain original Gurbani; source occurrence IDs bound separately","anchor":"pauri25"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0005.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Sri Guru Granth Darpan, Ang 5; Pauri 25","role":"consulted commentary; short attributed notes only","anchor":"Pauri 25"}],"researchScope":"Original close-reading draft with selected commentary checkpoints. Not a complete survey of traditions, line-by-line translation, approved pronunciation course, or human scholarly review.","directSensePa":"ਦਾਤਾਰ ਦੇ ਲਾਲਚ-ਰਹਿਤ ਦੇਣ ਦੇ ਸਾਹਮਣੇ ਲੈਣ ਵਾਲਿਆਂ ਦੀਆਂ ਵੱਖਰੀਆਂ ਹਾਲਤਾਂ ਹਨ। ਕੋਈ ਮੰਗਦਾ ਹੈ, ਕੋਈ ਲੈ ਕੇ ਮੁਕਰਦਾ ਹੈ, ਕੋਈ ਵਿਕਾਰਾਂ ਵਿੱਚ ਖਪਦਾ ਹੈ ਅਤੇ ਕੋਈ ਭੁੱਖ ਤੇ ਦੁੱਖ ਸਹਿੰਦਾ ਹੈ। ਇਹਨਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਵੀ ਦਾਤ ਕਹਿਣ ਵਾਲੀ ਔਖੀ ਤੁਕ ਭਗਤੀ ਦੇ ਸੰਬੋਧਨ ਵਿੱਚ ਆਉਂਦੀ ਹੈ। ਇਸ ਨੂੰ ਕਿਸੇ ਹੋਰ ਦਾ ਦੁੱਖ ਚੰਗਾ ਸਾਬਤ ਕਰਨ ਲਈ ਨਹੀਂ ਵਰਤਣਾ। ਅੰਤ ਵਿੱਚ ਸਿਫ਼ਤ ਦੀ ਦਾਤ ਰਾਜ ਦੇ ਮਾਣ ਤੋਂ ਵੀ ਵੱਡੀ ਠਹਿਰਦੀ ਹੈ।","reflectionPa":"ਸ਼ੁਕਰ ਦੇ ਨਾਲ ਅਜਿਹਾ ਕੰਮ ਕਰੋ ਜੋ ਕਿਸੇ ਹੋਰ ਦੀ ਔਖ ਘਟਾਏ। ਰਜ਼ਾ ਮੰਨਣ ਨੂੰ ਮਦਦ ਨਾ ਕਰਨ ਦਾ ਕਾਰਨ ਨਾ ਬਣਾਓ।","teachBackPa":"ਇਸ ਪਉੜੀ ਨੂੰ ਆਪਣੀ ਅਰਦਾਸ ਵਾਂਗ ਕਿਵੇਂ ਸੁਣੀਏ, ਬਿਨਾ ਕਿਸੇ ਹੋਰ ਦੇ ਦੁੱਖ ਨੂੰ ਛੋਟਾ ਕਰਨ ਦੇ?","researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","editorialCoverage":"unit-level bilingual meaning and structured bilingual study draft; no claim of complete line-by-line exegesis","id":"pauri25","sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri25.line01","ang":5,"sourceLine":11,"sha256":"5ff462d1ddc46131307049fed16ebe1f9d3df090889d4162cdfcddfe6b1a0460"},{"passageId":"pauri25.line02","ang":5,"sourceLine":11,"sha256":"e165b12ca8e184ec0087f08f836a286008e367748000d22627f924b1099106fc"},{"passageId":"pauri25.line03","ang":5,"sourceLine":12,"sha256":"824020717a8b53af623db2a74e7512af4f920dc54c046863dac70978e9ccda6c"},{"passageId":"pauri25.line04","ang":5,"sourceLine":12,"sha256":"0b606b416aacc797bae5908e47512bed0b98bfbc47e8af664bc778549a707f2e"},{"passageId":"pauri25.line05","ang":5,"sourceLine":12,"sha256":"e5b520198d67cf15210e42d1a08d01aa9cd4f88397055fe4c8839e769eb3e76c"},{"passageId":"pauri25.line06","ang":5,"sourceLine":12,"sha256":"fae1d022ef2bc4fcfb830b4e40b6d4ab953f5c25dc3d0927c4372eaf25083aed"},{"passageId":"pauri25.line07","ang":5,"sourceLine":13,"sha256":"04d4c1555d64c5beca8d4b6795046a138a5de135fbc9f7de9ed7289af6282177"},{"passageId":"pauri25.line08","ang":5,"sourceLine":13,"sha256":"a6e46545e372c5e8b2ef58536f6e363d986eae1e283193219aabcfb4a436a600"},{"passageId":"pauri25.line09","ang":5,"sourceLine":13,"sha256":"2a9b625ea67e7be7598255046130aedab84b2fb938190446ac31a9455df3694e"},{"passageId":"pauri25.line10","ang":5,"sourceLine":13,"sha256":"98e6c58f687ae73b9bf9449bb155280c146ed5447bd1d644350b70f0bbfe6f63"},{"passageId":"pauri25.line11","ang":5,"sourceLine":14,"sha256":"317a9034700b2aa7a4854c585a0047b2a869da7f869237fbf7b12b1473e3c816"},{"passageId":"pauri25.line12","ang":5,"sourceLine":14,"sha256":"0739b6c1f199fe80d42a8b9cb72ebdd719024e7dc1df8cf23850873698d0b354"},{"passageId":"pauri25.line13","ang":5,"sourceLine":14,"sha256":"249aaeb2aedcbfa6d4d83073b1c641ae311c29e2b172c57f321726288c4f5b68"},{"passageId":"pauri25.line14","ang":5,"sourceLine":14,"sha256":"ae29d67d34b1a63f77b3306a85786030da643c6acd774e80c0daad73a69f87b9"},{"passageId":"pauri25.line15","ang":5,"sourceLine":15,"sha256":"556e65f2e02412bc78afd729abb05ecd2a74de314acff086f80cc39bde5b749e"},{"passageId":"pauri25.line16","ang":5,"sourceLine":15,"sha256":"4aeff9815cd5f74758a19608a170e191f7af0991dce52e984b98a1cb277f78b8"},{"passageId":"pauri25.line17","ang":5,"sourceLine":15,"sha256":"4329463d5b7cdfed2a0718cf27755720ce4ed63b7ad1a8147bcc8b6fb1f38576"}],"humanReviewed":false},"pauri26":{"pauri":26,"meaningEn":"Divine qualities, justice and grace are beyond price. Many voices describe them, but none can turn that praise into a complete valuation of the One.","meaningPa":"ਕਰਤਾਰ ਦੇ ਗੁਣ, ਨਿਆਂ ਅਤੇ ਬਖ਼ਸ਼ਸ਼ ਕਿਸੇ ਮੁੱਲ ਵਿੱਚ ਨਹੀਂ ਆਉਂਦੇ। ਅਨੇਕਾਂ ਬੋਲਣ ਵਾਲੇ ਉਹਨਾਂ ਦਾ ਵਰਣਨ ਕਰਦੇ ਹਨ, ਪਰ ਕੋਈ ਵੀ ਇੱਕ ਦੀ ਪੂਰੀ ਵਡਿਆਈ ਮਾਪ ਨਹੀਂ ਸਕਦਾ।","directSense":"The language begins in a marketplace: trade, traders, stores and what is carried away. Yet ਅਮੁਲ repeatedly removes price from the transaction. Courtroom and weighing images follow, placing justice and grace beyond the reader’s attempt to assign a value. A long gathering of learned, mythic and devotional speakers cannot complete the description. The final warning concerns confident overstatement, not the mere act of speaking reverently.","context":"Pauri 25 presented praise as the highest gift. Pauri 26 asks what such a gift could cost and dissolves the question. It prepares the chorus of creation in Pauri 27: many can praise without any one speaker owning the whole truth.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਮੁਲ","note":"Beyond price or valuation; the recurrence is the organizing device."},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੁਲੁ","note":"A weighing instrument within the justice imagery."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬੋਲੁਵਿਗਾੜੁ","note":"Boastful or distorted speech; read with the final warning about presumed knowledge."}],"pronunciation":"Do not flatten ਅਮੁਲ and ਅਮੁਲੁ into an edited common spelling. The app preserves both exactly. Pause by sense groups within the long sequence of ਆਖਹਿ clauses.","interpretations":"The commercial language does not make devotion a purchasable service. Likewise, naming revered figures in a shared list need not settle every doctrinal question about those figures. This lesson follows the Pauri’s movement toward the limits of all claimants.","reflection":"When explaining a belief, distinguish what the passage says, what you infer and what you do not know. Avoid making certainty itself a performance.","teachBack":"Why does the Pauri borrow the language of price and weighing if its refrain is that the Divine cannot be priced?","commentaryNotes":[],"status":"draft","reviewStatus":"Research-started original draft; qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review pending","scholarReview":false,"pronunciationReview":false,"unitId":"pauri26","passageIds":["pauri26.line01","pauri26.line02","pauri26.line03","pauri26.line04","pauri26.line05","pauri26.line06","pauri26.line07","pauri26.line08","pauri26.line09","pauri26.line10","pauri26.line11","pauri26.line12","pauri26.line13","pauri26.line14","pauri26.line15","pauri26.line16","pauri26.line17","pauri26.line18","pauri26.line19","pauri26.line20","pauri26.line21","pauri26.line22","pauri26.line23","pauri26.line24","pauri26.line25","pauri26.line26"],"angs":[5,6],"sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Primary text: frozen Open Granth/Shabad OS import, pauri26; Ang 5, 6","role":"public-domain original Gurbani; source occurrence IDs bound separately","anchor":"pauri26"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0005.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Sri Guru Granth Darpan, Ang 5; Pauri 26","role":"consulted commentary; short attributed notes only","anchor":"Pauri 26"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0006.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Sri Guru Granth Darpan, Ang 6; Pauri 26","role":"consulted commentary; short attributed notes only","anchor":"Pauri 26"}],"researchScope":"Original close-reading draft with selected commentary checkpoints. Not a complete survey of traditions, line-by-line translation, approved pronunciation course, or human scholarly review.","directSensePa":"ਪਉੜੀ ਵਪਾਰ, ਵਪਾਰੀ ਅਤੇ ਭੰਡਾਰ ਦੀ ਬੋਲੀ ਨਾਲ ਸ਼ੁਰੂ ਹੁੰਦੀ ਹੈ, ਪਰ ਅਮੁਲ ਦੀ ਦੁਹਰਾਈ ਹਰ ਵਾਰ ਮੁੱਲ ਦੀ ਹੱਦ ਹਟਾ ਦਿੰਦੀ ਹੈ। ਫਿਰ ਦਰਬਾਰ ਅਤੇ ਤੱਕੜ ਦੀਆਂ ਤਸਵੀਰਾਂ ਨਿਆਂ ਤੇ ਬਖ਼ਸ਼ਸ਼ ਵੱਲ ਲੈ ਜਾਂਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ। ਅਨੇਕਾਂ ਗਿਆਨੀ, ਧਾਰਮਿਕ ਰੂਪ ਅਤੇ ਸੇਵਕ ਬੋਲਦੇ ਹਨ, ਪਰ ਵਰਣਨ ਪੂਰਾ ਨਹੀਂ ਹੁੰਦਾ। ਅੰਤ ਦੀ ਚੇਤਾਵਨੀ ਸਿਫ਼ਤ ਬੋਲਣ ਤੋਂ ਨਹੀਂ ਰੋਕਦੀ; ਉਹ ਪੂਰਾ ਅੰਤ ਪਾ ਲੈਣ ਦੇ ਬੜਬੋਲੇ ਦਾਅਵੇ ਨੂੰ ਟੋਕਦੀ ਹੈ।","reflectionPa":"ਕੋਈ ਵਿਚਾਰ ਸਮਝਾਉਂਦੇ ਹੋਏ ਵੱਖਰਾ ਦੱਸੋ: ਬਾਣੀ ਕੀ ਕਹਿੰਦੀ ਹੈ, ਮੇਰੀ ਸਮਝ ਕੀ ਹੈ, ਅਤੇ ਮੈਂ ਅਜੇ ਕੀ ਨਹੀਂ ਜਾਣਦਾ।","teachBackPa":"ਜੇ ਮੁੱਖ ਗੱਲ ਮੁੱਲ ਤੋਂ ਪਰੇ ਹੋਣਾ ਹੈ, ਤਾਂ ਪਉੜੀ ਮੁੱਲ ਤੇ ਤੋਲ ਦੀਆਂ ਤਸਵੀਰਾਂ ਕਿਉਂ ਵਰਤਦੀ ਹੈ?","researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","editorialCoverage":"unit-level bilingual meaning and structured bilingual study draft; no claim of complete line-by-line exegesis","id":"pauri26","sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri26.line01","ang":5,"sourceLine":16,"sha256":"d0ae9eee5c1689fb328263db16ac8e7e357426aa7c672a9313ad127050615797"},{"passageId":"pauri26.line02","ang":5,"sourceLine":16,"sha256":"287a9c38f8536370ea7a2c27acdfaf06e06badfb0b727c3605c696b32b0d008c"},{"passageId":"pauri26.line03","ang":5,"sourceLine":16,"sha256":"ac550fe203cb6c11d986ee04bc5ad78a1a07c6080b4448bbf1fa762a6080bdf2"},{"passageId":"pauri26.line04","ang":5,"sourceLine":17,"sha256":"795a6b2f6a555db2ee77b757d561602c651c5fb0b9d1037338b753fc41f6ba9a"},{"passageId":"pauri26.line05","ang":5,"sourceLine":17,"sha256":"428a14012b631b2f79f23caf33258791083236171263090ac7a69845688fb00d"},{"passageId":"pauri26.line06","ang":5,"sourceLine":17,"sha256":"2ad7e49245a0ec679c7e788904764f853c0367c8d468e3bf24584f1e2e061f32"},{"passageId":"pauri26.line07","ang":5,"sourceLine":17,"sha256":"11218f1dcc8f7f398f63b8e412807dd271c5ce71f330b73c26f731b93c84381f"},{"passageId":"pauri26.line08","ang":5,"sourceLine":18,"sha256":"8eef135117356cb3eb6fab03a03315c2eeb988a576041054d98cd9e3947f565b"},{"passageId":"pauri26.line09","ang":5,"sourceLine":18,"sha256":"13c5247c73d9c26f61885aeb7300190318b61e5388a09cd6198d7eb266ecef95"},{"passageId":"pauri26.line10","ang":5,"sourceLine":18,"sha256":"e6a22aede9a856bc5772f0731320616e8f900765d0b9cef7862a43e6b07086da"},{"passageId":"pauri26.line11","ang":5,"sourceLine":19,"sha256":"f65d8645e5d2eac52a4177f31935890bd85a4264ad889d60d3c5baec7e8f591f"},{"passageId":"pauri26.line12","ang":5,"sourceLine":19,"sha256":"3b8227e8e5c9a26286b8f9840c2c55ac93a2eef3c255f158f9ece5e6dcb0e90b"},{"passageId":"pauri26.line13","ang":5,"sourceLine":19,"sha256":"796f301f3d37f1020ba13b16610dbae0154060cd6a924cffb9a68b85311e62f0"},{"passageId":"pauri26.line14","ang":6,"sourceLine":1,"sha256":"ac7e9893f364a25604e06f72720553d076bd5c1ea21209b61f552d095b6ac1ba"},{"passageId":"pauri26.line15","ang":6,"sourceLine":1,"sha256":"fbef9cbb29948264d2511dbbf15152167130dbabe912137d61684835642287a5"},{"passageId":"pauri26.line16","ang":6,"sourceLine":1,"sha256":"b86184bd5344ae048e2d806899eb339fa7c7d722aba731af6694dd8b9f4e2cb9"},{"passageId":"pauri26.line17","ang":6,"sourceLine":1,"sha256":"b060989b08744218aba438c8741bdd0aa573b4e6d6af21e778544244c159800a"},{"passageId":"pauri26.line18","ang":6,"sourceLine":2,"sha256":"91ed05549ebab741d2e7bcbc42e2a35bd456365d59800ed4f1609b1040065d23"},{"passageId":"pauri26.line19","ang":6,"sourceLine":2,"sha256":"f90798ffcc2894cf8bcdc7c34a849533859a46a318bb073fa05379d2df47e21f"},{"passageId":"pauri26.line20","ang":6,"sourceLine":2,"sha256":"d945aa461733f86186d1392027bda70027496d11fd0a59abe3e407b4d352ddca"},{"passageId":"pauri26.line21","ang":6,"sourceLine":3,"sha256":"fc931adba566700f2492ae3881fd646f59b0945efec8155a5c44483af084e1ea"},{"passageId":"pauri26.line22","ang":6,"sourceLine":3,"sha256":"6e6571e9f60cd95941c82e2caaa66c44a6e605a87c6a60b116719a863ebaa2c3"},{"passageId":"pauri26.line23","ang":6,"sourceLine":3,"sha256":"1981bbbb0f9bc924c2f381808844c562d6ddd9d46c501508364bdd94bd3a9f20"},{"passageId":"pauri26.line24","ang":6,"sourceLine":3,"sha256":"7f2f7cf911189f1fadbb3f84d42a8a3a80173558ec65b2c8bb1508d83fdf694a"},{"passageId":"pauri26.line25","ang":6,"sourceLine":4,"sha256":"b25d201d9f96ca065964dcbda45caf789f36265adac5ec38da0f23cc59725e7a"},{"passageId":"pauri26.line26","ang":6,"sourceLine":4,"sha256":"c19e585cf9d47570bf390a4f199eb979959b10ff93d699de326750a515eb800f"}],"humanReviewed":false},"pauri27":{"pauri":27,"meaningEn":"All creation becomes a vast chorus before the One who sustains it. The lasting Sovereign creates and cares in freedom; our place is to live within that will.","meaningPa":"ਸਾਰੀ ਰਚਨਾ ਪਾਲਣਹਾਰ ਇੱਕ ਦੀ ਸਿਫ਼ਤ ਦਾ ਵਿਸ਼ਾਲ ਗਾਇਨ ਬਣਦੀ ਹੈ। ਸਦਾ ਕਾਇਮ ਕਰਤਾਰ ਆਪਣੀ ਰਜ਼ਾ ਵਿੱਚ ਰਚਦਾ ਤੇ ਸੰਭਾਲਦਾ ਹੈ; ਜੀਵ ਲਈ ਉਸ ਰਜ਼ਾ ਵਿੱਚ ਜੀਉਣਾ ਬਣਦਾ ਹੈ।","directSense":"The opening asks about the wondrous doorway and dwelling from which all are cared for. The answer unfolds as a chorus: elements, powers, seekers, learned people, beauty, courage and worlds. The repeated verbs of singing bring very different things into one scene. The closing returns to the enduring Creator, the variety of creation and a will that humans cannot command. Praise culminates in a way of living, not in claiming control over the Singer’s source.","context":"This is Japji Pauri 27, containing ਸੋ ਦਰੁ. A related So Dar composition begins after Japji on Ang 8, under its own heading; it must not be accidentally appended to this reader. Mention of many raags within this Pauri does not give Japji a prescribed raag.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸਮਾਲੇ","note":"Cares for or sustains; the opening question concerns care of all."},{"gurmukhi":"ਗਾਵਹਿ","note":"They sing; repeated across the many participants."},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਜਾਈ","note":"Within the will; the last line brings the vast chorus back to lived orientation."}],"pronunciation":"The many ਗਾਵਹਿ/ਗਾਵਨਿ openings offer natural visual landmarks. Keep the words and their written endings intact. The silent guide provides pacing only and cannot demonstrate the melodic or recited delivery.","interpretations":"For non-speaking elements, singing may be read as participation in divine order. That is an interpretive explanation of the image. It is not a claim that wind and water produce human words or that a particular musical scale is mandatory here.","reflection":"Listen to the sounds around you for a moment, then consider what it would mean to add a truthful action to the world’s chorus.","teachBack":"How does the repeated “singing” connect ordinary elements with revered beings without giving any of them ultimate authority?","commentaryNotes":[{"source":"darpan6","note":"Sahib Singh explains the elements’ praise as their functioning within divine will."}],"status":"draft","reviewStatus":"Research-started original draft; qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review pending","scholarReview":false,"pronunciationReview":false,"unitId":"pauri27","passageIds":["pauri27.line01","pauri27.line02","pauri27.line03","pauri27.line04","pauri27.line05","pauri27.line06","pauri27.line07","pauri27.line08","pauri27.line09","pauri27.line10","pauri27.line11","pauri27.line12","pauri27.line13","pauri27.line14","pauri27.line15","pauri27.line16","pauri27.line17","pauri27.line18","pauri27.line19","pauri27.line20","pauri27.line21","pauri27.line22"],"angs":[6],"sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Primary text: frozen Open Granth/Shabad OS import, pauri27; Ang 6","role":"public-domain original Gurbani; source occurrence IDs bound separately","anchor":"pauri27"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0006.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Sri Guru Granth Darpan, Ang 6; Pauri 27","role":"consulted commentary; short attributed notes only","anchor":"Pauri 27"}],"researchScope":"Original close-reading draft with selected commentary checkpoints. Not a complete survey of traditions, line-by-line translation, approved pronunciation course, or human scholarly review.","directSensePa":"ਸਾਰੇ ਜੀਵਾਂ ਦੀ ਸੰਭਾਲ ਵਾਲੇ ਅਚਰਜ ਦਰ ਬਾਰੇ ਸਵਾਲ ਤੋਂ ਇੱਕ ਵਿਸ਼ਾਲ ਗਾਇਨ ਖੁਲ੍ਹਦਾ ਹੈ। ਤੱਤ, ਸਾਧਕ, ਵਿਦਵਾਨ, ਸੁੰਦਰਤਾ, ਬਲ ਅਤੇ ਜਗਤ ਇਕੱਠੇ ਸਿਫ਼ਤ ਦੀ ਤਸਵੀਰ ਵਿੱਚ ਆਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ। ਗਾਉਣ ਵਾਲੇ ਅਨੇਕ ਹਨ, ਪਰ ਸਦਾ ਕਾਇਮ ਪਾਲਣਹਾਰ ਇੱਕ ਹੈ। ਅੰਤ ਰਚਨਾ ਦੀ ਰੰਗਤ ਤੋਂ ਰਜ਼ਾ ਵਿੱਚ ਜੀਉਣ ਵੱਲ ਲੈ ਆਉਂਦਾ ਹੈ। ਇਹ ਜਪੁਜੀ ਦੀ ਪਉੜੀ 27 ਹੈ; ਅੰਗ 8 ਉੱਤੇ ਜਪੁਜੀ ਤੋਂ ਬਾਅਦ ਸ਼ੁਰੂ ਹੋਣ ਵਾਲੀ ਵੱਖਰੀ ਸੋ ਦਰੁ ਬਾਣੀ ਨਹੀਂ।","reflectionPa":"ਆਲੇ-ਦੁਆਲੇ ਦੀਆਂ ਆਵਾਜ਼ਾਂ ਸੁਣੋ, ਫਿਰ ਸੋਚੋ ਕਿ ਤੁਹਾਡਾ ਇੱਕ ਸੱਚਾ ਕਰਮ ਇਸ ਸਾਂਝੇ ਗਾਇਨ ਵਿੱਚ ਕੀ ਜੋੜ ਸਕਦਾ ਹੈ।","teachBackPa":"ਵਾਰ-ਵਾਰ ਗਾਉਣ ਦੀ ਗੱਲ ਸਧਾਰਨ ਤੱਤਾਂ ਅਤੇ ਮੰਨੇ ਹੋਏ ਧਾਰਮਿਕ ਰੂਪਾਂ ਨੂੰ ਇਕੱਠਾ ਕਿਵੇਂ ਕਰਦੀ ਹੈ?","researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","editorialCoverage":"unit-level bilingual meaning and structured bilingual study draft; no claim of complete line-by-line exegesis","id":"pauri27","sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri27.line01","ang":6,"sourceLine":4,"sha256":"c2e7d3289ba4da0a9b5fd5252908e789c0f99a23b89f7def9551c126b9f1dc77"},{"passageId":"pauri27.line02","ang":6,"sourceLine":5,"sha256":"ebe0d3568905f9807362b08f8f4a0523f23ffc05891511d21798598192a41d31"},{"passageId":"pauri27.line03","ang":6,"sourceLine":5,"sha256":"7eec31fce7d61b2ef65938c929879885836755f304a92c06242fcd948ebc17a3"},{"passageId":"pauri27.line04","ang":6,"sourceLine":6,"sha256":"1a97d657931882e2a56eb027b8a60a2d95e94f5b9a6c69d978138cd40a46bc06"},{"passageId":"pauri27.line05","ang":6,"sourceLine":6,"sha256":"794c3f91cb89155d39ec18dca42f0045cf19bdc3eb7b4f453dab5013558d4718"},{"passageId":"pauri27.line06","ang":6,"sourceLine":7,"sha256":"a0f455d68595813adf4b1f6977974289075ec8650b5f11dad7cc23017e9d21ed"},{"passageId":"pauri27.line07","ang":6,"sourceLine":7,"sha256":"8186a5e0ee80332a9956a3577b51129b2badaeb656299120193060ea587e3928"},{"passageId":"pauri27.line08","ang":6,"sourceLine":8,"sha256":"951067f67f12403fd15b4307a6da9b45114e0d5afd0e6dc5cadc69d4e3bd5803"},{"passageId":"pauri27.line09","ang":6,"sourceLine":8,"sha256":"3075a629ac1f96ec0ae36a658df900218148d798998966018eb3b2f4fc82472f"},{"passageId":"pauri27.line10","ang":6,"sourceLine":9,"sha256":"e1da52ed0ba8ac1e1b04edc2730c751d10dba33e40d99b7e65230a9efef2a92a"},{"passageId":"pauri27.line11","ang":6,"sourceLine":9,"sha256":"943502fce3f214f21fb77a0773365a7607a0dfa10a9c0c9b164ad8482664464b"},{"passageId":"pauri27.line12","ang":6,"sourceLine":10,"sha256":"0a099e7341f10c2bea088fad4461c4d1d2c7ef0817964e71c6181525b4ae6f98"},{"passageId":"pauri27.line13","ang":6,"sourceLine":10,"sha256":"0f4252eb136c68b30ac94a56b0a0a1bbe8b7e4efb9b439589a6ceb0f20c4b71a"},{"passageId":"pauri27.line14","ang":6,"sourceLine":11,"sha256":"1921d3d03a1b33232fc8ceda1e134a02ba2309d6ca1115eba9a9110881f675f2"},{"passageId":"pauri27.line15","ang":6,"sourceLine":11,"sha256":"6b79233e9823a75fffd9b8baa89fed54d28de375d93b2d743efc74e1c1d19bf6"},{"passageId":"pauri27.line16","ang":6,"sourceLine":12,"sha256":"b218b819becce9c131bdf650b779f86e9d7d372443be2d521ddd366665306b95"},{"passageId":"pauri27.line17","ang":6,"sourceLine":13,"sha256":"ebeba4c82e4e3ce3a2feb0882dbbe1f775169f8fad33fb2c9ee57df3f39178ae"},{"passageId":"pauri27.line18","ang":6,"sourceLine":13,"sha256":"bf6d5b2ca0ea387dc771f43fc3b14cc4016d5f68ae27cd9e668746971d9ad19a"},{"passageId":"pauri27.line19","ang":6,"sourceLine":14,"sha256":"45594075492e291bcd4597ee55e2f4a56cd3f14754d15f7335f413503aa093a4"},{"passageId":"pauri27.line20","ang":6,"sourceLine":14,"sha256":"9120c5575fa047c8316085efd15905ddfa78e839f3a04e8b1498c0cb68587047"},{"passageId":"pauri27.line21","ang":6,"sourceLine":15,"sha256":"672181bf7ce407076776e93b314b7d763bbd312cc14f3143d7359de918c24273"},{"passageId":"pauri27.line22","ang":6,"sourceLine":15,"sha256":"6e0ee51981ad0cf23dba8802ce97030a1a7b68d5a14e8e99d6f5e2d04a94ace8"}],"humanReviewed":false},"pauri28":{"pauri":28,"meaningEn":"Make contentment, effort, remembrance and trust your spiritual equipment. Regard all as companions; the conquest that matters is of the mind, with reverence for the One.","meaningPa":"ਸੰਤੋਖ, ਉੱਦਮ, ਧਿਆਨ ਅਤੇ ਭਰੋਸੇ ਨੂੰ ਆਪਣੀ ਆਤਮਕ ਰਹਿਤ ਬਣਾਓ। ਸਭ ਨੂੰ ਸੰਗੀ ਸਮਝੋ; ਮਨ ਨੂੰ ਜਿੱਤਣਾ ਹੀ ਅਸਲ ਜਿੱਤ ਹੈ, ਅਤੇ ਨਮਸਕਾਰ ਉਸ ਇੱਕ ਨੂੰ ਹੈ।","directSense":"The Pauri addresses recognizable ascetic equipment—earrings, bowl, bag, ashes, patched garment and staff—through inward qualities. The point is a transformed orientation carried into conduct. The community expands to all, while victory moves from controlling others to overcoming the mind’s domination. The repeated salutation begins a four-Pauri sequence honouring the One who is without beginning and remains unchanged.","context":"After Pauri 27’s universal chorus, Pauris 28–31 reconsider religious appearance, nourishment, divine agency and provision. The same salutation binds them together. Read each reworked object in relation to the whole rather than as an isolated slogan.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਤੋਖੁ","note":"Contentment; paired with the image of earrings."},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਰਤੀਤਿ","note":"Trust or confidence, here made a staff."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਗਲ ਜਮਾਤੀ","note":"All as companions in one company; the phrase widens belonging."}],"pronunciation":"Observe the difference between ਮਨਿ and ਮਨੁ elsewhere in Japji; this line preserves ਮਨਿ. ਪਤੁ is also kept exactly as written. Recognition of these forms is not a ruling that a final matra must be sounded or omitted.","interpretations":"The teaching critiques reliance on external signs alone. It does not grant permission to mock people who wear religious clothing. The inward and social transformation is the focus of this draft.","reflection":"Choose one situation where you normally try to win an argument. Practise first noticing the desire to dominate, while still speaking honestly.","teachBack":"Why are “all as companions” and “conquering the mind” placed next to each other?","commentaryNotes":[{"source":"darpan6","note":"Sahib Singh reads ਸਰਮੁ here as effort and the ascetic objects as metaphors for inward qualities."}],"status":"draft","reviewStatus":"Research-started original draft; qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review pending","scholarReview":false,"pronunciationReview":false,"unitId":"pauri28","passageIds":["pauri28.line01","pauri28.line02","pauri28.line03","pauri28.line04","pauri28.line05"],"angs":[6],"sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Primary text: frozen Open Granth/Shabad OS import, pauri28; Ang 6","role":"public-domain original Gurbani; source occurrence IDs bound separately","anchor":"pauri28"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0006.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Sri Guru Granth Darpan, Ang 6; Pauri 28","role":"consulted commentary; short attributed notes only","anchor":"Pauri 28"}],"researchScope":"Original close-reading draft with selected commentary checkpoints. Not a complete survey of traditions, line-by-line translation, approved pronunciation course, or human scholarly review.","directSensePa":"ਮੁੰਦਰਾਂ, ਖੱਪਰ, ਝੋਲੀ, ਸੁਆਹ, ਖਿੰਥਾ ਅਤੇ ਡੰਡੇ ਦੀਆਂ ਤਸਵੀਰਾਂ ਅੰਦਰਲੇ ਗੁਣਾਂ ਨਾਲ ਜੋੜੀਆਂ ਜਾਂਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ। ਪਾਠ ਦਾ ਕੇਂਦਰ ਜੀਵਨ ਦੀ ਰਹਿਤ ਬਦਲਣਾ ਹੈ। ਸੰਗਤ ਦਾ ਘੇਰਾ ਸਭ ਜੀਵਾਂ ਤੱਕ ਵਧਦਾ ਹੈ ਅਤੇ ਜਿੱਤ ਦਾ ਮਤਲਬ ਦੂਜਿਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਵੱਸ ਕਰਨਾ ਨਹੀਂ, ਮਨ ਦੀ ਹਕੂਮਤ ਨੂੰ ਸਮਝਣਾ ਬਣਦਾ ਹੈ। ਅੰਤਲੀ ਨਮਸਕਾਰ ਅਗਲੀਆਂ ਤਿੰਨ ਪਉੜੀਆਂ ਵਿੱਚ ਵੀ ਮੁੜਦੀ ਹੈ ਅਤੇ ਧਿਆਨ ਉਸੇ ਇੱਕ ਉੱਤੇ ਰੱਖਦੀ ਹੈ।","reflectionPa":"ਜਿੱਥੇ ਆਮ ਤੌਰ ਉੱਤੇ ਬਹਿਸ ਜਿੱਤਣੀ ਚਾਹੁੰਦੇ ਹੋ, ਉੱਥੇ ਪਹਿਲਾਂ ਆਪਣੇ ਹਾਵੀ ਹੋਣ ਦੇ ਚਾਅ ਨੂੰ ਵੇਖੋ; ਸੱਚੀ ਗੱਲ ਫਿਰ ਵੀ ਕਹੋ।","teachBackPa":"ਸਭ ਨੂੰ ਸੰਗੀ ਮੰਨਣਾ ਅਤੇ ਮਨ ਨੂੰ ਜਿੱਤਣਾ ਇਕੱਠੇ ਕਿਉਂ ਰੱਖੇ ਗਏ ਹਨ?","researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","editorialCoverage":"unit-level bilingual meaning and structured bilingual study draft; no claim of complete line-by-line exegesis","id":"pauri28","sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri28.line01","ang":6,"sourceLine":16,"sha256":"2af2f0b34221c07ecabbbcfab0cba7511e765793c75cb5df6b753aa3ef6c93a5"},{"passageId":"pauri28.line02","ang":6,"sourceLine":16,"sha256":"a15f656087fe0ba8d657e8c46803fc46d36ad00a95b5233eafb734c9f383e6bf"},{"passageId":"pauri28.line03","ang":6,"sourceLine":17,"sha256":"fecd2a974beffd3ceb1fcc5634ac75dbc18351a91d505690148ceb5c16390aa2"},{"passageId":"pauri28.line04","ang":6,"sourceLine":17,"sha256":"81215c9a5557ab6280099959f34c4c4a3fcbe38d36a3890a0bed92c86a529fb2"},{"passageId":"pauri28.line05","ang":6,"sourceLine":17,"sha256":"0a0dd7e299e9ddb86f18c13090be1cc4243ab1e0fbc3c2a0b112a2ef014d132a"}],"humanReviewed":false},"pauri29":{"pauri":29,"meaningEn":"Let understanding nourish you and compassion serve it. The One holds all; fascination with extraordinary powers distracts from that relation, while meeting and parting belong within divine order.","meaningPa":"ਗਿਆਨ ਨੂੰ ਆਪਣਾ ਭੋਜਨ ਅਤੇ ਦਇਆ ਨੂੰ ਉਸ ਦੀ ਵਰਤਾਉਣ ਵਾਲੀ ਬਣਾਓ। ਸਭ ਦਾ ਨਾਥ ਇੱਕ ਹੈ; ਕਰਾਮਾਤਾਂ ਦਾ ਚਸਕਾ ਇਸ ਸੰਬੰਧ ਤੋਂ ਭਟਕਾਉਂਦਾ ਹੈ, ਅਤੇ ਮਿਲਣਾ-ਵਿਛੜਨਾ ਰਜ਼ਾ ਅੰਦਰ ਹੈ।","directSense":"The feast image joins understanding with compassion, so nourishment is neither merely information nor an impressive display. The Divine is named as the true ਨਾਥ, while extraordinary attainments are called other tastes. Meeting and separation carry the world’s work forward. The concluding salutation redirects attention from coveted capacities to the One. The draft does not convert references to powers into promises that a reader will acquire them.","context":"This continues Pauri 28’s reinterpretation of ascetic practice. Clothing and equipment have become qualities; now the shared meal and leadership imagery are reoriented. The recurring refrain keeps the object of devotion constant.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭੁਗਤਿ","note":"Food or a meal in the opening image."},{"gurmukhi":"ਭੰਡਾਰਣਿ","note":"The one serving from the store; compassion takes that role."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੰਜੋਗੁ / ਵਿਜੋਗੁ","note":"Meeting and separation, held together rather than treating one as outside order."}],"pronunciation":"ਭੁਗਤਿ and ਭਗਤਿ are distinct written words; do not silently substitute the more familiar one. Preserve ਘਟਿ ਘਟਿ as a deliberate repetition. Oral pronunciation still needs a checked human model.","interpretations":"The Pauri’s criticism of fascination with powers suggests that unusual experiences alone are a poor measure of spiritual maturity. That is this lesson’s application of the text, not a medical or scientific assessment of such experiences.","reflection":"Before sharing knowledge, ask whether the way you share it also nourishes the other person. Let compassion shape tone, timing and usefulness.","teachBack":"What would be missing if the opening offered knowledge as food but left out compassion as the server?","commentaryNotes":[],"status":"draft","reviewStatus":"Research-started original draft; qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review pending","scholarReview":false,"pronunciationReview":false,"unitId":"pauri29","passageIds":["pauri29.line01","pauri29.line02","pauri29.line03","pauri29.line04","pauri29.line05"],"angs":[6,7],"sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Primary text: frozen Open Granth/Shabad OS import, pauri29; Ang 6, 7","role":"public-domain original Gurbani; source occurrence IDs bound separately","anchor":"pauri29"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0006.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Sri Guru Granth Darpan, Ang 6; Pauri 29","role":"consulted commentary; short attributed notes only","anchor":"Pauri 29"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0007.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Sri Guru Granth Darpan, Ang 7; Pauri 29","role":"consulted commentary; short attributed notes only","anchor":"Pauri 29"}],"researchScope":"Original close-reading draft with selected commentary checkpoints. Not a complete survey of traditions, line-by-line translation, approved pronunciation course, or human scholarly review.","directSensePa":"ਭੋਜਨ ਦੀ ਤਸਵੀਰ ਵਿੱਚ ਗਿਆਨ ਦੇ ਨਾਲ ਦਇਆ ਦੀ ਵਰਤਾਈ ਜੁੜੀ ਹੈ। ਇਸ ਲਈ ਪਾਲਣਾ ਸਿਰਫ਼ ਜਾਣਕਾਰੀ ਇਕੱਠੀ ਕਰਨ ਜਾਂ ਪ੍ਰਭਾਵ ਪਾਉਣ ਦਾ ਨਾਮ ਨਹੀਂ। ਇੱਕ ਨੂੰ ਸਭ ਦਾ ਨਾਥ ਕਿਹਾ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹੈ ਅਤੇ ਰਿੱਧੀਆਂ-ਸਿੱਧੀਆਂ ਦਾ ਚਸਕਾ ਹੋਰ ਪਾਸੇ ਲੈ ਜਾਣ ਵਾਲਾ ਸੁਆਦ ਬਣਦਾ ਹੈ। ਮਿਲਣਾ ਤੇ ਵਿਛੜਨਾ ਸੰਸਾਰ ਦੀ ਕਾਰ ਵਿੱਚ ਇਕੱਠੇ ਆਉਂਦੇ ਹਨ। ਅੰਤਲੀ ਨਮਸਕਾਰ ਚਾਹੀਦੀਆਂ ਸ਼ਕਤੀਆਂ ਤੋਂ ਧਿਆਨ ਮੁੜ ਇੱਕ ਵੱਲ ਕਰਦੀ ਹੈ।","reflectionPa":"ਗਿਆਨ ਸਾਂਝਾ ਕਰਨ ਤੋਂ ਪਹਿਲਾਂ ਵੇਖੋ ਕਿ ਤੁਹਾਡਾ ਢੰਗ ਵੀ ਦੂਜੇ ਦੀ ਸਹਾਇਤਾ ਕਰਦਾ ਹੈ ਜਾਂ ਨਹੀਂ। ਦਇਆ ਨੂੰ ਲਹਿਜ਼ਾ ਤੇ ਸਮਾਂ ਚੁਣਨ ਦਿਓ।","teachBackPa":"ਜੇ ਗਿਆਨ ਭੋਜਨ ਹੋਵੇ ਪਰ ਦਇਆ ਵਰਤਾਉਣ ਵਾਲੀ ਨਾ ਹੋਵੇ, ਤਾਂ ਕੀ ਘਾਟ ਰਹਿ ਜਾਂਦੀ ਹੈ?","researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","editorialCoverage":"unit-level bilingual meaning and structured bilingual study draft; no claim of complete line-by-line exegesis","id":"pauri29","sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri29.line01","ang":6,"sourceLine":18,"sha256":"4139ffb91b5c91cafb13663f6d3e17e2ad50401abf40894fb388bdd3c29e5b53"},{"passageId":"pauri29.line02","ang":6,"sourceLine":19,"sha256":"4476b02bba7abbfe1ebccbae432854096d6f9f9451b79b009441b555cf67cd2a"},{"passageId":"pauri29.line03","ang":6,"sourceLine":19,"sha256":"5b706939c39eb74211f935fe22a421e4d12451848a8b10cedb2c1015c567c514"},{"passageId":"pauri29.line04","ang":7,"sourceLine":1,"sha256":"81215c9a5557ab6280099959f34c4c4a3fcbe38d36a3890a0bed92c86a529fb2"},{"passageId":"pauri29.line05","ang":7,"sourceLine":1,"sha256":"a67e410b186e166433e51cc12597f512831039d58ff9a1c3f0457c940eb580fd"}],"humanReviewed":false},"pauri30":{"pauri":30,"meaningEn":"A familiar story assigns creating, providing and judging to three figures; this Pauri directs our reverence beyond them to the One whose will sustains the whole.","meaningPa":"ਪ੍ਰਚਲਿਤ ਕਥਾ ਰਚਣ, ਪਾਲਣ ਅਤੇ ਸੰਘਾਰ ਦੀ ਕਾਰ ਤਿੰਨ ਰੂਪਾਂ ਨਾਲ ਜੋੜਦੀ ਹੈ। ਪਉੜੀ ਸਾਡਾ ਧਿਆਨ ਉਹਨਾਂ ਤੋਂ ਪਰੇ ਉਸ ਇੱਕ ਵੱਲ ਕਰਦੀ ਹੈ ਜਿਸ ਦੀ ਰਜ਼ਾ ਵਿੱਚ ਸਾਰੀ ਕਾਰ ਚੱਲਦੀ ਹੈ।","directSense":"The opening presents a mother and three recognized figures with different functions. The following lines shift the controlling reference to the One: affairs proceed in that will, while the One sees yet is not seen by them. The salutation follows the same pattern as Pauris 28–29. Read the opening story and the subsequent turn together; stopping after the first two lines would miss the Pauri’s direction.","context":"Pauri 29 named the true ਨਾਥ. Pauri 30 now questions treating familiar divine functions as separately ultimate. The four-part salutation continues to identify the same beginningless One.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭੰਡਾਰੀ","note":"Keeper or provider of stores, one of the functions named."},{"gurmukhi":"ਫੁਰਮਾਣੁ","note":"Command or ordinance; the next lines locate ultimate direction."},{"gurmukhi":"ਵਿਡਾਣੁ","note":"Wonder or astonishing mystery at the asymmetry of seeing."}],"pronunciation":"Notice the three ਇਕੁ clauses in the second line. Keep ਤਿਨਿ, ਤਿਸੁ and ਓਹੁ distinct in reading; they do not have identical referents. This lesson avoids replacing the written pronouns with an unreviewed recitation gloss.","interpretations":"This draft follows the reading that the opening invokes a known cosmological story before subordinating its figures to the One. It is not a genealogy independently established as history, nor a reason to caricature another community’s beliefs.","reflection":"Notice when a role, institution or expert becomes “ultimate” in your own thinking. Respect useful functions while remembering their limits.","teachBack":"What do the third and fourth lines do to the picture introduced in the first two?","commentaryNotes":[{"source":"darpan7","note":"Sahib Singh identifies the three figures as Brahma, Vishnu and Shiva, then emphasizes the One’s agency rather than independent divine managers."}],"status":"draft","reviewStatus":"Research-started original draft; qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review pending","scholarReview":false,"pronunciationReview":false,"unitId":"pauri30","passageIds":["pauri30.line01","pauri30.line02","pauri30.line03","pauri30.line04","pauri30.line05","pauri30.line06"],"angs":[7],"sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Primary text: frozen Open Granth/Shabad OS import, pauri30; Ang 7","role":"public-domain original Gurbani; source occurrence IDs bound separately","anchor":"pauri30"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0007.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Sri Guru Granth Darpan, Ang 7; Pauri 30","role":"consulted commentary; short attributed notes only","anchor":"Pauri 30"}],"researchScope":"Original close-reading draft with selected commentary checkpoints. Not a complete survey of traditions, line-by-line translation, approved pronunciation course, or human scholarly review.","directSensePa":"ਸ਼ੁਰੂ ਵਿੱਚ ਇੱਕ ਮਾਈ ਅਤੇ ਤਿੰਨ ਮੰਨੇ ਹੋਏ ਰੂਪਾਂ ਦੀ ਕਥਾ ਹੈ, ਜਿਨ੍ਹਾਂ ਨਾਲ ਵੱਖਰੀਆਂ ਕਾਰਾਂ ਜੁੜਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ। ਅਗਲੀਆਂ ਤੁਕਾਂ ਧਿਆਨ ਉਸ ਇੱਕ ਦੇ ਫੁਰਮਾਣ ਵੱਲ ਮੋੜਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ। ਉਹ ਵੇਖਦਾ ਹੈ, ਪਰ ਉਹਨਾਂ ਦੀ ਨਜ਼ਰ ਵਿੱਚ ਨਹੀਂ ਆਉਂਦਾ। ਇਸ ਲਈ ਪਹਿਲੀਆਂ ਦੋ ਤੁਕਾਂ ਉੱਤੇ ਰੁਕ ਜਾਣ ਨਾਲ ਪਉੜੀ ਦਾ ਮੋੜ ਰਹਿ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹੈ। ਅੰਤਲੀ ਨਮਸਕਾਰ ਵੀ ਉਸੇ ਆਦਿ, ਅਨਾਦਿ ਇੱਕ ਨੂੰ ਹੈ।","reflectionPa":"ਵੇਖੋ ਕਿ ਕੋਈ ਅਹੁਦਾ, ਸੰਸਥਾ ਜਾਂ ਜਾਣਕਾਰ ਤੁਹਾਡੇ ਮਨ ਵਿੱਚ ਅੰਤਲਾ ਅਧਿਕਾਰ ਤਾਂ ਨਹੀਂ ਬਣ ਗਿਆ। ਉਸ ਦੀ ਸਹਾਇਤਾ ਮੰਨੋ, ਨਾਲ ਹੱਦ ਵੀ ਯਾਦ ਰੱਖੋ।","teachBackPa":"ਤੀਜੀ ਅਤੇ ਚੌਥੀ ਤੁਕ ਪਹਿਲੀਆਂ ਦੋ ਤੁਕਾਂ ਦੀ ਤਸਵੀਰ ਨੂੰ ਕਿਵੇਂ ਬਦਲਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ?","researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","editorialCoverage":"unit-level bilingual meaning and structured bilingual study draft; no claim of complete line-by-line exegesis","id":"pauri30","sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri30.line01","ang":7,"sourceLine":2,"sha256":"af6ffb49413293a1571c012562aa45d54f249a91f5be1b414bccb7d3a1696a2e"},{"passageId":"pauri30.line02","ang":7,"sourceLine":2,"sha256":"313eeb46e3b36a0cb2db70c8ef7de6c692b11dc829ae97d5e3b0279fa807cb08"},{"passageId":"pauri30.line03","ang":7,"sourceLine":2,"sha256":"e660e46b7b197257f2eed0b6c109b82d9fbe10bff50dfb1678c7fea6a9139f79"},{"passageId":"pauri30.line04","ang":7,"sourceLine":3,"sha256":"3e4fce59ed01b6ff692f3bdf47b15bfbb5c58ecd84b08716a36c3eefff1104ff"},{"passageId":"pauri30.line05","ang":7,"sourceLine":3,"sha256":"81215c9a5557ab6280099959f34c4c4a3fcbe38d36a3890a0bed92c86a529fb2"},{"passageId":"pauri30.line06","ang":7,"sourceLine":4,"sha256":"2588b2f6d29dac9bc08ff15716d192de58bba75caa8fcc83c3b5b57ab6d48cee"}],"humanReviewed":false},"pauri31":{"pauri":31,"meaningEn":"The Creator’s provision reaches every realm, and creation is continually held in care. Reverence returns to the One whose truth endures.","meaningPa":"ਕਰਤਾਰ ਦੇ ਭੰਡਾਰ ਹਰ ਥਾਂ ਹਨ ਅਤੇ ਰਚਨਾ ਉਸ ਦੀ ਸੰਭਾਲ ਵਿੱਚ ਹੈ। ਸਦਾ ਕਾਇਮ ਸੱਚ ਦੀ ਇਹ ਕਾਰ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਨਮਸਕਾਰ ਉਸ ਇੱਕ ਨੂੰ ਕੀਤੀ ਜਾਂਦੀ ਹੈ।","directSense":"The Pauri speaks of provision across every realm, of what has been placed, and of the Creator making and attending to creation. Its compact statement about truth and action is followed by the refrain heard since Pauri 28. The emphasis is trust in sustaining care. The verse does not offer a budget for human consumption or a promise that social arrangements distribute resources justly.","context":"This completes the linked Pauris 28–31. The path moved from transformed personal equipment to compassionate nourishment, then ultimate agency and universal provision. The return of the same refrain lets a reader hear the unity of that movement.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਲੋਇ ਲੋਇ","note":"Realm by realm or in every realm; repetition extends the scope."},{"gurmukhi":"ਭੰਡਾਰ","note":"Stores or treasuries of provision."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਿਰਜਣਹਾਰੁ","note":"The One who creates; the subject of making and care."}],"pronunciation":"Give the repeated ਲੋਇ its full place in the line instead of collapsing it. Keep ਸਚੇ and ਸਾਚੀ as written; similar roots do not make the forms interchangeable. These are visual reading observations.","interpretations":"Calling divine provision inexhaustible is devotional language. This draft does not infer that land, water or human supplies can be wasted without consequences; that would confuse praise with an empirical resource claim.","reflection":"Identify a resource entrusted to you—food, water, time or attention—and use it carefully enough that others can benefit too.","teachBack":"How can trust in divine provision coexist with responsibility for fair sharing and careful use?","commentaryNotes":[],"status":"draft","reviewStatus":"Research-started original draft; qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review pending","scholarReview":false,"pronunciationReview":false,"unitId":"pauri31","passageIds":["pauri31.line01","pauri31.line02","pauri31.line03","pauri31.line04","pauri31.line05","pauri31.line06"],"angs":[7],"sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Primary text: frozen Open Granth/Shabad OS import, pauri31; Ang 7","role":"public-domain original Gurbani; source occurrence IDs bound separately","anchor":"pauri31"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0007.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Sri Guru Granth Darpan, Ang 7; Pauri 31","role":"consulted commentary; short attributed notes only","anchor":"Pauri 31"}],"researchScope":"Original close-reading draft with selected commentary checkpoints. Not a complete survey of traditions, line-by-line translation, approved pronunciation course, or human scholarly review.","directSensePa":"ਹਰ ਲੋਕ ਵਿੱਚ ਭੰਡਾਰਾਂ ਦੀ ਗੱਲ ਰਚਨਾ ਦੇ ਵੱਡੇ ਘੇਰੇ ਵਿੱਚ ਪਾਲਣਾ ਦਿਖਾਉਂਦੀ ਹੈ। ਸਿਰਜਣਹਾਰ ਰਚਦਾ ਹੈ ਅਤੇ ਸੰਭਾਲਦਾ ਹੈ। ਸੱਚੇ ਦੀ ਸਾਚੀ ਕਾਰ ਕਹਿ ਕੇ ਉਹੀ ਨਮਸਕਾਰ ਮੁੜਦੀ ਹੈ ਜੋ ਪਉੜੀ 28 ਤੋਂ ਚੱਲੀ ਆ ਰਹੀ ਹੈ। ਇੱਥੇ ਆਸਰਾ ਅਤੇ ਭਰੋਸਾ ਮੁੱਖ ਹਨ। ਇਸ ਨੂੰ ਮਨੁੱਖੀ ਵਰਤੋਂ ਲਈ ਬੇਹਿਸਾਬ ਖਪਤ ਦੀ ਛੂਟ ਜਾਂ ਸਮਾਜ ਵਿੱਚ ਸਾਰੇ ਸਾਧਨਾਂ ਦੀ ਨਿਆਂਪੂਰਨ ਵੰਡ ਦਾ ਸਬੂਤ ਨਹੀਂ ਬਣਾਉਣਾ।","reflectionPa":"ਭੋਜਨ, ਪਾਣੀ, ਸਮੇਂ ਜਾਂ ਧਿਆਨ ਵਿੱਚੋਂ ਕੋਈ ਸਾਧਨ ਸੰਭਾਲ ਕੇ ਵਰਤੋ ਤਾਂ ਜੋ ਦੂਜਿਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਵੀ ਲਾਭ ਮਿਲੇ।","teachBackPa":"ਕਰਤਾਰ ਦੀ ਪਾਲਣਾ ਉੱਤੇ ਭਰੋਸਾ ਅਤੇ ਸਾਧਨਾਂ ਦੀ ਨਿਆਂਪੂਰਨ ਵੰਡ ਲਈ ਜ਼ਿੰਮੇਵਾਰੀ ਇਕੱਠੇ ਕਿਵੇਂ ਰਹਿ ਸਕਦੇ ਹਨ?","researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","editorialCoverage":"unit-level bilingual meaning and structured bilingual study draft; no claim of complete line-by-line exegesis","id":"pauri31","sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri31.line01","ang":7,"sourceLine":4,"sha256":"68515b438dc8b4bd88c50b4396716fdf690ee67984e03cd78323fce41b03cb12"},{"passageId":"pauri31.line02","ang":7,"sourceLine":5,"sha256":"09dfa50e864f1b58c504c6a9b3559fc7e2c578fe5abe4d86648540ad862295e0"},{"passageId":"pauri31.line03","ang":7,"sourceLine":5,"sha256":"84ddd1f8a86bd35b1a8198dfd9ee610f7c79e40f4ff18c4a4f4f5394d02c52cb"},{"passageId":"pauri31.line04","ang":7,"sourceLine":5,"sha256":"5ec4ff70aa00c9955f173db50d1b11682ce65d7f88a3928b358fb008ea617bb3"},{"passageId":"pauri31.line05","ang":7,"sourceLine":5,"sha256":"81215c9a5557ab6280099959f34c4c4a3fcbe38d36a3890a0bed92c86a529fb2"},{"passageId":"pauri31.line06","ang":7,"sourceLine":6,"sha256":"51f3c24ffb0ed194f01e92c9ee8feffa871df3552646399a75934c5d5c7fb6de"}],"humanReviewed":false},"pauri32":{"pauri":32,"meaningEn":"Even an imagined multitude of tongues cannot make union a possession earned by counting. Devotion turns toward the One, while the final word is grace and the refusal of boastfulness.","meaningPa":"ਲੱਖਾਂ ਜੀਭਾਂ ਦੀ ਕਲਪਨਾ ਵੀ ਮਿਲਾਪ ਨੂੰ ਗਿਣਤੀ ਨਾਲ ਖਰੀਦਿਆ ਹੋਇਆ ਹੱਕ ਨਹੀਂ ਬਣਾਉਂਦੀ। ਸਿਮਰਨ ਇੱਕ ਵੱਲ ਜੋੜਦਾ ਹੈ, ਪਰ ਅੰਤਲੀ ਗੱਲ ਮਿਹਰ ਹੈ ਅਤੇ ਆਪਣੇ ਮਾਣ ਦਾ ਤਿਆਗ ਹੈ।","directSense":"The opening multiplies tongues and repetitions beyond ordinary capacity. The imagery then changes to steps, ascent and a small creature aspiring toward the sky. The final line sets divine grace beside the emptiness of false boasting. Keeping that ending in view prevents the large numbers from becoming a mechanical target. The Pauri can support wholehearted remembrance while unsettling the claim that my quantity of performance obliges the Divine.","context":"After the repeated salutations of Pauris 28–31, this Pauri asks how one approaches the One. Pauri 33 follows by repeatedly denying self-sufficient power. Reading them together guards against turning practice into proof of superiority.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਲਖੁ ਲਖੁ","note":"An emphatic multiplication, not an app achievement goal."},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਵੜੀਆ","note":"Steps; a new image after the multiplication of tongues."},{"gurmukhi":"ਠੀਸ","note":"An empty boast or self-assertion, challenged in the final line."}],"pronunciation":"ਪਵੜੀਆ here and the modern label ਪਉੜੀ share a stair-related image but are different written forms. Keep ਜੀਭੌ intact. Do not use the visual guide’s token count as a spiritual repetition score.","interpretations":"Two modern readings consulted stress different features. SREC warns against mechanical repetition and self-display; Sikh Dharma International emphasizes the expansive image of loving recitation. Both discuss grace. This draft keeps practice and humility together, without endorsing automatic worldly benefits or claiming a survey of all traditions.","reflection":"If you repeat a passage, pause afterward to ask what it asks of your conduct. Let repetition support attention rather than comparison with another person’s count.","teachBack":"How does the final line change the way you understand the enormous numbers at the beginning?","commentaryNotes":[{"source":"srec","note":"SREC warns against mechanical repetition and self-display."},{"source":"sdi32","note":"Sikh Dharma International emphasizes the expansive image of loving recitation; its distinct lineage is not a consensus authority."}],"status":"draft","reviewStatus":"Research-started original draft; qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review pending","scholarReview":false,"pronunciationReview":false,"unitId":"pauri32","passageIds":["pauri32.line01","pauri32.line02","pauri32.line03","pauri32.line04","pauri32.line05"],"angs":[7],"sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Primary text: frozen Open Granth/Shabad OS import, pauri32; Ang 7","role":"public-domain original Gurbani; source occurrence IDs bound separately","anchor":"pauri32"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0007.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Sri Guru Granth Darpan, Ang 7; Pauri 32","role":"consulted commentary; short attributed notes only","anchor":"Pauri 32"},{"url":"https://srec.gurmat.info/articles/sri-guru-granth-sahib/japji-sahib/","label":"SREC, Japji Sahib; Pauri 32 and associated note","role":"modern interpretive comparison; not independent human approval","anchor":"Pauri 32"},{"url":"https://www.sikhdharma.org/japji-sahib-thirty-second-pauree/","label":"Sikh Dharma International, 32nd Pauree, 1 February 2019","role":"distinct modern lineage perspective; excerpt-based comparison only","anchor":"paragraphs on the multitude of tongues and grace"}],"researchScope":"Original close-reading draft with selected commentary checkpoints. Not a complete survey of traditions, line-by-line translation, approved pronunciation course, or human scholarly review.","directSensePa":"ਇੱਕ ਜੀਭ ਤੋਂ ਲੱਖਾਂ ਜੀਭਾਂ ਅਤੇ ਅਨੇਕ ਦੁਹਰਾਈਆਂ ਦੀ ਕਲਪਨਾ ਆਮ ਸਮਰੱਥਾ ਤੋਂ ਪਰੇ ਲੈ ਜਾਂਦੀ ਹੈ। ਫਿਰ ਪੌੜੀਆਂ, ਚੜ੍ਹਾਈ ਅਤੇ ਆਕਾਸ਼ ਦੀ ਰੀਸ ਕਰਦੇ ਕੀੜੇ ਦੀ ਤਸਵੀਰ ਆਉਂਦੀ ਹੈ। ਅੰਤਲੀ ਤੁਕ ਮਿਹਰ ਨੂੰ ਸਾਹਮਣੇ ਰੱਖਦੀ ਹੈ ਅਤੇ ਕੂੜੇ ਮਾਣ ਨੂੰ ਟੋਕਦੀ ਹੈ। ਇਸ ਲਈ ਵੱਡੀਆਂ ਗਿਣਤੀਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਪੂਰਾ ਕਰਨ ਵਾਲਾ ਅੰਕੜਾ ਨਹੀਂ ਬਣਾਉਣਾ। ਇਹ ਪੜ੍ਹਤ ਸਿਮਰਨ ਦੇ ਪਿਆਰ ਨੂੰ ਰੱਖਦੀ ਹੈ, ਪਰ ਆਪਣੀ ਕੀਤੀ ਗਿਣਤੀ ਨਾਲ ਰੱਬ ਉੱਤੇ ਹੱਕ ਨਹੀਂ ਜਤਾਉਂਦੀ।","reflectionPa":"ਕਿਸੇ ਤੁਕ ਨੂੰ ਦੁਹਰਾਉਣ ਤੋਂ ਬਾਅਦ ਰੁਕ ਕੇ ਪੁੱਛੋ ਕਿ ਉਹ ਤੁਹਾਡੇ ਵਰਤਾਰੇ ਤੋਂ ਕੀ ਮੰਗਦੀ ਹੈ। ਗਿਣਤੀ ਨੂੰ ਮੁਕਾਬਲਾ ਨਾ ਬਣਾਓ।","teachBackPa":"ਅੰਤਲੀ ਤੁਕ ਸ਼ੁਰੂ ਦੀਆਂ ਵੱਡੀਆਂ ਗਿਣਤੀਆਂ ਦੀ ਸਮਝ ਨੂੰ ਕਿਵੇਂ ਬਦਲਦੀ ਹੈ?","researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","editorialCoverage":"unit-level bilingual meaning and structured bilingual study draft; no claim of complete line-by-line exegesis","id":"pauri32","sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri32.line01","ang":7,"sourceLine":6,"sha256":"93522da4e9224a8a35705ec1a5e2873215755d8ca4d13d73e3d60b61e350495a"},{"passageId":"pauri32.line02","ang":7,"sourceLine":7,"sha256":"10241af7775a86c48cd163fba5c9e06fc7b97d208fc8db624f1fda1631716bb6"},{"passageId":"pauri32.line03","ang":7,"sourceLine":7,"sha256":"4b5d01403b7dede028f8379a77c1cfbcf2441af8cfa7f2657fcfd639a14e78eb"},{"passageId":"pauri32.line04","ang":7,"sourceLine":8,"sha256":"f0e40c289ae88a23410927b9ff996249798feb5fbfd9a3c48290d65207d65c7b"},{"passageId":"pauri32.line05","ang":7,"sourceLine":8,"sha256":"dba07edd9914f189ea7dbea0795c01df411b47fd844a52db243b3eb528c99d86"}],"humanReviewed":false},"pauri33":{"pauri":33,"meaningEn":"Speech, silence, possessions, insight and life itself are not ours to control absolutely. Recognizing their source loosens pride in being inherently higher or lower than another.","meaningPa":"ਬੋਲਣਾ, ਚੁੱਪ, ਧਨ, ਸਮਝ ਅਤੇ ਜੀਵਨ ਉੱਤੇ ਸਾਡਾ ਪੂਰਾ ਆਪਣਾ ਵੱਸ ਨਹੀਂ। ਇਹਨਾਂ ਦੇ ਮੂਲ ਨੂੰ ਪਛਾਣਿਆਂ ਆਪਣੇ ਆਪ ਨੂੰ ਦੂਜਿਆਂ ਨਾਲੋਂ ਉੱਚਾ ਜਾਂ ਨੀਵਾਂ ਮੰਨਣ ਦਾ ਮਾਣ ਢਿੱਲਾ ਪੈਂਦਾ ਹੈ।","directSense":"The repeated ਜੋਰੁ ਨ moves through speech and silence, asking and giving, life and death, wealth and rule, knowledge and liberation. The range leaves no protected area in which the isolated self can claim total power. The closing locates power with the One and challenges inherent human ranking. This draft reads the Pauri as undermining self-sufficiency, while its place beside Pauri 34 keeps responsible action within the lesson.","context":"Pauri 32 ended with grace rather than boast. Pauri 33 expands the critique of boastfulness into a whole account of dependence. Pauri 34 immediately speaks of deeds being considered, so humility need not become moral indifference.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋਰੁ","note":"Power or capacity; repeated to question absolute self-command."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੋਰੁ","note":"Noise or commotion, here associated with the mind and worldly possession."},{"gurmukhi":"ਉਤਮੁ / ਨੀਚੁ","note":"High and low; the final pair unsettles human claims to inherent rank."}],"pronunciation":"The recurrent ਜੋਰੁ is a reading anchor, but each following phrase deserves its own attention. Retain the source’s alternation of ਨ and ਨਹ. No words are to be regularized for modern spelling.","interpretations":"The relation between divine agency and human responsibility remains a major interpretive question. This draft does not settle it by announcing that choices never matter. Its contextual reading places dependence beside the next Pauri’s attention to deeds.","reflection":"Name one effort that is yours to make and one outcome you cannot guarantee. Act on the first without pretending to own the second.","teachBack":"Why is it important to read Pauri 34’s account of deeds after Pauri 33’s repeated denial of personal power?","commentaryNotes":[],"status":"draft","reviewStatus":"Research-started original draft; qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review pending","scholarReview":false,"pronunciationReview":false,"unitId":"pauri33","passageIds":["pauri33.line01","pauri33.line02","pauri33.line03","pauri33.line04","pauri33.line05","pauri33.line06","pauri33.line07","pauri33.line08"],"angs":[7],"sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Primary text: frozen Open Granth/Shabad OS import, pauri33; Ang 7","role":"public-domain original Gurbani; source occurrence IDs bound separately","anchor":"pauri33"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0007.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Sri Guru Granth Darpan, Ang 7; Pauri 33","role":"consulted commentary; short attributed notes only","anchor":"Pauri 33"}],"researchScope":"Original close-reading draft with selected commentary checkpoints. Not a complete survey of traditions, line-by-line translation, approved pronunciation course, or human scholarly review.","directSensePa":"ਜੋਰੁ ਨ ਦੀ ਦੁਹਰਾਈ ਬੋਲਣ ਤੇ ਚੁੱਪ ਤੋਂ ਲੈ ਕੇ ਮੰਗਣ, ਦੇਣ, ਜੀਵਨ, ਮੌਤ, ਰਾਜ, ਧਨ, ਗਿਆਨ ਅਤੇ ਛੁਟਕਾਰੇ ਤੱਕ ਜਾਂਦੀ ਹੈ। ਕੋਈ ਖੇਤਰ ਨਹੀਂ ਛੱਡਿਆ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਜਿੱਥੇ ਇਕੱਲਾ ਆਪਾ ਪੂਰਾ ਆਪਣਾ ਵੱਸ ਮੰਨ ਲਵੇ। ਅੰਤ ਵਿੱਚ ਸਮਰੱਥਾ ਉਸ ਇੱਕ ਕੋਲ ਰੱਖੀ ਜਾਂਦੀ ਹੈ ਅਤੇ ਆਪਣੇ ਆਪ ਨੂੰ ਮੂਲੋਂ ਉੱਚਾ ਜਾਂ ਨੀਵਾਂ ਮੰਨਣ ਦੀ ਸੋਚ ਟੁੱਟਦੀ ਹੈ। ਅਗਲੀ ਪਉੜੀ ਕਰਮਾਂ ਦੀ ਪਰਖ ਕਰਦੀ ਹੈ; ਇਸ ਲਈ ਇਹ ਨਿਮਰਤਾ ਕਰਮਹੀਣਤਾ ਦਾ ਬਹਾਨਾ ਨਹੀਂ ਬਣਦੀ।","reflectionPa":"ਇੱਕ ਯਤਨ ਦੱਸੋ ਜੋ ਤੁਸੀਂ ਕਰ ਸਕਦੇ ਹੋ ਅਤੇ ਇੱਕ ਨਤੀਜਾ ਜਿਸ ਦੀ ਗਰੰਟੀ ਨਹੀਂ ਦੇ ਸਕਦੇ। ਪਹਿਲਾ ਕਰੋ, ਦੂਜੇ ਦੇ ਮਾਲਕ ਨਾ ਬਣੋ।","teachBackPa":"ਇਸ ਪਉੜੀ ਤੋਂ ਬਾਅਦ ਕਰਮਾਂ ਦੀ ਪਰਖ ਵਾਲੀ ਪਉੜੀ 34 ਪੜ੍ਹਨਾ ਕਿਉਂ ਜ਼ਰੂਰੀ ਹੈ?","researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","editorialCoverage":"unit-level bilingual meaning and structured bilingual study draft; no claim of complete line-by-line exegesis","id":"pauri33","sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri33.line01","ang":7,"sourceLine":9,"sha256":"ade3b226b624cf9937989b47b3e8f183fcb5bccd53edcfe5cf4d60cd789c68c8"},{"passageId":"pauri33.line02","ang":7,"sourceLine":9,"sha256":"1579d09d681acfe4064637684a70d3bd5242f7573f95c96be7ffd6e54ad1e4bd"},{"passageId":"pauri33.line03","ang":7,"sourceLine":9,"sha256":"ddfc030aa4fd96db568026675f9b9f16b9955c0dcec869430a177ca6e7272436"},{"passageId":"pauri33.line04","ang":7,"sourceLine":9,"sha256":"e095fde7cff2689dbd9f1860873644afd93aea1ea475bfe99edb7eff95228ac5"},{"passageId":"pauri33.line05","ang":7,"sourceLine":10,"sha256":"d0432791c0e224589505b4c29be925065abeef2872315acc863251ae2c42b5ff"},{"passageId":"pauri33.line06","ang":7,"sourceLine":10,"sha256":"f4a3740976d71b3ee09bd575757b3a93e8a9876300ce2eaa655b08669f5b0404"},{"passageId":"pauri33.line07","ang":7,"sourceLine":10,"sha256":"6f56d3555efb1176936e5449582a4d524c68fbf6680ebafd340b14fd8fb2b2e0"},{"passageId":"pauri33.line08","ang":7,"sourceLine":11,"sha256":"1fd4e0b8d6775669aa7b119bc0585d978498fd2263992868766f55704c493ebd"}],"humanReviewed":false},"pauri34":{"pauri":34,"meaningEn":"Earth is a place for living truthfully amid the variety of life. Deeds are weighed in a truthful court; genuine maturity is not decided by worldly reputation.","meaningPa":"ਜੀਵਨ ਦੇ ਅਨੇਕ ਰੰਗਾਂ ਵਿੱਚ ਧਰਤੀ ਧਰਮ ਕਮਾਉਣ ਦੀ ਥਾਂ ਹੈ। ਸੱਚੇ ਦਰਬਾਰ ਵਿੱਚ ਕਰਮਾਂ ਦੀ ਪਰਖ ਹੁੰਦੀ ਹੈ; ਅਸਲ ਪਕਿਆਈ ਦਾ ਫੈਸਲਾ ਦੁਨਿਆਵੀ ਨਾਮਣਾ ਨਹੀਂ ਕਰਦਾ।","directSense":"The Pauri situates Earth among rhythms of time and the elements, then calls it ਧਰਮ ਸਾਲ. Its many living forms have innumerable names. The next movement concerns deeds, a truthful court, acceptance and grace. The closing contrast of unripe and ripe shifts attention from appearance to tested maturity. The lesson is grounded in life here, even while the language of judgment reaches beyond ordinary human appraisal.","context":"This opens the passage conventionally discussed through the five khands. The next Pauri names ਧਰਮ ਖੰਡ and moves toward ਗਿਆਨ ਖੰਡ. The sequence begins with responsibility rather than an invitation to rank oneself by mystical status.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਧਰਮ ਸਾਲ","note":"A place of dharam: living with responsibility and truth in this draft."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਰਮੀ ਕਰਮੀ","note":"Deeds, repeatedly brought into consideration."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਚ / ਪਕਾਈ","note":"Unripeness and ripeness, used as an image of what has truly matured."}],"pronunciation":"Keep ਕਰਮੀ in the deeds phrase distinct from ਕਰਮਿ in the grace phrase later in the Pauri. Written resemblance does not justify treating all occurrences as one fixed English word. A human teacher should confirm the oral teaching.","interpretations":"Court and ripening images can guide examination of one’s own conduct. They do not make this application a tribunal that declares another person spiritually accepted or rejected. The five-khand discussion remains a learning framework, not a scoring system.","reflection":"Choose one ordinary responsibility and carry it out carefully when no one is watching. Consider the difference between looking mature and becoming dependable.","teachBack":"Why does the movement through the khands begin with Earth and deeds rather than with extraordinary experiences?","commentaryNotes":[{"source":"darpan7","note":"Sahib Singh reads Pauris 34–37 as a description of spiritual development; this draft does not make the khands measurable achievement levels."}],"status":"draft","reviewStatus":"Research-started original draft; qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review pending","scholarReview":false,"pronunciationReview":false,"unitId":"pauri34","passageIds":["pauri34.line01","pauri34.line02","pauri34.line03","pauri34.line04","pauri34.line05","pauri34.line06","pauri34.line07","pauri34.line08","pauri34.line09","pauri34.line10","pauri34.line11"],"angs":[7],"sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Primary text: frozen Open Granth/Shabad OS import, pauri34; Ang 7","role":"public-domain original Gurbani; source occurrence IDs bound separately","anchor":"pauri34"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0007.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Sri Guru Granth Darpan, Ang 7; Pauri 34","role":"consulted commentary; short attributed notes only","anchor":"Pauri 34"}],"researchScope":"Original close-reading draft with selected commentary checkpoints. Not a complete survey of traditions, line-by-line translation, approved pronunciation course, or human scholarly review.","directSensePa":"ਰਾਤਾਂ, ਰੁੱਤਾਂ ਅਤੇ ਤੱਤਾਂ ਦੇ ਵਿਚਕਾਰ ਧਰਤੀ ਨੂੰ ਧਰਮ ਸਾਲ ਕਿਹਾ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ। ਇਸ ਉੱਤੇ ਜੀਵਨ ਦੇ ਅਨੇਕ ਰੂਪ ਅਤੇ ਨਾਮ ਹਨ। ਫਿਰ ਧਿਆਨ ਕਰਮਾਂ, ਸੱਚੇ ਦਰਬਾਰ, ਪ੍ਰਵਾਨਗੀ ਅਤੇ ਮਿਹਰ ਵੱਲ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹੈ। ਕੱਚੇ-ਪੱਕੇ ਦਾ ਅੰਤਲਾ ਚਿੱਤਰ ਬਾਹਰਲੇ ਨਾਮਣੇ ਦੀ ਥਾਂ ਅਸਲ ਘਾੜਤ ਨੂੰ ਮਾਪ ਬਣਾਉਂਦਾ ਹੈ। ਸਿੱਖਿਆ ਜੀਉਂਦੇ ਜਗਤ ਵਿੱਚ ਜ਼ਿੰਮੇਵਾਰੀ ਤੋਂ ਸ਼ੁਰੂ ਹੁੰਦੀ ਹੈ; ਆਪਣੇ ਆਤਮਕ ਦਰਜੇ ਦਾ ਅੰਕ ਦੇਣ ਤੋਂ ਨਹੀਂ।","reflectionPa":"ਅਜਿਹੀ ਸਧਾਰਨ ਜ਼ਿੰਮੇਵਾਰੀ ਧਿਆਨ ਨਾਲ ਨਿਭਾਓ ਜਿਸ ਨੂੰ ਕੋਈ ਵੇਖ ਨਹੀਂ ਰਿਹਾ। ਪੱਕੇ ਦਿੱਸਣ ਅਤੇ ਭਰੋਸੇਯੋਗ ਬਣਨ ਦਾ ਫ਼ਰਕ ਵੇਖੋ।","teachBackPa":"ਖੰਡਾਂ ਦੀ ਵਿਚਾਰ ਅਸਧਾਰਨ ਅਨੁਭਵਾਂ ਦੀ ਥਾਂ ਧਰਤੀ ਅਤੇ ਕਰਮਾਂ ਤੋਂ ਕਿਉਂ ਸ਼ੁਰੂ ਹੁੰਦੀ ਹੈ?","researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","editorialCoverage":"unit-level bilingual meaning and structured bilingual study draft; no claim of complete line-by-line exegesis","id":"pauri34","sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri34.line01","ang":7,"sourceLine":11,"sha256":"8936bb5b8e4c6f5d8b4fc5de95c3ec83b3e2ac56208018b008d3dbf320c1a34f"},{"passageId":"pauri34.line02","ang":7,"sourceLine":11,"sha256":"94c3a86a9b7200740e533dae3dcfc291f7f63c2446b4fc2887e1c2332bde07bd"},{"passageId":"pauri34.line03","ang":7,"sourceLine":12,"sha256":"97b4aa3f453ed7b3b3443c4495bd9f29cf6aa9326f3cb54b292ac1634f5c20ff"},{"passageId":"pauri34.line04","ang":7,"sourceLine":12,"sha256":"5324fbc310900a7fa4849610dab2e727ee754b8d2c6d36538c76ee27f3b4ee99"},{"passageId":"pauri34.line05","ang":7,"sourceLine":12,"sha256":"991fcfcca78cf76678c06515c040fadd6aca58d9e6a6eb629309d6ac26e9a655"},{"passageId":"pauri34.line06","ang":7,"sourceLine":13,"sha256":"625e217cea4b3338197c836a4f76f1c033c7e3231c46bbcc3d256b8351d14f59"},{"passageId":"pauri34.line07","ang":7,"sourceLine":13,"sha256":"c3c0530ea8d5dcf44510e372c4f0ee1407b87849c83daff0078e289ee348c584"},{"passageId":"pauri34.line08","ang":7,"sourceLine":13,"sha256":"8c4f057cb95a1bc6b225f8170ca30be4925ff9fc6efbcbc9e174c7863086104d"},{"passageId":"pauri34.line09","ang":7,"sourceLine":13,"sha256":"01f6e760d672ac8c6ed1de0709c37b4a501bbd8b561ec0322701ee2ee067956c"},{"passageId":"pauri34.line10","ang":7,"sourceLine":14,"sha256":"113c0eed24a6ad914f65dd1980442de067b255b31dbf5c7dcfd4c70f40688424"},{"passageId":"pauri34.line11","ang":7,"sourceLine":14,"sha256":"3cc15a5cef70b868ed5ca06d284c2dd522fa7ca7ab2cb54875737c070326666d"}],"humanReviewed":false},"pauri35":{"pauri":35,"meaningEn":"From responsibility, awareness opens into the vastness of creation: worlds, forms, languages and ways of knowing exceed our inventory. Knowledge widens the field rather than closing it.","meaningPa":"ਧਰਮ ਦੀ ਪਛਾਣ ਤੋਂ ਸੁਰਤ ਰਚਨਾ ਦੀ ਵਿਸ਼ਾਲਤਾ ਵੱਲ ਖੁਲ੍ਹਦੀ ਹੈ। ਜਗਤ, ਰੂਪ, ਬੋਲੀਆਂ ਅਤੇ ਸੂਝਾਂ ਗਿਣਤੀ ਤੋਂ ਪਰੇ ਹਨ; ਗਿਆਨ ਨਜ਼ਰ ਨੂੰ ਖੋਲ੍ਹਦਾ ਹੈ, ਹੱਦ ਵਿੱਚ ਨਹੀਂ ਬੰਨ੍ਹਦਾ।","directSense":"The first two lines turn from the work of dharam toward ਗਿਆਨ ਖੰਡ. What follows is an expanding series of many: elements, revered figures, worlds, lights, seekers, languages and awarenesses. The recurring question of quantity ends without a final end. This knowledge is therefore not presented as a short list that lets the learner possess creation. The form of the Pauri itself stretches attention beyond a single familiar world.","context":"The vocabulary recalls the vast catalogues earlier in Japji, especially Pauris 17–19 and 27. Within the khand sequence, the widening field follows moral responsibility and leads into the shaping of awareness described in Pauri 36.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗਿਆਨ ਖੰਡ","note":"The domain or sphere of knowledge, named explicitly."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੇਤੇ / ਕੇਤੀਆ","note":"Recurring forms meaning many or how many; their variation belongs to the source."},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਣੀ","note":"Speech or languages in this catalogue; context matters for the word’s sense."}],"pronunciation":"Keep ਕੇਤੇ and ਕੇਤੀਆ distinct when following the catalogue. In ਸੁਰਤੀ, retain the full written ending rather than replacing it with the more familiar ਸੁਰਤਿ. These observations help accurate visual reading, not substitute for santhiya.","interpretations":"The lists employ the cosmological and religious vocabulary of the passage. This lesson does not turn them into a census of astronomical objects, nor assume that modern scientific categories map exactly onto each term.","reflection":"Learn something from a language, community or part of nature outside your usual circle. Notice how it changes the boundary of what you call familiar.","teachBack":"What kind of knowledge becomes possible when you stop expecting the catalogue of creation to end?","commentaryNotes":[],"status":"draft","reviewStatus":"Research-started original draft; qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review pending","scholarReview":false,"pronunciationReview":false,"unitId":"pauri35","passageIds":["pauri35.line01","pauri35.line02","pauri35.line03","pauri35.line04","pauri35.line05","pauri35.line06","pauri35.line07","pauri35.line08","pauri35.line09","pauri35.line10"],"angs":[7],"sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Primary text: frozen Open Granth/Shabad OS import, pauri35; Ang 7","role":"public-domain original Gurbani; source occurrence IDs bound separately","anchor":"pauri35"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0007.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Sri Guru Granth Darpan, Ang 7; Pauri 35","role":"consulted commentary; short attributed notes only","anchor":"Pauri 35"}],"researchScope":"Original close-reading draft with selected commentary checkpoints. Not a complete survey of traditions, line-by-line translation, approved pronunciation course, or human scholarly review.","directSensePa":"ਪਹਿਲੀਆਂ ਤੁਕਾਂ ਧਰਮ ਖੰਡ ਦੀ ਗੱਲ ਤੋਂ ਗਿਆਨ ਖੰਡ ਵੱਲ ਲੈ ਜਾਂਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ। ਫਿਰ ਅਨੇਕ ਤੱਤ, ਰੂਪ, ਲੋਕ, ਚਾਨਣ, ਸਾਧਕ, ਬੋਲੀਆਂ ਅਤੇ ਸੁਰਤਾਂ ਸਾਹਮਣੇ ਆਉਂਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ। ਕੇਤੇ ਅਤੇ ਕੇਤੀਆ ਦੀ ਮੁੜਦੀ ਆਵਾਜ਼ ਅੰਤਲੀ ਸੂਚੀ ਨਹੀਂ ਬਣਾਉਂਦੀ; ਨਜ਼ਰ ਹੋਰ ਖੋਲ੍ਹਦੀ ਹੈ। ਗਿਆਨ ਇੱਥੇ ਇੱਕ ਛੋਟੀ ਸੂਚੀ ਯਾਦ ਕਰਕੇ ਰਚਨਾ ਨੂੰ ਆਪਣੇ ਵੱਸ ਵਿੱਚ ਕਰਨ ਦਾ ਨਾਮ ਨਹੀਂ। ਸਿੱਖਣ ਵਾਲੇ ਦਾ ਜਾਣਿਆ ਘੇਰਾ ਵੱਡਾ ਹੁੰਦਾ ਜਾਂਦਾ ਹੈ।","reflectionPa":"ਆਪਣੇ ਰੋਜ਼ਾਨਾ ਘੇਰੇ ਤੋਂ ਬਾਹਰ ਕਿਸੇ ਬੋਲੀ, ਭਾਈਚਾਰੇ ਜਾਂ ਕੁਦਰਤੀ ਰੂਪ ਬਾਰੇ ਸਿੱਖੋ। ਵੇਖੋ ਕਿ ਜਾਣ-ਪਛਾਣ ਦਾ ਘੇਰਾ ਕਿਵੇਂ ਬਦਲਦਾ ਹੈ।","teachBackPa":"ਜੇ ਰਚਨਾ ਦੀ ਸੂਚੀ ਮੁੱਕਣ ਦੀ ਉਡੀਕ ਛੱਡ ਦਈਏ, ਤਾਂ ਕਿਹੋ ਜਿਹਾ ਗਿਆਨ ਖੁਲ੍ਹ ਸਕਦਾ ਹੈ?","researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","editorialCoverage":"unit-level bilingual meaning and structured bilingual study draft; no claim of complete line-by-line exegesis","id":"pauri35","sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri35.line01","ang":7,"sourceLine":14,"sha256":"246d417db74e6239449c205de744399d998e5ea907401aeb80346ddbedb58d9e"},{"passageId":"pauri35.line02","ang":7,"sourceLine":15,"sha256":"3e8508dc085c72297c1241a157b02d887e1547f179ff70709662f3da85a81a79"},{"passageId":"pauri35.line03","ang":7,"sourceLine":15,"sha256":"9978d05c4a1a1546fffe40b4e83b8f03d35d238842cf8bfffb8231af8ce66e0b"},{"passageId":"pauri35.line04","ang":7,"sourceLine":15,"sha256":"c7f7b90eeacea34b54d6a1d57a5a4293897c2c36202daca8ab8d55bc6b2f2f2e"},{"passageId":"pauri35.line05","ang":7,"sourceLine":16,"sha256":"af73c90f47a2d8e2bff25c4820299417b6ac16c72edf649e62e0be276b7b98b4"},{"passageId":"pauri35.line06","ang":7,"sourceLine":16,"sha256":"2c3ebbabb003bbc1689576b63c64279f6d8266eabb5e598cf3736d9b011f7634"},{"passageId":"pauri35.line07","ang":7,"sourceLine":17,"sha256":"6cd606407cc3dd72b43f3c33b5d4774d62b9aa888d9d3ad06b6677d01f07ef9b"},{"passageId":"pauri35.line08","ang":7,"sourceLine":17,"sha256":"5bff21c79c150e49cc06f0dc4164a978b9673bc84eb50fd23a5b93931323e9be"},{"passageId":"pauri35.line09","ang":7,"sourceLine":18,"sha256":"1d501efe705395b3aa0eb7e74fb1c0a252ac80aea13f065cc7972c89f8fe36f7"},{"passageId":"pauri35.line10","ang":7,"sourceLine":18,"sha256":"dd02a3ef6fb23dc3254e00c7f2d558a5f2afdc419df6f6ed6d881b4c635a3a99"}],"humanReviewed":false},"pauri36":{"pauri":36,"meaningEn":"Knowledge shines with wonder, and the field of formation reshapes awareness and understanding. Its beauty exceeds a complete verbal account; the learner is changed, not merely informed.","meaningPa":"ਗਿਆਨ ਵਿੱਚ ਅਚਰਜ ਅਤੇ ਆਨੰਦ ਜਾਗਦੇ ਹਨ; ਘਾੜਤ ਦੀ ਅਵਸਥਾ ਵਿੱਚ ਸੁਰਤ ਤੇ ਮਤ ਨਵਾਂ ਰੂਪ ਲੈਂਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ। ਇਹ ਸੁੰਦਰਤਾ ਪੂਰੀ ਤਰ੍ਹਾਂ ਬੋਲਾਂ ਵਿੱਚ ਨਹੀਂ ਆਉਂਦੀ—ਸਿੱਖਣ ਵਾਲਾ ਅੰਦਰੋਂ ਬਦਲਦਾ ਹੈ।","directSense":"The opening completes the picture of ਗਿਆਨ ਖੰਡ through intensity, sound, wonder and delight. ਸਰਮ ਖੰਡ then introduces repeated shaping: awareness, discernment and understanding are formed. The speaker also marks a limit to verbal description. The movement is from seeing more widely to becoming differently formed. This draft keeps that transformation distinct from having accumulated information about a spiritual state.","context":"Pauri 35 widened the field of knowledge. Pauri 36 asks what happens to the learner within that widening. Its shaping vocabulary will return concretely in the workshop imagery of Pauri 38.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪਰਚੰਡੁ","note":"Intense or strongly radiant; describes knowledge here."},{"gurmukhi":"ਘਾੜਤਿ / ਘੜੀਐ","note":"Formation and being formed; repeated craft language."},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਰਤਿ / ਮਤਿ","note":"Awareness and discernment, named among what is reshaped."}],"pronunciation":"ਘੜੀਐ occurs repeatedly; do not lose the vowel sequence while moving quickly. The letter ੜ in these words differs from ਡ. Precise sound and rhythm should be learned with a qualified human reader.","interpretations":"This draft follows the effort-and-formation sense of ਸਰਮ in the consulted commentary. It has not surveyed every traditional explanation. The text’s acknowledgement that the state resists description should also restrain claims that a lesson or animation reproduces that experience.","reflection":"Choose a small practice that reforms a habit rather than merely adding information: listening without interruption, doing a task carefully, or returning calmly after distraction.","teachBack":"How is being “formed” different from simply knowing more facts?","commentaryNotes":[{"source":"darpan8","note":"Sahib Singh reads ਸਰਮ as effort."}],"status":"draft","reviewStatus":"Research-started original draft; qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review pending","scholarReview":false,"pronunciationReview":false,"unitId":"pauri36","passageIds":["pauri36.line01","pauri36.line02","pauri36.line03","pauri36.line04","pauri36.line05","pauri36.line06","pauri36.line07","pauri36.line08"],"angs":[7,8],"sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Primary text: frozen Open Granth/Shabad OS import, pauri36; Ang 7, 8","role":"public-domain original Gurbani; source occurrence IDs bound separately","anchor":"pauri36"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0007.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Sri Guru Granth Darpan, Ang 7; Pauri 36","role":"consulted commentary; short attributed notes only","anchor":"Pauri 36"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0008.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Sri Guru Granth Darpan, Ang 8; Pauri 36","role":"consulted commentary; short attributed notes only","anchor":"Pauri 36"}],"researchScope":"Original close-reading draft with selected commentary checkpoints. Not a complete survey of traditions, line-by-line translation, approved pronunciation course, or human scholarly review.","directSensePa":"ਪਉੜੀ ਦਾ ਸ਼ੁਰੂ ਗਿਆਨ ਖੰਡ ਦੀ ਤੀਬਰਤਾ, ਅਚਰਜ ਅਤੇ ਆਨੰਦ ਦੀ ਗੱਲ ਪੂਰੀ ਕਰਦਾ ਹੈ। ਫਿਰ ਸਰਮ ਖੰਡ ਵਿੱਚ ਸੁਰਤ, ਮਤ ਅਤੇ ਬੁੱਧ ਦੀ ਘਾੜਤ ਆਉਂਦੀ ਹੈ। ਇਹ ਸਿਰਫ਼ ਹੋਰ ਜਾਣਕਾਰੀ ਮਿਲਣ ਦੀ ਗੱਲ ਨਹੀਂ; ਜਾਣਨ ਵਾਲਾ ਵੀ ਨਵਾਂ ਰੂਪ ਲੈਂਦਾ ਹੈ। ਨਾਲ ਹੀ ਇਸ ਹਾਲਤ ਨੂੰ ਪੂਰੀ ਤਰ੍ਹਾਂ ਕਹਿ ਨਾ ਸਕਣ ਦੀ ਹੱਦ ਦੱਸੀ ਜਾਂਦੀ ਹੈ। ਪਾਠ ਦੀ ਵਿਆਖਿਆ ਜਾਂ ਚੱਲਦੇ ਅੱਖਰ ਉਸ ਅਨੁਭਵ ਦੀ ਥਾਂ ਨਹੀਂ ਲੈ ਸਕਦੇ।","reflectionPa":"ਇੱਕ ਅਜਿਹਾ ਅਭਿਆਸ ਚੁਣੋ ਜੋ ਆਦਤ ਬਦਲੇ—ਬਿਨਾ ਟੋਕੇ ਸੁਣਨਾ, ਧਿਆਨ ਨਾਲ ਕੰਮ ਕਰਨਾ ਜਾਂ ਭਟਕਣ ਤੋਂ ਸ਼ਾਂਤੀ ਨਾਲ ਮੁੜਨਾ।","teachBackPa":"ਨਵੀਂ ਘਾੜਤ ਹੋਣਾ ਅਤੇ ਸਿਰਫ਼ ਹੋਰ ਗੱਲਾਂ ਜਾਣ ਲੈਣਾ ਵੱਖਰੇ ਕਿਵੇਂ ਹਨ?","researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","editorialCoverage":"unit-level bilingual meaning and structured bilingual study draft; no claim of complete line-by-line exegesis","id":"pauri36","sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri36.line01","ang":7,"sourceLine":19,"sha256":"b84d2923e600b34e5c725ba0e40bb06af50a3981e75b82878a5ea66815f2b71d"},{"passageId":"pauri36.line02","ang":7,"sourceLine":19,"sha256":"6d43b35fa9e7f106b0f786a5d0adbf695a3c8d129af3f55c110af8b9c63dc23e"},{"passageId":"pauri36.line03","ang":8,"sourceLine":1,"sha256":"ce2db16e7fcecbc5374233f67c2ef980fcbee094f4b7c1f1345b71b59b82d3e8"},{"passageId":"pauri36.line04","ang":8,"sourceLine":1,"sha256":"203bbbb1af3a12730df87879d51e1548c5e9b57055c37af9f19fc87218568da1"},{"passageId":"pauri36.line05","ang":8,"sourceLine":1,"sha256":"2aacb19ad03a53ab9606650e8f09b7d91cafdc9d67d61ce5bd6fbd9fec55223a"},{"passageId":"pauri36.line06","ang":8,"sourceLine":1,"sha256":"550927bb142636c42d326a14e5ca02b50034359f4bcffc269c7017879b45aba7"},{"passageId":"pauri36.line07","ang":8,"sourceLine":2,"sha256":"68d24383965bf575f06bbb82df3e20bc77be4095e7e753640ff11de03c14909c"},{"passageId":"pauri36.line08","ang":8,"sourceLine":2,"sha256":"bcda2cb31b4a00194e14ccd518a7cee18f69c752bb8d494ce9e2645db20e8115"}],"humanReviewed":false},"pauri37":{"pauri":37,"meaningEn":"Grace brings strength and a heart absorbed in the Divine. The realm of Truth opens onto the Formless One’s limitless creation and care, where all activity follows hukam.","meaningPa":"ਮਿਹਰ ਨਾਲ ਅੰਦਰ ਬਲ ਪੈਦਾ ਹੁੰਦਾ ਹੈ ਅਤੇ ਮਨ ਰੱਬ ਦੀ ਮਹਿਮਾ ਨਾਲ ਜੁੜਦਾ ਹੈ। ਸਚ ਖੰਡ ਵਿੱਚ ਨਿਰੰਕਾਰ ਦੀ ਬੇਅੰਤ ਰਚਨਾ ਤੇ ਸੰਭਾਲ ਸਾਹਮਣੇ ਆਉਂਦੀ ਹੈ, ਜਿੱਥੇ ਸਾਰੀ ਕਾਰ ਹੁਕਮ ਅਨੁਸਾਰ ਹੈ।","directSense":"The Pauri begins with strength in ਕਰਮ ਖੰਡ, describing brave figures filled with the Divine and devotion woven into praise. It then names ਸਚ ਖੰਡ and ਨਿਰੰਕਾਰ. The view opens onto worlds without an end to their account, and the relation between hukam and action becomes explicit. The close admits that telling this is hard. This lesson is an account of the passage’s movement, not a certificate that a reader has attained the states described.","context":"Following responsibility, knowledge and formation, this Pauri brings grace and truth into view. The recurrence of hukam connects the closing development to Pauri 2. It also prepares Pauri 38’s return to concrete qualities and practice.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋਰੁ","note":"Strength; compare the denial of self-sufficient ਜੋਰੁ in Pauri 33."},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਿਰੰਕਾਰੁ","note":"The Formless One, explicitly named in the realm of Truth."},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਵ ਜਿਵ / ਤਿਵੈ ਤਿਵ","note":"A paired construction connecting how the command is with how activity proceeds."}],"pronunciation":"Keep ਸੀਤੋ ਸੀਤਾ exactly as the two written forms; a reading aid must not silently turn them into a person’s name. Preserve the distinct vowels in ਨਦਰਿ and ਨਿਹਾਲ. Pronunciation review is still pending.","interpretations":"This draft follows the grace sense of ਕਰਮ ਖੰਡ and reads ਸੀਤੋ ਸੀਤਾ as being deeply woven into praise. The consulted SREC note rejects identifying the phrase with Sita as a proper name. That issue and the wider khand traditions warrant qualified review before treating one English rendering as final.","reflection":"Reflect on strength that does not need to dominate: holding to truth, remaining compassionate, or admitting error. These are reflection prompts, not proof of reaching a khand.","teachBack":"How does the strength described here differ from the self-claimed power questioned in Pauri 33?","commentaryNotes":[{"source":"darpan8","note":"Sahib Singh reads ਕਰਮ ਖੰਡ through grace."},{"source":"srec","note":"SREC disputes taking ਸੀਤੋ ਸੀਤਾ as Sita’s name."}],"status":"draft","reviewStatus":"Research-started original draft; qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review pending","scholarReview":false,"pronunciationReview":false,"unitId":"pauri37","passageIds":["pauri37.line01","pauri37.line02","pauri37.line03","pauri37.line04","pauri37.line05","pauri37.line06","pauri37.line07","pauri37.line08","pauri37.line09","pauri37.line10","pauri37.line11","pauri37.line12","pauri37.line13","pauri37.line14","pauri37.line15","pauri37.line16","pauri37.line17","pauri37.line18"],"angs":[8],"sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Primary text: frozen Open Granth/Shabad OS import, pauri37; Ang 8","role":"public-domain original Gurbani; source occurrence IDs bound separately","anchor":"pauri37"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0008.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Sri Guru Granth Darpan, Ang 8; Pauri 37","role":"consulted commentary; short attributed notes only","anchor":"Pauri 37"},{"url":"https://srec.gurmat.info/articles/sri-guru-granth-sahib/japji-sahib/","label":"SREC, Japji Sahib; Pauri 37 and associated note","role":"modern interpretive comparison; not independent human approval","anchor":"Pauri 37"}],"researchScope":"Original close-reading draft with selected commentary checkpoints. Not a complete survey of traditions, line-by-line translation, approved pronunciation course, or human scholarly review.","directSensePa":"ਕਰਮ ਖੰਡ ਦੀ ਸ਼ੁਰੂਆਤ ਬਲ ਨਾਲ ਹੁੰਦੀ ਹੈ; ਸੂਰਮੇ ਰਾਮ ਨਾਲ ਭਰੇ ਅਤੇ ਮਹਿਮਾ ਵਿੱਚ ਜੁੜੇ ਦਿਖਾਏ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ। ਫਿਰ ਸਚ ਖੰਡ ਅਤੇ ਨਿਰੰਕਾਰ ਦਾ ਨਾਮ ਆਉਂਦਾ ਹੈ। ਬੇਅੰਤ ਜਗਤਾਂ ਦੀ ਕਾਰ ਹੁਕਮ ਨਾਲ ਜੁੜਦੀ ਹੈ ਅਤੇ ਸੰਭਾਲ ਦੀ ਤਸਵੀਰ ਖੁਲ੍ਹਦੀ ਹੈ। ਅੰਤ ਵਿੱਚ ਇਸ ਨੂੰ ਕਹਿਣ ਦੀ ਔਖ ਮੰਨੀ ਜਾਂਦੀ ਹੈ। ਇਹ ਪੜ੍ਹਤ ਪਉੜੀ ਦੀ ਚਾਲ ਸਮਝਾਉਂਦੀ ਹੈ; ਕਿਸੇ ਪੜ੍ਹਨ ਵਾਲੇ ਨੂੰ ਉਹ ਅਵਸਥਾ ਮਿਲ ਜਾਣ ਦਾ ਪ੍ਰਮਾਣ ਨਹੀਂ ਦਿੰਦੀ।","reflectionPa":"ਅਜਿਹੇ ਬਲ ਬਾਰੇ ਸੋਚੋ ਜਿਸ ਨੂੰ ਹਾਵੀ ਹੋਣ ਦੀ ਲੋੜ ਨਾ ਹੋਵੇ—ਸੱਚ ਉੱਤੇ ਟਿਕਣਾ, ਦਇਆ ਰੱਖਣਾ ਜਾਂ ਗ਼ਲਤੀ ਮੰਨਣਾ।","teachBackPa":"ਇੱਥੇ ਦਾ ਬਲ ਪਉੜੀ 33 ਵਿੱਚ ਟੋਕੇ ਗਏ ਆਪਣੇ ਦਾਅਵੇ ਵਾਲੇ ਜੋਰ ਤੋਂ ਕਿਵੇਂ ਵੱਖਰਾ ਹੈ?","researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","editorialCoverage":"unit-level bilingual meaning and structured bilingual study draft; no claim of complete line-by-line exegesis","id":"pauri37","sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri37.line01","ang":8,"sourceLine":3,"sha256":"f1970a3db9612b0f934bdbc3d7a873ca2da7e600f0ad5e827962000dc6d66e84"},{"passageId":"pauri37.line02","ang":8,"sourceLine":3,"sha256":"41f67609c065f22391148e2bf86cfbd58c962bd1b0ad96359ef7b5319f7c9f22"},{"passageId":"pauri37.line03","ang":8,"sourceLine":3,"sha256":"81d9a4b9b04e7968ed5a53fd251bed00d21e6fe57c8fde518f3c405ef362b161"},{"passageId":"pauri37.line04","ang":8,"sourceLine":3,"sha256":"09a5991abe3d63f60a043549fdc6be0089e025d5b32b2a16bc3626da8c04304b"},{"passageId":"pauri37.line05","ang":8,"sourceLine":4,"sha256":"838fb498c62bf530008d78ef4ab1865f6c5e6558df8638692ccd12e948789ca5"},{"passageId":"pauri37.line06","ang":8,"sourceLine":4,"sha256":"b1e67ca617782bcba84d37b5d497b48c440854842712459702ffb3649bc6fe42"},{"passageId":"pauri37.line07","ang":8,"sourceLine":4,"sha256":"4380a37514f80243880196bdf1a74ed9026d156ece65a90fa421a7d72b4b874a"},{"passageId":"pauri37.line08","ang":8,"sourceLine":4,"sha256":"5af52b67cfe5a16fa0c086f176c43af9977dc870c39d5f17318c216d529f349c"},{"passageId":"pauri37.line09","ang":8,"sourceLine":5,"sha256":"5062feb2f557aeab229d5edf87fb46c0c9428851192166d5324d1dfc6a526697"},{"passageId":"pauri37.line10","ang":8,"sourceLine":5,"sha256":"8c2803ba1a930d5eee45c91a15f63e7adf84c150ae9d7ebcbdca5f59380bc1b6"},{"passageId":"pauri37.line11","ang":8,"sourceLine":5,"sha256":"07b312267bc39c1369f16ad41a0451c96a5e6370cb9e493d2067eac783542a7b"},{"passageId":"pauri37.line12","ang":8,"sourceLine":6,"sha256":"9fbbde34502a610ab6ae437ecf673df1272278543689919787d84016b71d1053"},{"passageId":"pauri37.line13","ang":8,"sourceLine":6,"sha256":"f739e4ddc8572d6f1a78c96dfab5e8ec44c510b820cd742fc930054a8bc72171"},{"passageId":"pauri37.line14","ang":8,"sourceLine":6,"sha256":"945515366c841ad973993ea3674bb824fa5952148ba37f8ba9128bc6589c2efb"},{"passageId":"pauri37.line15","ang":8,"sourceLine":6,"sha256":"5247fd5e252bc3c018a307f460a5d809636b9b5aae0539783317a2d80f61ab20"},{"passageId":"pauri37.line16","ang":8,"sourceLine":7,"sha256":"8a7004f063a70912b48e5012e98742cebce500eb24ed5d8b70ee5e43a012764f"},{"passageId":"pauri37.line17","ang":8,"sourceLine":7,"sha256":"0080c015cce3840c112b8d12aa6e41dd3059e120384baa5a3e9354c8b3a982e8"},{"passageId":"pauri37.line18","ang":8,"sourceLine":7,"sha256":"7dfc9c5e067e7d80cec70736024c4478dbea56e4d9a7943cbf3abdd7b3bfc561"}],"humanReviewed":false},"pauri38":{"pauri":38,"meaningEn":"Form life as a true workshop: self-restraint, patience, understanding, reverence, sustained effort and love. In this setting the Shabad is lived, with grace sustaining the work.","meaningPa":"ਜੀਵਨ ਨੂੰ ਸੱਚੀ ਟਕਸਾਲ ਬਣਾਓ—ਜਤ, ਧੀਰਜ, ਮਤ, ਗਿਆਨ, ਭਉ, ਘਾਲ ਅਤੇ ਪਿਆਰ ਨਾਲ। ਇਸ ਘਾੜਤ ਵਿੱਚ ਸਬਦ ਜੀਵਨ ਵਿੱਚ ਉਤਰਦਾ ਹੈ; ਕਾਰ ਨੂੰ ਮਿਹਰ ਦਾ ਆਸਰਾ ਮਿਲਦਾ ਹੈ।","directSense":"A goldsmith’s work provides the final Pauri’s structure. Workshop, craftsperson, anvil, tool, bellows, fire and vessel are paired with qualities of life. The image joins discipline to patience and love, rather than letting any one quality stand alone. The Shabad and the true mint come into the foreground, and the last two lines return to gracious regard. The teaching closes neither with self-sufficiency nor with an excuse to avoid practice.","context":"The formation language of Pauri 36 becomes a vivid workshop. After Pauri 37’s difficult-to-describe vision, Pauri 38 returns to how a life is shaped. The closing Salok then places remembrance and effort within the shared world.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਧੀਰਜੁ","note":"Patience or steadiness, assigned the role of the goldsmith."},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਉ / ਭਾਉ","note":"Reverence or awe, and love: distinct words with distinct roles."},{"gurmukhi":"ਟਕਸਾਲ","note":"A mint, where the image culminates in a true formation."}],"pronunciation":"The contrast between ਭਉ and ਭਾਉ is essential; do not drop the ਕੰਨਾ in ਭਾਉ or make the two words identical. Keep ਘੜੀਐ and ਸਬਦੁ as supplied. This text note is not an authoritative sound demonstration.","interpretations":"The workshop is a sustained metaphor. This draft reads it as the shaping of a life able to receive and live the Shabad, not as manufacturing new scripture. ਭਉ and ਭਾਉ should be held together: reverence does not make love dispensable.","reflection":"Choose one workshop quality that your next action needs. Practise it concretely, then notice how it depends on the others—for example, discipline without patience or knowledge without love.","teachBack":"Why does this final Pauri need both a furnace and a vessel of love?","commentaryNotes":[{"source":"darpan8","note":"Sahib Singh reads ਵੇਦੁ here as knowledge."}],"status":"draft","reviewStatus":"Research-started original draft; qualified Punjabi/Gurbani review pending","scholarReview":false,"pronunciationReview":false,"unitId":"pauri38","passageIds":["pauri38.line01","pauri38.line02","pauri38.line03","pauri38.line04","pauri38.line05","pauri38.line06","pauri38.line07"],"angs":[8],"sources":[{"url":"https://github.com/opengranth/open-granth","label":"Primary text: frozen Open Granth/Shabad OS import, pauri38; Ang 8","role":"public-domain original Gurbani; source occurrence IDs bound separately","anchor":"pauri38"},{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0008.html","label":"Professor Sahib Singh, Sri Guru Granth Darpan, Ang 8; Pauri 38","role":"consulted commentary; short attributed notes only","anchor":"Pauri 38"}],"researchScope":"Original close-reading draft with selected commentary checkpoints. Not a complete survey of traditions, line-by-line translation, approved pronunciation course, or human scholarly review.","directSensePa":"ਅੰਤਲੀ ਪਉੜੀ ਸੁਨਿਆਰੇ ਦੀ ਕਾਰ ਦੀ ਪੂਰੀ ਤਸਵੀਰ ਬਣਾਉਂਦੀ ਹੈ। ਦੁਕਾਨ, ਸੁਨਿਆਰਾ, ਅਹਰਣ, ਹਥਿਆਰ, ਧੌਂਕਣੀ, ਅੱਗ ਅਤੇ ਭਾਂਡਾ ਜੀਵਨ ਦੇ ਗੁਣਾਂ ਨਾਲ ਜੋੜੇ ਜਾਂਦੇ ਹਨ। ਜਤ ਦੇ ਨਾਲ ਧੀਰਜ ਅਤੇ ਪਿਆਰ ਹਨ; ਕੋਈ ਇਕੱਲਾ ਗੁਣ ਪੂਰੀ ਕਾਰ ਨਹੀਂ ਕਰਦਾ। ਸਬਦ ਅਤੇ ਸੱਚੀ ਟਕਸਾਲ ਦੇ ਬਾਅਦ ਅੰਤਲੀਆਂ ਤੁਕਾਂ ਫਿਰ ਮਿਹਰ ਵੱਲ ਲੈ ਜਾਂਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ। ਇਸ ਤਰ੍ਹਾਂ ਯਤਨ ਵੀ ਰਹਿੰਦਾ ਹੈ ਅਤੇ ਆਪਣੇ ਆਪ ਨੂੰ ਹੀ ਸਭ ਕੁਝ ਮੰਨਣ ਦਾ ਮਾਣ ਵੀ ਨਹੀਂ ਰਹਿੰਦਾ।","reflectionPa":"ਅਗਲੇ ਕੰਮ ਲਈ ਇੱਕ ਗੁਣ ਚੁਣੋ—ਧੀਰਜ, ਜਤ, ਸਮਝ ਜਾਂ ਪਿਆਰ। ਫਿਰ ਵੇਖੋ ਕਿ ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਬਾਕੀ ਗੁਣਾਂ ਦਾ ਸਹਾਰਾ ਕਿਵੇਂ ਚਾਹੀਦਾ ਹੈ।","teachBackPa":"ਅੰਤਲੀ ਪਉੜੀ ਵਿੱਚ ਅੱਗ ਦੇ ਨਾਲ ਪਿਆਰ ਦਾ ਭਾਂਡਾ ਵੀ ਕਿਉਂ ਚਾਹੀਦਾ ਹੈ?","researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete","editorialCoverage":"unit-level bilingual meaning and structured bilingual study draft; no claim of complete line-by-line exegesis","id":"pauri38","sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"pauri38.line01","ang":8,"sourceLine":8,"sha256":"ba47956d0a47bc0b586f85e323a7ad3dce85f1252fced7a97a6e17fc6c5b72cf"},{"passageId":"pauri38.line02","ang":8,"sourceLine":8,"sha256":"3d8baf5ad392be3e61f804c0bdea1c2f0c66cdab959414cf8f514646d06d907e"},{"passageId":"pauri38.line03","ang":8,"sourceLine":8,"sha256":"c0d2f8f11686b4b3a2ac6e5442629a59d8e67b0d26c5789e26f96d8cb04d501f"},{"passageId":"pauri38.line04","ang":8,"sourceLine":9,"sha256":"e8ba3af87ab58416f3cda5a37660847f5ed53d007fcc3f193c564371b11595e0"},{"passageId":"pauri38.line05","ang":8,"sourceLine":9,"sha256":"d06aad3e5cb5dc44bcbb11b80bff30a2170875d9da97b859c680fb26f63eaa36"},{"passageId":"pauri38.line06","ang":8,"sourceLine":9,"sha256":"c29cbacd2b12f6236f1914c3bd3dfa6d3ec489875a2566a0041ec449e077689f"},{"passageId":"pauri38.line07","ang":8,"sourceLine":10,"sha256":"3f4f6b6cf0e5b5f91ff0dc9d4389be1e05607c725b714b352f2dbe772bed4797"}],"humanReviewed":false},"closing":{"id":"closing","meaningEn":"Air, water and earth sustain our shared life, while our actions carry moral weight. Those who live in remembrance of Naam are honoured, and their company helps others too.","meaningPa":"ਪਵਣ, ਪਾਣੀ ਅਤੇ ਧਰਤੀ ਸਾਂਝੇ ਜੀਵਨ ਨੂੰ ਸੰਭਾਲਦੇ ਹਨ; ਕੀਤੇ ਕਰਮਾਂ ਦਾ ਲੇਖਾ ਵੀ ਹੈ। ਨਾਮ ਵਿਚ ਜੁੜ ਕੇ ਘਾਲਣਾ ਕਰਨ ਵਾਲੇ ਉੱਜਲ ਹੁੰਦੇ ਹਨ ਅਤੇ ਉਨ੍ਹਾਂ ਦਾ ਸੰਗ ਹੋਰਾਂ ਲਈ ਵੀ ਸਹਾਈ ਬਣਦਾ ਹੈ।","directSense":"After the Salok heading, air is named Guru, water father and earth great mother. Day and night appear as carers within whose care the world plays. The passage then turns to deeds and their reckoning, to nearness and distance according to actions, and to the honoured faces of those who have remembered Naam and laboured. Its final movement includes others with them. The ecological images and ethical reckoning belong to one closing passage; neither half should disappear when it is quoted.","directSensePa":"‘ਸਲੋਕੁ’ ਦੇ ਸਿਰਲੇਖ ਤੋਂ ਬਾਅਦ ਪਵਣ ਨੂੰ ਗੁਰੂ, ਪਾਣੀ ਨੂੰ ਪਿਤਾ ਅਤੇ ਧਰਤੀ ਨੂੰ ਵੱਡੀ ਮਾਂ ਕਿਹਾ ਹੈ। ਦਿਨ ਤੇ ਰਾਤ ਦੀ ਗੋਦ ਵਿਚ ਜਗਤ ਖੇਡਦਾ ਹੈ। ਅੱਗੇ ਕੀਤੇ ਕਰਮਾਂ, ਉਨ੍ਹਾਂ ਦੇ ਲੇਖੇ ਅਤੇ ਨੇੜੇ-ਦੂਰ ਹੋਣ ਦੀ ਗੱਲ ਆਉਂਦੀ ਹੈ। ਅੰਤ ਵਿਚ ਨਾਮ ਧਿਆਉਣ ਅਤੇ ਘਾਲਣਾ ਕਰਨ ਵਾਲਿਆਂ ਦੇ ਉੱਜਲ ਮੁਖਾਂ ਨਾਲ ਹੋਰਾਂ ਦੇ ਵੀ ਸਹਾਈ ਹੋਣ ਦਾ ਜ਼ਿਕਰ ਹੈ। ਕੁਦਰਤੀ ਸੰਬੰਧ ਅਤੇ ਕਰਮਾਂ ਦੀ ਜ਼ਿੰਮੇਵਾਰੀ ਦੋਵੇਂ ਇਸੇ ਸਲੋਕ ਵਿਚ ਹਨ।","context":"Pauri 38’s workshop image joins discipline, patience, understanding and grace. The closing Salok returns the reader to shared earthly life and accountable conduct. This is the end of Japji in this reader. The subsequent So Dar material on Ang 8 is a different composition and is not included.","vocabulary":[{"gurmukhi":"ਪਵਣੁ · ਪਾਣੀ · ਧਰਤਿ","note":"Air, water, earth. Their kinship and teaching names create a relationship, not a scientific classification."},{"gurmukhi":"ਚੰਗਿਆਈਆ ਬੁਰਿਆਈਆ","note":"Good and bad deeds/qualities in the reckoning of conduct; both are named."},{"gurmukhi":"ਘਾਲਿ","note":"Having laboured or made effort. Naam remembrance is placed beside lived exertion."},{"gurmukhi":"ਨਾਲਿ","note":"With; the final line widens the effect beyond the individual."}],"pronunciation":"The final Salok has its own heading and line sequence. Keep the signs in ਪਵਣੁ and ਧਰਤਿ and the nasal/vowel forms visible. The app’s added visual dwell at the final line is a convenience, not a prescribed end-of-recitation cadence.","interpretations":"A direct relational reading attends to the air, water and earth that support life. SREC also offers an allegorical reading in which these images carry qualities such as thought and humility. These should be presented as different interpretive approaches, not silently combined into a single literal translation. Contemporary environmental responsibility is a reasoned application; the passage does not supply a modern climate-policy programme. Its account of deeds should prompt self-examination rather than confident verdicts on another person’s spiritual standing.","reflection":"Choose one concrete way to care for the shared conditions of life today, and one action for which you should take responsibility. Keep both care and accountability in view.","reflectionPa":"ਅੱਜ ਸਾਂਝੇ ਜੀਵਨ ਦੀ ਸੰਭਾਲ ਦਾ ਇੱਕ ਕੰਮ ਚੁਣੋ ਅਤੇ ਆਪਣੇ ਕਿਸੇ ਕਰਮ ਦੀ ਜ਼ਿੰਮੇਵਾਰੀ ਲਵੋ। ਸੰਭਾਲ ਅਤੇ ਜਵਾਬਦੇਹੀ ਦੋਵੇਂ ਮਨ ਵਿਚ ਰੱਖੀਏ।","teachBack":"How does the Salok connect the natural family images, the reckoning of deeds and the effect of a Naam-centred life on others?","teachBackPa":"ਕੁਦਰਤ ਦੇ ਪਰਿਵਾਰਕ ਰੂਪਕ, ਕਰਮਾਂ ਦਾ ਲੇਖਾ ਅਤੇ ਨਾਮ ਨਾਲ ਜੁੜੇ ਜੀਵਨ ਦਾ ਹੋਰਾਂ ਉੱਤੇ ਅਸਰ—ਇਹ ਤਿੰਨੇ ਸਲੋਕ ਵਿਚ ਕਿਵੇਂ ਮਿਲਦੇ ਹਨ?","sources":[{"url":"https://www.gurugranthdarpan.net/0008.html","label":"Darpan · Ang 8 · closing Salok and boundary before So Dar"},{"url":"https://srec.gurmat.info/articles/sri-guru-granth-sahib/japji-sahib/","label":"SREC · Japji · final Salok and allegorical reading"}],"status":"draft","unitId":"closing","passageIds":["closing.line01","closing.line02","closing.line03","closing.line04","closing.line05","closing.line06","closing.line07"],"sourceAnchors":[{"passageId":"closing.line01","ang":8,"sourceLine":10,"sha256":"e895e7940ff77673e4a3ef4489bd88d396e1a88c58d5cdeda7c6c1fd928edf87"},{"passageId":"closing.line02","ang":8,"sourceLine":10,"sha256":"b4fda938f52424fc058dd966722808a6c7e85de8808e824791aef002c1b5d906"},{"passageId":"closing.line03","ang":8,"sourceLine":11,"sha256":"773729cceffc4d3a629242d3860de568b29e2f1be776ce4cb6dc2bd8a75955f3"},{"passageId":"closing.line04","ang":8,"sourceLine":11,"sha256":"e0f94e55af966567d3cb85df400bf83df6a42e1c9b4d640d2867be851f331a36"},{"passageId":"closing.line05","ang":8,"sourceLine":12,"sha256":"5146de9ec3a431049b4b6e8b383398d2817fdb9bb06dcfc1f381db0ebd932db6"},{"passageId":"closing.line06","ang":8,"sourceLine":12,"sha256":"53b8309130014e8daba807ef70a12251541821fc613ad66513d753f1ad7bd208"},{"passageId":"closing.line07","ang":8,"sourceLine":12,"sha256":"140ad5b0d658880e8603f1b713e55e68f4ea63dcf650b85fd1f429728a21edee"}],"humanReviewed":false,"researchStatus":"Research-started; comparative scholarship incomplete"}}};
